      "comment": "Resets JPEG frame info buffer pointers for a new decoding pass.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check buffer mode flag at offset 0x3C\n2. If flag set (internal buffer mode):\n   - Clear state counters and flags to zero\n   - Set read/write pointers to internal buffer at offset +0x1040\n3. If flag clear (external buffer mode):\n   - Set read pointer from external buffer address (offset 0x14)\n   - Calculate write pointer: external_ptr + buffer_size\n   - Store buffer size in available bytes field\n\nParameters:\npFrameInfo - Pointer to IJL frame info structure containing buffer management fields\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. Modifies pFrameInfo structure in-place.\n\nStructure Layout (pFrameInfo offsets, 4-byte DWORD indices):\nOffset  Field               Description\n0x00    dwProcessedBytes    Running count of bytes processed\n0x04    dwPendingBytes      Bytes pending in buffer\n0x0C    dwReadOffset        Current read position within buffer\n0x10    pReadPtr            Pointer to current read position\n0x14    pExternalBuffer     External buffer base address (external mode)\n0x18    pWritePtr           Pointer to write position / buffer end\n0x20    dwExternalBufSize   Size of external buffer\n0x24    dwAvailableBytes    Available bytes in buffer\n0x30    bResetFlag          Single-byte reset/state flag\n0x38    dwStateFlags        Additional state flags\n0x3C    dwBufferMode        0 = external buffer, non-zero = internal buffer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x1040 - Offset to internal buffer within frame info structure (4160 bytes)\n0x410  - DWORD index for internal buffer (0x1040 / 4 = 1040 decimal)",
