      "name": "FillJpegInputBuffer",
      "signature": "undefined4 FillJpegInputBuffer(DWORD param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Fills the JPEG input buffer by reading up to 4096 bytes from file.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save context pointer to preserve across ReadFile call\n2. Calculate buffer pointer at context offset 0x40\n3. Get file handle from context offset 0x3C\n4. Call ReadFileWrapper to read up to 0x1000 (4096) bytes\n5. Check if read failed (non-zero return) AND zero bytes read\n6. If error condition met, return -23 (ERROR_UNEXPECTED_EOF)\n7. Store buffer start pointer at context offset 0x10\n8. Store bytes read count at context offset 0x24\n9. Calculate and store buffer end pointer at context offset 0x18\n10. Return 0 indicating success\n\nParameters:\npContext (BitstreamContext*): Pointer to bitstream context structure\n  - Offset 0x3C: hFile - File handle for reading JPEG data\n  - Offset 0x40: abBuffer - 4096-byte input buffer\n\nReturns:\n0: Success - buffer filled with data from file\n-23 (0xFFFFFFE9): Error - ReadFile failed with zero bytes read\n\nStructure Layout (BitstreamContext relevant fields):\nOffset  Size  Field             Type      Description\n0x10    4     pBufferStart      void*     Pointer to start of filled buffer\n0x18    4     pBufferEnd        void*     Pointer to end of valid data\n0x24    4     dwBytesAvailable  uint      Number of bytes read into buffer\n0x3C    4     hFile             HANDLE    File handle for reading\n0x40    4096  abBuffer          byte[]    Input buffer for file data",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
