      "comment": "Advances the read position in a JPEG bitstream by consuming bytes from the buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output position to 0 (indicating failure state)\n2. If refill flag is set and buffer has insufficient bytes:\n   a. Call FillJpegInputBuffer to refill the buffer\n   b. Return -23 (0xFFFFFFE9) if refill fails\n   c. Return -24 (0xFFFFFFE8) if still insufficient bytes after refill\n3. Check if buffer has enough bytes to satisfy request\n4. Return -5 (0xFFFFFFFB) if insufficient bytes available\n5. Update stream context:\n   - Advance read position by dwBytesToAdvance\n   - Decrease remaining byte count\n   - Increase total consumed byte count\n6. Output previous read position and return success\n\nParameters:\n  pStreamCtx - Pointer to BitstreamContext structure containing:\n    +0x10: Current read position pointer (pReadPos)\n    +0x1c: Total bytes consumed counter (dwTotalConsumed)\n    +0x24: Bytes remaining in buffer (dwBytesRemaining)\n    +0x3c: Refill capability flag (bCanRefill)\n  dwBytesToAdvance - Number of bytes to consume/advance\n  pnPreviousPosition - Output: receives the read position before advancing\n\nReturns:\n  0 - Success, pnPreviousPosition contains valid pointer\n  -5 (0xFFFFFFFB) - Insufficient bytes in buffer (no refill available)\n  -23 (0xFFFFFFE9) - Buffer refill operation failed\n  -24 (0xFFFFFFE8) - Insufficient bytes even after refill attempt\n\nSSA Variables (decompiler temporaries):\n  pbVar1 - Pointer to updated read position (pStreamCtx->pReadPos + dwBytesToAdvance)\n  iVar2 - Cached value of current read position before update\n\nError Handling:\n  Sets *pnPreviousPosition to 0 on entry, only updates on success",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
