      "name": "SkipJpegFillBytes",
      "signature": "undefined4 SkipJpegFillBytes(DWORD param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Skips JPEG fill bytes (0xFF padding) in a bitstream to locate the next marker.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if buffer has data available (pbWritePos < pbBufferEnd)\n2. If buffer empty, attempt to refill via dwReserved38 callback\n3. Scan through buffer bytes, counting consumed bytes in dwReserved1C\n4. When 0xFF byte found, set marker-found flag\n5. After 0xFF, check next byte: if non-zero and non-0xFF, valid marker found\n6. If next byte is 0x00 or 0xFF, skip it (stuffed byte) and continue scanning\n7. Repeat until valid marker found or buffer exhausted\n\nParameters:\n    pContext - Pointer to BitstreamContext with buffer state\n\nReturns:\n    0  - Success, positioned at valid marker byte after 0xFF prefix\n    -5 - Error: No refill callback and buffer exhausted (EOF)\n   -23 - Error: Buffer refill operation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n    - 0xFF 0x00 sequence is byte-stuffed 0xFF data, not a marker\n    - 0xFF 0xFF is fill padding, skip and continue\n    - Any 0xFF followed by 0x01-0xFE (except 0xFF) is a valid marker\n\nStructure Layout (BitstreamContext relevant fields):\n    Offset  Size  Field           Description\n    0x10    4     pbWritePos      Current read position in buffer\n    0x18    4     pbBufferEnd     End of valid buffer data\n    0x1C    4     dwReserved1C    Bytes consumed counter\n    0x20    4     dwReserved20    Bytes remaining to process\n    0x38    4     dwReserved38    Refill callback (0=no refill)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
