      "name": "InitializeJpegComponentParams",
      "signature": "undefined4 InitializeJpegComponentParams(int param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes JPEG decoder component parameters and determines color space type.\n\nAnalyzes the component sampling factors and image type to configure MCU dimensions,\ncalculate block counts, and determine the appropriate color space encoding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check image type at offset 0x58 against known types (1, 4, 5, 0xFF)\n2. Set interleave flag at offset 0x68 based on image type\n3. Iterate through component info array to find max H/V sampling factors\n4. Calculate MCU dimensions (8 * max sampling factor or 8 for single component)\n5. Compute horizontal/vertical MCU counts using image dimensions\n6. Calculate total MCU count for progressive scan ordering\n7. Validate component configurations and determine color space type\n8. Store determined color space type at offset 0x18\n\nParameters:\npJpegDecoder - Pointer to JPEG_CORE_PROPERTIES structure containing:\n    +0x18: Output color space type (set by this function)\n    +0x30: Number of color components\n    +0x34: Color space identifier (1=YCbCr, 2=?, 5=YCCK)\n    +0x4c: Image width in pixels\n    +0x50: Image height in pixels\n    +0x58: JPEG image type marker\n    +0x68: Interleave flag (0=interleaved, 1=non-interleaved)\n    +0x6c: Non-uniform sampling flag\n    +0x74: Single component mode flag\n    +0x78: Horizontal MCU count\n    +0x7c: Vertical MCU count\n    +0x37b0: Max V sampling * 8\n    +0x37b4: Max H sampling * 8\n    +0x37b8: Max H sampling factor\n    +0x37bc: Max V sampling factor\n    +0x37c0: Number of components in scan\n    +0x37c4: Horizontal MCU count (duplicate)\n    +0x37c8: Total MCU count\n    +0x37cc: Pointer to component info array\n    +0x4de0: Progressive scan flag\n\nReturns:\n0 - Success, color space type determined and stored\n-14 (0xFFFFFFF2) - Error, component count out of valid range (1-255)\n\nColor Space Types:\n0 - Unknown/default\n1 - YCbCr (1x1, 1x1, 1x1) baseline\n2 - YCbCr (2x1, 1x1, 1x1)\n3 - YCbCr (2x2, 1x1, 1x1) 4:2:0\n4 - YCbCr (2x2, 1x1, 1x1) with color ID 2\n5 - YCbCr (2x1, 1x1, 1x1) 4:2:2 horizontal\n6 - YCbCr (2x1, 1x1, 1x1) with color ID 2\n8 - YCCK 4 component\n11 - CMYK 4 component\n13 - Adobe RGB 3 component\n14 - Adobe CMYK 4 component",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
