      "name": "FlushJpegEncodeBufferToFile",
      "signature": "undefined4 FlushJpegEncodeBufferToFile(DWORD param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Flushes the JPEG encode buffer to the output file.\n\nFinalizes the current encoding state via callback, then writes accumulated\nbuffer data to the file handle if present. Validates that all bytes were\nsuccessfully written.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Call encode finalization callback (g_pfnDecodeProc1) with output buffer\n  2. If callback returns non-zero, return error -23\n  3. Check if file handle exists at pOutputBuffer+0x3c\n  4. Calculate buffer size: (pOutputBuffer+0x10) - (pOutputBuffer+0x40)\n  5. Write buffer data from pOutputBuffer+0x40 to file via WriteFileWrapper\n  6. Verify bytes written equals buffer size\n  7. Return 0 on success, -23 on write failure\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputBuffer (JpegOutputBuffer*): Pointer to JPEG output buffer structure\n    +0x10: Pointer to end of buffered data (dwDataEndPtr)\n    +0x3c: File handle for output (hOutputFile)\n    +0x40: Start of buffer data region (abBufferData)\n\nReturns:\n  0: Success - buffer flushed and all bytes verified written\n  -23 (0xFFFFFFE9): Error - callback failed or incomplete write\n\nCalled By:\n  WriteJpegHeadersAndInitEncode - Flushes after header initialization\n  ProcessJpegEncodeScan - Flushes after scan data encoding",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
