      "name": "WriteBufferedOutputBytes",
      "signature": "undefined4 WriteBufferedOutputBytes(int param_1, uint param_2, uint * param_3)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Writes bytes to a buffered output stream with 0xFF escape sequence handling.\n\nThis function is used as a decode output handler in JPEG decoding tables\n(scalar, SSE, SSE2 variants). It writes decoded data to a 4KB internal buffer\nand flushes to file when full.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. If no file handle (offset 0x3C is NULL), use direct buffer mode\n  2. Check if output buffer has space for dwByteCount + 2 bytes\n  3. If buffer full, flush 4KB to file via WriteFile\n  4. If bit position < 8, write pending byte from context\n  5. Handle 0xFF escape: when byte is 0xFF, write 0xFF followed by 0x00 marker\n  6. Reset bit state after writing pending byte\n  7. Loop through source bytes, copying each to output buffer\n  8. If buffer fills during loop, flush and continue\n  9. Update buffer pointers and byte counters\n\nParameters:\n  pBitstream   - Pointer to BitstreamContext structure containing:\n                 +0x00: Current byte value being processed\n                 +0x04: Reserved\n                 +0x0C: Bit position counter (0-7)\n                 +0x10: Current output buffer pointer\n                 +0x18: End of buffer pointer\n                 +0x1C: Total bytes written counter\n                 +0x3C: File handle (HANDLE) or NULL for memory-only\n                 +0x40: 4096-byte (0x1000) output buffer\n  dwByteCount  - Number of bytes to write from source\n  pbSourceData - Pointer to source byte array\n\nReturns:\n  0          - Success\n  0xFFFFFFE9 - Write error (WriteFile failed or incomplete write)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - When byte value is 0xFF, an escape sequence 0xFF 0x00 is written\n  - NULL file handle uses direct memory buffer without file I/O\n  - Buffer size is 4096 bytes (0x1000)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1000 (4096) - Output buffer size\n  0xFF          - Marker byte requiring escape sequence\n  0x00          - Escape marker following 0xFF\n  0xFFFFFFE9    - Error return code (-23 signed)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
