      "name": "FlushBitstreamAndWriteBytes",
      "signature": "undefined4 FlushBitstreamAndWriteBytes(int param_1, int param_2, longlong * param_3)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Flushes pending bits from the bit accumulator and writes raw bytes to the output bitstream.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if output buffer needs flushing to file (within 2 bytes of buffer end)\n2. If buffer full, call WriteFile wrapper (FUN_60018110) to flush buffer to disk\n3. On write failure, return error code -23 (0xFFFFFFE9)\n4. Reset buffer pointers to start of internal buffer (offset 0x40)\n5. Extract accumulated bits byte-by-byte from the 64-bit accumulator (MSB first)\n6. Apply JPEG-style byte stuffing: insert 0x00 after any 0xFF byte\n7. Increment bytes written counter for each byte output including escape bytes\n8. Copy source data bytes to output buffer if pbSrcData is not NULL\n9. Update write position pointer and total bytes written counter\n10. Return 0 on success\n\nParameters:\n  pbSrcData - Pointer to source data bytes to write, NULL to perform flush only\n  nByteCount - Number of bytes to copy from source buffer\n  pBitstream - Pointer to BitstreamContext structure containing buffer state\n\nReturns:\n  0 - Success, all bytes written and bits flushed\n  -23 (0xFFFFFFE9) - WriteFile failed or bytes written count mismatch\n\nBitstreamContext Structure Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field              Type        Description\n  0x00    8     llBitAccumulator   longlong    64-bit bit buffer, MSB-first\n  0x0C    4     nBitsPending       int         Bits pending in accumulator (multiple of 8)\n  0x10    4     pbWritePos         byte*       Current write position in buffer\n  0x18    4     pbBufferEnd        byte*       Pointer to end of buffer\n  0x1C    4     dwBytesWritten     dword       Running total of bytes written\n  0x3C    4     hFile              HANDLE      File handle for output (0 if none)\n  0x40    4096  abBuffer           byte[4096]  Internal output buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - 0xFF byte stuffing prevents JPEG marker collision in output stream\n  - NULL pbSrcData performs flush-only operation without copying data\n  - Uses MMX registers (MM0-MM2) for efficient 64-bit bit manipulation\n  - EMMS instruction clears MMX state before returning for FPU compatibility",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
