      "name": "WriteBitsToJpegStream",
      "signature": "undefined4 WriteBitsToJpegStream(uint param_1, int param_2, int param_3)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Writes bits to a JPEG output bitstream with byte stuffing for 0xFF markers.\n\nThis function is part of the JPEG entropy encoder. It accumulates bits in a\n64-bit MMX register (MM7) and flushes complete 32-bit words to the output\nbuffer. When a 0xFF byte is encountered, it inserts a 0x00 byte after it\nto prevent the marker from being interpreted as a JPEG marker code.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Add nBitCount to current bit position in pBitstream\n2. Shift dwBitData into the accumulator at the appropriate position\n3. If accumulated bits >= 32:\n   a. Extract top 32 bits (4 bytes)\n   b. Check each byte for 0xFF using MMX PCMPEQB\n   c. If no 0xFF bytes found, write packed bytes directly\n   d. If 0xFF found, insert 0x00 stuffing byte and adjust bit count\n   e. Continue loop while bits >= 32\n4. Update output pointer and bit count in pBitstream\n\nParameters:\n  dwBitData   - Bit data to write (right-aligned, up to 32 bits)\n  nBitCount   - Number of valid bits in dwBitData (1-32)\n  pBitstream  - Pointer to JpegOutputBuffer with current state:\n                +0x0C: nPendingBits - bits accumulated but not written\n                +0x10: pdwOutput    - current output pointer\n                +0x1C: dwBytesWritten - total bytes written\n\nReturns:\n  Always returns 0 (success)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x40 - 64 bits total in accumulator (MMX register MM7)\n  0x20 - 32 bits threshold for flushing to output\n  0x18 - 24 bits consumed when stuffing 1 byte\n  0x10 - 16 bits consumed when stuffing 2 bytes\n  0xFF - JPEG marker prefix requiring byte stuffing\n\nStructure Layout (JpegOutputBuffer offsets used):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Description\n  0x0C    4     nPendingBits    Number of bits in accumulator\n  0x10    4     pdwOutput       Current output write pointer\n  0x1C    4     dwBytesWritten  Total bytes written to output\n\nNote: Decompiler SSA variables (cVar1, bVar2, local_MM0_106) are transient\nMMX byte extractions that cannot be persisted - they represent byte slices\nof the qwPackedBytes MMX register at different bit offsets.",
