      "name": "FlushJpegOutputBuffer",
      "signature": "undefined4 FlushJpegOutputBuffer(int param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Flushes the JPEG output buffer to the file handle.\n\nWrites all pending data from the internal data buffer to the associated\nfile handle. Called when the bit accumulator approaches capacity during\nJPEG encoding to prevent buffer overflow.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Calculate bytes to write: pWritePos - abDataBuffer start\n  2. Call WriteFile via FUN_60018110 wrapper\n  3. If write fails or partial write: return error -23 (0xFFFFFFE9)\n  4. On success: reset pWritePos to buffer start (offset 0x40)\n  5. Update pBufferEnd to buffer end (offset 0x1040)\n  6. Return 0 for success\n\nParameters:\n  pOutBuffer - Pointer to JpegOutputBuffer structure containing:\n               +0x10: pWritePos - current write position\n               +0x18: pBufferEnd - buffer end boundary\n               +0x3C: hFile - file HANDLE for output\n               +0x40: abDataBuffer[0x1000] - 4KB data buffer\n\nReturns:\n  0 on success\n  -23 (0xFFFFFFE9) on write failure or partial write\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x40 - Offset to data buffer start within structure\n  0x1040 - Offset to data buffer end (0x40 + 0x1000)\n  0xFFFFFFE9 (-23) - Write error code\n\nError Handling:\n  Returns error if WriteFile returns 0 (failure) or if bytes written\n  does not match bytes requested (partial write).",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:b6a61047de48651ab8c40be7327bcce5ee64894a9bfc9eddc12d991c6f8bdf1f",
