      "name": "ComputeClippedTileRegion",
      "signature": "undefined4 ComputeClippedTileRegion(int * param_1, uint param_2, uint param_3, int param_4, int param_5, int param_6, int param_7, int param_8, int param_9, uint param_10, int * param_11, uint * param_12)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Computes the visible portion of a tile within a clipping rectangle.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If clip rectangle is empty (all zeros), compute full tile coverage:\n   a. Calculate output offset from tile position and strides\n   b. Clamp tile width/height to remaining image bounds\n2. If clip rectangle is active:\n   a. Check if tile intersects the clip rectangle\n   b. If no intersection, return -8 (TILE_OUTSIDE_CLIP)\n   c. Calculate adjusted offset relative to clip origin\n   d. Compute visible X/Y start positions (clamped to 0)\n   e. Compute visible width/height (clamped to bounds)\n3. Write results to output offset and output rectangle\n\nParameters:\n  pnClipRect   - Pointer to clip rectangle [x, y, right, bottom] (4 ints)\n  dwTileX      - Tile X coordinate (in tile units)\n  dwTileY      - Tile Y coordinate (in tile units)\n  nTileWidth   - Width of each tile in pixels\n  nTileHeight  - Height of each tile in pixels\n  nRowStride   - Bytes per row for X offset calculation\n  nColStride   - Bytes per column for Y offset calculation\n  nBaseOffset  - Base offset to add to calculated position\n  nMaxWidth    - Maximum allowed width (image width limit)\n  dwMaxHeight  - Maximum allowed height (signed, image height limit)\n  pnOutOffset  - Receives calculated pixel offset\n  pdwOutRect   - Receives visible rect [startX, startY, width, height]\n\nReturns:\n  0  - Success, tile is visible and results written\n  -8 - Tile is completely outside the clip rectangle\n\nStructure Layout (pdwOutRect):\n  Offset  Size  Field    Description\n  0x00    4     startX   Starting X pixel within tile\n  0x04    4     startY   Starting Y pixel within tile\n  0x08    4     width    Visible width in pixels\n  0x0C    4     height   Visible height in pixels\n\nStructure Layout (pnClipRect):\n  Offset  Size  Field    Description\n  0x00    4     x        Left edge of clip region\n  0x04    4     y        Top edge of clip region\n  0x08    4     right    Right edge of clip region\n  0x0C    4     bottom   Bottom edge of clip region",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
