      "name": "ProcessAndConvertImagePlanes",
      "signature": "undefined ProcessAndConvertImagePlanes(int param_1, int param_2, int * param_3, int param_4, int param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Dispatches image plane processing based on subsampling mode and converts YCbCr to RGB.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check subsampling flag at pImageContext+0x4DE0\n2. If not subsampled (flag == 0):\n   - Call ProcessImagePlanes with standard plane layout\n3. If subsampled (flag != 0):\n   - Call ProcessSubsampledImagePlanes for chroma subsampling\n4. Convert processed planes from YCbCr to RGB color space\n\nParameters:\n- pImageContext: Pointer to image context structure containing subsampling flag at offset 0x4DE0\n- pSourcePlanes: Pointer to source image plane data\n- pDestPlanes: Pointer to destination plane buffer\n- nHeight: Number of rows to process\n- nWidth: Number of columns to process\n\nReturns:\n- void (output written to pDestPlanes via callee functions)\n\nControl Flow:\n- Two paths based on subsampling flag, both converge on YCbCr to RGB conversion\n- Subsampling typically indicates 4:2:0 or 4:2:2 chroma format",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:49be1287444b234d3a315ba921eeefb467fad2c843be3053f7b95969afd13d19",
