      "name": "ProcessImagePlaneAndConvertColor",
      "signature": "undefined ProcessImagePlaneAndConvertColor(int param_1, int param_2, int param_3, uint param_4)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Processes image plane blocks and converts YCbCr color space to RGB.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call ProcessImagePlaneBlocks with plane data, zero offset mode, and dimensions\n2. Call ConvertYCbCrToRgb to transform color space from YCbCr to RGB\n\nParameters:\n    pnPlaneY    - int*: Pointer to Y (luminance) plane data\n    pnPlaneCbCr - int*: Pointer to CbCr (chrominance) plane data\n    nWidth      - int: Width of the image in pixels\n    dwHeight    - uint: Height of the image in pixels\n\nReturns:\n    void\n\nNotes:\n    - Passes hardcoded 0 as third param to ProcessImagePlaneBlocks (likely offset or mode)\n    - This function is called by DispatchImagePlaneProcessor as part of image decoding pipeline\n    - Typical use case: JPEG/image decoding where YCbCr must be converted to displayable RGB",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
