      "name": "ProcessImagePlanes",
      "signature": "undefined ProcessImagePlanes(int param_1, int param_2, int * param_3, undefined4 param_4, int param_5, int param_6)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Processes image color planes for non-subsampled image data rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load image context dimensions and calculate scale factors\n2. If special case (context[0] == 1 and context[0x4de0] == 0), apply scale division\n3. Call FUN_60002700 to calculate clipping region with output offset\n4. If clipping result is non-zero (out of bounds), exit early\n5. Calculate initial output row position based on image format type\n6. For each color plane index up to plane count:\n   a. Skip processing if format is 4 and plane index >= 24\n   b. Calculate width and height scaling factors from plane data\n   c. For each height block:\n      - For each width block:\n        - Read pixel values from source data pointer\n        - Fill pixel buffer with scaled pixel values using REP STOSD/STOSB\n   d. Call FUN_60003620 to transfer pixel buffer to output\n   e. Adjust output row position based on format flags\n7. If remaining planes exist after main loop, fill them via FUN_60003620\n\nParameters:\n  pImageContext - Pointer to image context structure containing format, dimensions, offsets\n  pOutputInfo   - Pointer to output information structure with buffer pointers\n  pPlaneData    - Pointer to plane sampling configuration data\n  nParam4       - Processing mode flag (0 or 1)\n  nSrcX         - Source X coordinate offset\n  nSrcY         - Source Y coordinate offset\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Format type 2 with subformat 1: Decrements output row after each plane\n  - Format type 4: Limits processing to first 24 planes (0x18)\n  - Format 255 with subformat 255: Skips final plane fill loop\n\nStructure Layout (pImageContext):\n  Offset  Size  Field               Description\n  0x0004  16    dwClipRect[4]       Clipping rectangle bounds\n  0x0030  4     dwPlaneCount        Number of color planes\n  0x0034  4     dwFormatType        Image format type (1,2,5,255)\n  0x003C  4     dwRowStride         Row stride in bytes\n  0x0058  4     dwSubFormat         Sub-format flags\n  0x0074  4     dwFlags             Processing flags\n  0x37B8  4     dwScaledWidth       Scaled image width\n  0x37BC  4     dwScaledHeight      Scaled image height\n  0x4834  4     pPixelData          Pointer to source pixel data\n  0x4DE0  4     dwSubsampleFlag     Subsampling flag (0 = none)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
