      "name": "ProcessSubsampledImagePlanes",
      "signature": "undefined ProcessSubsampledImagePlanes(int param_1, int param_2, undefined4 param_3, undefined4 param_4, int param_5, int param_6)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Processes subsampled image planes for image decoding/encoding operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output parameters via FUN_60002700 with scaled coordinates\n2. Calculate initial output row based on sampling mode and offset\n3. Iterate through each image plane up to the maximum plane count\n4. For each plane, calculate width/height scaling factors from sampling info\n5. Process pixel blocks using nested loops for subsampling factors\n6. Read source pixels with 2-byte stride, replicate to fill output blocks\n7. Call FUN_60003620 to write each processed row to output\n8. Handle special cases for interlaced/progressive output direction\n\nParameters:\n  pImageContext - Pointer to image context structure containing dimensions, \n                  sampling info at offsets 0x37b8, 0x37bc, 0x37c0, 0x37cc\n  pOutputInfo   - Output descriptor with row offset at +0x2c and mode at +0x38\n  nParam3       - Unused parameter (reserved)\n  nParam4       - Unused parameter (reserved)  \n  nSrcX         - Source X coordinate for processing region\n  nSrcY         - Source Y coordinate for processing region\n\nReturns:\n  void - Writes processed data through FUN_60003620 calls\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Mode 2/1 at +0x34/+0x58: Uses reverse row direction (decrement)\n  - Mode 4 at +0x58: Limits processing to first 16 bytes of plane info\n  - Mode 0xff/0xff: Skips remaining plane fill loop\n  - Flag at +0x74: Skips trailing fill loop when set\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x4834 - Source pixel buffer pointer offset in context\n  0x37b8 - Horizontal sampling factor offset (multiplied by 8)\n  0x37bc - Vertical sampling factor offset (multiplied by 8)\n  0x37c0 - Maximum plane count offset\n  0x37cc - Plane descriptor array pointer offset\n  0x500  - Scratch buffer size (1280 bytes)\n  0x100  - Row stride multiplier (256)\n  0x20   - Block stride (32 bytes)\n\nStructure Layout (pImageContext):\n  Offset  Size  Field                    Description\n  0x04    4     pCoordinates             Coordinate data array\n  0x20    4     nWidth                   Image width\n  0x24    4     nHeight                  Image height\n  0x28    4     dwStride                 Row stride value\n  0x30    4     nMaxPlanes               Maximum plane count\n  0x34    4     nModeH                   Horizontal output mode\n  0x3c    4     nColorDepth              Color depth value\n  0x58    4     nModeV                   Vertical output mode\n  0x74    4     fSkipFill                Skip fill flag\n  0x37b8  4     nSampleH                 Horizontal sampling factor\n  0x37bc  4     nSampleV                 Vertical sampling factor\n  0x37c0  4     nPlanesToProcess         Active plane count\n  0x37cc  4     pPlaneDescriptors        Plane info array pointer\n  0x4834  4     pPixelBuffer             Source pixel data pointer",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
