      "name": "ProcessImagePlaneBlocks",
      "signature": "undefined ProcessImagePlaneBlocks(int param_1, int param_2, undefined4 param_3, int param_4, uint param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Processes image plane blocks by computing clipped tile regions and copying pixel data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call ComputeClippedTileRegion to determine valid region boundaries for block\n2. If clipping fails (non-zero return), exit early without processing\n3. Calculate destination buffer offset based on subsampling mode (mode 2 with type 1 adds 2)\n4. For each plane in the image (0 to planeCount-1):\n   a. If plane >= 1 and subsampling type is 4: fill alpha channel with 0xFF\n   b. Otherwise if plane < maxPlaneBlocks: copy from source using 8x8 block stride\n   c. If plane == 3 and mode == 5: fill opacity plane with 0xFF\n5. Adjust destination offset: decrement if mode 2/type 1, else increment\n6. Loop until all planes are processed\n\nParameters:\n  nDecoder      - Decoder context handle containing image configuration\n  nOutputContext - Output buffer context with destination pointers\n  nSubsamplingMode - Subsampling mode (2=special handling, 4=alpha fill, 5=opacity)\n  nBlockX       - Horizontal block coordinate in tile grid\n  dwBlockY      - Vertical block coordinate in tile grid\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value. Modifies destination buffer in place through nOutputContext.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Early exit if ComputeClippedTileRegion returns non-zero (outside valid region)\n  - Mode 2 with type 1: Destination offset adjusted for interlaced data\n  - Plane 0: Normal pixel copy from source buffer\n  - Plane >= 1 with type 4: Alpha channel filled with 0xFF (opaque)\n  - Plane 3 with mode 5: Opacity plane filled with 0xFF\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x8 (8)     - Block dimension (8x8 pixel blocks)\n  0x80 (128)  - Bytes per block row (8x8 blocks x 2 bytes/pixel)\n  0x37c0      - Offset to plane block count in decoder structure\n  0x37cc      - Offset to plane info array pointer in decoder\n  0x4834      - Offset to source buffer pointer in decoder structure\n  0xFF        - Opaque alpha/opacity value",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
