      "name": "WriteScaledPixelsToSurface",
      "signature": "undefined WriteScaledPixelsToSurface(int param_1, int * param_2, int param_3, int param_4, int param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Writes scaled pixel data from source buffer to destination surface based on format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate mip level against max levels at [nTextureInfo+0x30]\n2. Check format type at [nTextureInfo+0x58] and pixel format at [nTextureInfo+0x34]\n3. For RGBA format (type 4, format 5): Copy 4 bytes per pixel with alpha=0xFF\n4. For RGB format (type 3/1, format 5): Copy single byte per pixel to RGBA position\n5. For special format (type 4, format 1/2): Copy 3 bytes per pixel (RGB only)\n6. For default format: Copy single byte per pixel using row stride calculation\n7. Inner loops iterate over clip rect bounds from pnClipRect structure\n8. Calculate destination offset using row stride at [nTextureInfo+0x3c]\n\nParameters:\n  nTextureInfo   - Pointer to texture/surface info structure (cast to int)\n                   +0x30: Max mipmap level count\n                   +0x34: Pixel format type (5=standard, others=special)\n                   +0x3c: Row stride in bytes\n                   +0x58: Format subtype (1/3/4 for different pixel layouts)\n  pnClipRect     - Pointer to clipping rectangle with iteration bounds\n                   [+0x00]: Start X, [+0x04]: Start Y\n                   [+0x08]: End X, [+0x0C]: End Y\n  nMipLevel      - Current mipmap level being processed (0-based)\n  nDestLine      - Destination line/Y-coordinate for output\n  nSourceBuffer  - Pointer to source pixel data buffer (32-byte row blocks)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; writes directly to destination surface\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x20 (32)  - Row block size in source buffer\n  0xFF       - Full alpha value written for RGBA format\n\nFormat Paths:\n  Path 1 (0x60003651): RGBA with alpha fill - type 4, format 5\n  Path 2 (0x60003705): Single channel copy - type 3/1, format 5, level < 3\n  Path 3 (0x60003755): Alpha fill only - type 3/1, format 5, level >= 3\n  Path 4 (0x600037bc): RGB 3-byte copy - type 4, format 1/2\n  Path 5 (0x60003848): Default single byte copy",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
