      "name": "DispatchMipmapProcessing",
      "signature": "undefined DispatchMipmapProcessing(int param_1, int param_2, int * param_3, int param_4, int param_5, uint param_6)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Dispatches mipmap processing to specialized handlers based on texture format flags.\nRoutes to different processing paths based on flags at IJL_TextureInfo offsets 0x74, 0x68, 0x6c, and 0x4de0.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if processing complete flag (0x74) set and alternate path (0x4de0) not set\n   - If true: Call ProcessMipmapTextureSamples with mode=0\n2. Read vertical direction flag from offset 0x6c\n3. Check horizontal direction flag at offset 0x68\n4. If both vertical (0x6c) and horizontal (0x68) flags set:\n   - Call FUN_600039d0 for full bidirectional processing\n5. If only horizontal (0x68) flag set:\n   - Call FUN_60003a50 for horizontal-only processing\n6. If only vertical (0x6c) flag set and horizontal (0x68) unset:\n   - Check mipmap info level at pnMipmapInfo[2]\n   - If level==0 and alternate path (0x4de0) unset: Call ProcessMipmapTextureSamples mode=1\n   - Otherwise: Call ProcessMipmapLevelData\n7. Fallback path (neither flag set):\n   - Call ProcessMipmapPixelTransfer for basic pixel copy\n\nParameters:\n  pTextureInfo  - IJL_TextureInfo* with format flags and dimensions\n  pSurfaceData  - IJL_SurfaceData* target surface information\n  pnMipmapInfo  - Mipmap level descriptors (level count at [0], level data at [2])\n  nDestX        - Destination X coordinate\n  nDestY        - Destination Y coordinate\n  dwScaleFactor - Scale factor for block dimensions\n\nReturns:\n  void - Processing results written to destination surface\n\nStructure Offsets (IJL_TextureInfo):\n  +0x68  - Horizontal direction flag\n  +0x6c  - Vertical direction flag\n  +0x74  - Processing complete flag\n  +0x4de0 - Alternate processing path flag\n\nCalled By:\n  DecodeJpegScanData, ProcessBaselineDctScanBlocks, ProcessProgressiveDctScanBlocks, ProcessMcuBlocksDecode\n\nCalls:\n  ProcessMipmapTextureSamples, ProcessMipmapPixelTransfer, ProcessMipmapLevelData, FUN_600039d0, FUN_60003a50",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:44b04893e8808b9e56cd291f8047f3308b529d05ad58358b7118df113da210f5",
