      "name": "ProcessBidirectionalMipmapWithColorConvert",
      "signature": "undefined ProcessBidirectionalMipmapWithColorConvert(int param_1, int param_2, int * param_3, int param_4, int param_5, int param_6)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Processes bidirectional mipmap data with YCbCr to RGB color conversion.\n\nThis function handles the case where both horizontal (0x68) and vertical (0x6c) direction\nflags are set in the texture info structure. It dispatches to either texture sample or\nlevel data processing based on mipmap state, then performs color space conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check mipmap level at pnMipmapInfo[2] and alternate path flag at pTextureInfo+0x4de0\n2. If both are zero: Call ProcessMipmapTextureSamples with mode=0, final flag=1\n3. Otherwise: Call ProcessMipmapLevelData with mode=0, final flag=1\n4. Always call ConvertYCbCrToRGB to convert processed data to RGB color space\n\nParameters:\n  pTextureInfo  - IJL_TextureInfo* containing format flags, dimensions, and source data\n  pSurfaceData  - IJL_SurfaceData* target surface with clipping info at offset 0x2c\n  pnMipmapInfo  - Mipmap level descriptors (level count at [0], current level at [2])\n  nDestX        - Destination X coordinate for output placement\n  nDestY        - Destination Y coordinate for output placement\n  dwScaleFactor - Scale factor applied to block dimensions during processing\n\nReturns:\n  void - Results written directly to destination surface buffer\n\nStructure Offsets (IJL_TextureInfo):\n  +0x4de0 - Alternate processing path flag (non-zero uses ProcessMipmapLevelData)\n\nCalled By:\n  DispatchMipmapProcessing (when both horizontal and vertical flags set)\n\nCalls:\n  ProcessMipmapTextureSamples - For initial mipmap level (level==0, no alternate path)\n  ProcessMipmapLevelData      - For subsequent levels or alternate processing path\n  ConvertYCbCrToRGB           - Final color space conversion to RGB format",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:17bed07ac234ee2a8f4cd52e23899724a44b38445b901eaa824c6c3b87ea08d7",
