      "name": "ProcessMipmapTextureSamples",
      "signature": "undefined ProcessMipmapTextureSamples(int param_1, int param_2, int * param_3, undefined4 param_4, int param_5, int param_6, int param_7, int param_8)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Processes mipmap texture samples by scaling and copying pixel data to destination buffer.\nThis function is part of the Intel JPEG Library (IJL) and handles texture mipmap \nlevel processing with scaling for texture mapping operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate scaled dimensions based on mipmap level (divide by mipmap divisor if level==1)\n2. Call FUN_60002700 to calculate clipping rectangle based on destination coordinates\n3. If clipping succeeds (return 0), determine initial destination line based on mode\n4. For mode==0: Process levels forward, adjusting dest line based on surface format type\n5. For mode==1: Process levels using separate offset tracking with buffer pointer\n6. Inner loops copy source bytes from 8x2 stride pattern to 32-byte row blocks\n7. Call FUN_60003620 to write processed buffer to destination surface\n8. Continue until all mipmap levels processed or offset limit (0x18 bytes) reached\n9. If texture format requires, fill remaining levels beyond processed count\n\nParameters:\n  pTextureInfo - Pointer to IJL_TextureInfo structure with dimensions, format, source data\n  pSurfaceData - Pointer to IJL_SurfaceData structure with clipping info at offset 0x2c\n  pnMipmapInfo - Pointer to mipmap info (level count at [0], level descriptors at [0xd])\n  nFlags       - Processing flags (passed but unused in this implementation path)\n  nDestX       - Destination X coordinate for clipping calculation\n  nDestY       - Destination Y coordinate for clipping calculation\n  nScaleFactor - Scale factor applied to block dimensions during copy\n  nMode        - Processing mode: 0=forward level processing, 1=offset-based processing\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value, writes directly to destination surface\n\nStructure Offsets (IJL_TextureInfo):\n  +0x04  - Clip rect base pointer\n  +0x20  - Clip calculation param 1\n  +0x24  - Clip calculation param 2  \n  +0x28  - Clip calculation param 3\n  +0x30  - Max mipmap levels count\n  +0x34  - Texture format type (2=special adjustment)\n  +0x3c  - Row stride in bytes\n  +0x58  - Subformat selector (1=special, 4=limited levels)\n  +0x74  - Processing complete flag (non-zero skips level fill)\n  +0x37b8 - Source texture width\n  +0x37bc - Source texture height  \n  +0x4834 - Source data buffer pointer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x80 (128) - Block stride in source data buffer\n  0x20 (32)  - Row size in destination temp buffer\n  0x18 (24)  - Maximum mipmap level offset limit (format 4)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
