      "name": "ProcessMipmapLevelData",
      "signature": "undefined ProcessMipmapLevelData(int param_1, int param_2, int * param_3, undefined4 param_4, int param_5, int param_6, int param_7, int param_8)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Processes mipmap level data by copying scaled pixel data from source to destination surface.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate clipping bounds via FUN_60002700 for source/destination regions\n2. If clipping check fails (returns non-zero), exit early\n3. Calculate initial Y position based on surface format flags\n4. Iterate through each mipmap level up to maximum level count\n5. For each mipmap level, calculate width/height scale factors\n6. Copy pixel data from source buffer to local temp buffer with scaling\n7. Call FUN_60003620 to write scaled data to destination surface\n8. Adjust Y position (increment or decrement based on format flags)\n9. If padding mode active, fill remaining levels with last buffer data\n\nParameters:\n  nSurfaceCtx - Surface context structure pointer (as int) with dimensions and buffers\n  nMipmapInfo - Mipmap information structure pointer (offset 0x2c has Y coord)\n  pnClipBounds - Pointer to clip bounds array (element 0 is max mip level)\n  nUnused - Unused parameter (always 1 in callers)\n  nDestX - Destination X coordinate for output\n  nDestY - Destination Y coordinate for output\n  nScaleFactor - Scale multiplier for mipmap dimensions\n  nUseMipmapTable - Mode flag: 0=use param bounds, 1=use internal table\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value, data written to destination surface directly",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:b37876b4f5f700180fccab7c70dc4fff538d0e058cb37726fade88c00397b452",
