      "name": "ProcessMipmapPixelTransfer",
      "signature": "undefined ProcessMipmapPixelTransfer(int param_1, int param_2, undefined4 param_3, int param_4, int param_5, uint param_6)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Processes mipmap pixel transfer by copying scaled pixel data from source buffer to destination surface.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get source data buffer pointer from texture context at offset 0x4834\n2. Get Y coordinate pointer from surface data at offset 0x2c\n3. Call FUN_60002700 to calculate clipping rectangle for destination region\n4. If clipping fails (non-zero return), exit early without processing\n5. Calculate initial destination line based on format type (mode 2 with subformat 1 adds 2)\n6. Iterate through each mipmap level up to maximum level count at offset 0x30\n7. For levels within mipmap table bounds (offset 0x37c0), copy pixels using block-based loop\n8. For format type 4 with level >= 1, duplicate previous row pixels (edge extension)\n9. For level 3 with format 5, fill destination with 0xFF (alpha fill)\n10. Adjust destination line (decrement for mode 2/subformat 1, else increment)\n11. Continue until all mipmap levels processed\n\nParameters:\n  nTextureCtx   - Pointer to texture context structure with dimensions and source data\n  nSurfaceData  - Pointer to surface data structure (Y coord at offset 0x2c)\n  nUnused       - Unused parameter (always 0 or 1 from callers)\n  nDestX        - Destination X coordinate for clipping calculation\n  nDestY        - Destination Y coordinate for clipping calculation\n  dwScaleFactor - Scale factor for block dimensions (used for both X and Y)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value, writes directly to destination surface\n\nStructure Offsets (Texture Context):\n  +0x04  - Clip rect base pointer (passed to FUN_60002700)\n  +0x20  - Clip calculation param 1\n  +0x24  - Clip calculation param 2\n  +0x28  - Clip calculation param 3\n  +0x30  - Max mipmap levels count / row stride\n  +0x34  - Texture format type (2=special Y adjustment)\n  +0x3c  - Column stride in bytes\n  +0x58  - Subformat selector (1=Y decrement, 4=edge extension)\n  +0x37c0 - Mipmap table entry count\n  +0x37cc - Mipmap table pointer (16 bytes per entry)\n  +0x4834 - Source data buffer pointer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x80 (128) - Block stride in source data buffer\n  0x10 (16)  - Mipmap table entry size\n  0xFF       - Alpha fill value for format 5 special case\n  0x08       - Pixels per source row in 8x2 stride pattern",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:866646fc75eb287f951ec1c2c177f55a70f604620c0f0ed057bdeeaf586b7d9f",
