      "name": "ConvertYCbCrToRGB",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYCbCrToRGB(int param_1, int param_2, int param_3, int param_4, int param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YCbCr color space data to RGB format within a JPEG image buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate color type (1=YCbCr, 2=YCrCb, 5=YCCK) at offset 0x34\n2. Call FUN_60002700 to calculate output bounds (nRow/nEndRow, dwStartCol/nEndCol)\n3. If pixel stride is 3 (24-bit RGB), process 3-byte pixels directly\n4. For each pixel, extract Y (luminance), Cb, Cr components\n5. Apply ITU-R BT.601 YCbCr to RGB conversion formulas:\n   - R = Y + 1.402 * Cr (0x167/256 = 1.402)\n   - G = Y - 0.344 * Cb - 0.714 * Cr (-0x58/256, -0xB7/256)\n   - B = Y + 1.772 * Cb (0x1C6/256 = 1.772)\n6. Clamp RGB values to 0-255 range\n7. Write converted RGB back to buffer (order depends on color type)\n\nParameters:\n  pImageCtx    - Pointer to JPEG image context structure\n  pOutputBuffer - Pointer to output buffer descriptor (RGB data at offset 0x2C)\n  nBlockX      - X block coordinate for scaling\n  nBlockY      - Y block coordinate for scaling\n  nScaleFactor - Scale factor multiplier for coordinate calculation\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nStructure Offsets (JpegImageContext):\n  0x04      - Clipping rectangle data\n  0x20      - Base X offset\n  0x24      - Base Y offset\n  0x28      - Width/stride info\n  0x30      - Pixel stride (3 for 24-bit RGB)\n  0x34      - Color type (1=YCbCr, 2=YCrCb, 5=YCCK)\n  0x3C      - Row stride in bytes\n  0x58      - Output format (3=RGB, 6=inverted RGB)\n  0x37B8    - Horizontal scale factor\n  0x37BC    - Vertical scale factor\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x167     - Cr to R coefficient (359/256 = 1.402)\n  0xB7      - Cr to G coefficient (183/256 = 0.714)\n  0x58      - Cb to G coefficient (88/256 = 0.344)\n  0x1C6     - Cb to B coefficient (454/256 = 1.772)\n  0xB2F5    - R channel offset (45813 = 179 * 256 + 25)\n  0x87F6    - G channel offset (34806 = 135 * 256 + 246)\n  0xE251    - B channel offset (57937 = 226 * 256 + 49)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:fb3bc47fdc8c2bba3d22b4a08c0f2be482e38bed5040366ddb0ce91c257f6353",
