      "name": "ConvertYCbCrToRgb",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYCbCrToRgb(int param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YCbCr color space to RGB for JPEG image data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate color type is 1, 2, or 5 and conversion flag at offset 0x68 is set\n2. Get bytes per pixel from offset 0x30 (3 for RGB, others for RGBA variants)\n3. For bytes_per_pixel == 3 (RGB mode):\n   a. Iterate over image rows (height at offset 0x28)\n   b. For each row, iterate over pixels (width*3 at offset 0x24)\n   c. Read Y, Cb, Cr bytes from source buffer\n   d. Apply fixed-point YCbCr to RGB conversion formulas\n   e. Clamp results to 0-255 range\n   f. Write RGB or BGR based on color type (2=BGR, 1/5=RGB)\n4. For other modes (RGBA variants):\n   a. Similar processing with different byte stride\n   b. Handle output format 6 (inverted colors) and format 3 (with alpha=0xFF)\n\nParameters:\npImageContext - Pointer to image context structure containing:\n  +0x20: Pointer to pixel data buffer\n  +0x24: Image width in pixels\n  +0x28: Image height in pixels (absolute value used)\n  +0x30: Bytes per pixel (3=RGB, 4=RGBA)\n  +0x34: Color type (1=RGB, 2=BGR, 5=RGB variant)\n  +0x3c: Row stride in bytes\n  +0x58: Output format (3=RGBA with alpha, 6=inverted RGB)\n  +0x68: Conversion enabled flag (must be non-zero)\n\nReturns: void\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x167 (359)     - Cr coefficient for Y->R: 1.402 * 256 = 358.9\n  0xB2F5 (45813)  - Offset for R channel: 128 * 358 = 45824\n  0x58 (88)       - Cb coefficient for G: 0.344 * 256 = 88.1\n  0xB7 (183)      - Cr coefficient for G: 0.714 * 256 = 182.8\n  0x87F6 (34806)  - Offset for G channel: 128 * (88+183) = 34688\n  0x1C6 (454)     - Cb coefficient for B: 1.772 * 256 = 453.6\n  0xE251 (57937)  - Offset for B channel: 128 * 454 = 58112\n\nYCbCr to RGB conversion formulas (ITU-R BT.601):\n  R = Y + 1.402 * (Cr - 128)\n  G = Y - 0.344 * (Cb - 128) - 0.714 * (Cr - 128)\n  B = Y + 1.772 * (Cb - 128)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
