      "name": "PrepareCoefficientsForMcu",
      "signature": "undefined PrepareCoefficientsForMcu(uint param_1, uint param_2, undefined4 param_3, ushort * param_4, int param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Prepares DCT coefficient blocks for an MCU at the specified grid position.\nThis function dispatches to the appropriate YCbCr color space conversion\nhandler based on the chroma subsampling mode stored in the JPEG context.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read chroma subsampling mode from pJpegContext+0x18\n2. Switch on mode value to select conversion path:\n   - Mode 3 (4:4:4): Full resolution chroma, 16x16 blocks\n   - Mode 4 (4:2:2): Horizontal subsampling, 16x16 blocks\n   - Mode 5 (4:2:0): Both directions subsampled, 16x8 blocks\n   - Mode 6 (4:1:1): Heavy horizontal subsampling, 16x8 blocks\n   - Mode 11 (4:4:0): Vertical subsampling only, 16x16 with stride 0x40\n   - Mode 14 (4:1:0): Both heavy subsampled, 8x8 blocks\n   - Mode 0: Grayscale or RGB (no chroma conversion)\n3. For each mode, calculate output buffer position:\n   a. Check if at last MCU column (compare with context+0x78)\n   b. Check if at last MCU row (compare with context+0x7c)\n   c. Apply partial width/height masks for edge blocks\n4. Call the appropriate function pointer from the conversion table\n5. For mode 0, check progressive and interleaved flags to route to handlers\n\nParameters:\n  pJpegContext (JpegImageContext*) - JPEG decoder context with subsampling mode\n  pScanState (JpegOutputBuffer*) - Scan state structure with output buffer\n  pScanHeader (int*) - Scan header with component descriptors\n  pwMcuColumn (ushort*) - Pointer to current MCU column index\n  nMcuRow (int) - Current MCU row index (0-based)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Output written to coefficient buffer at context+0x4834\n\nStructure Offsets (pJpegContext):\n  0x18  Chroma subsampling mode | 0x20  Output buffer base\n  0x24  Image width            | 0x28  Image height\n  0x3c  Row stride             | 0x68  Interleaved flag\n  0x6c  Progressive flag       | 0x78  MCU columns count\n  0x7c  MCU rows count         | 0x4834 Coeff buffer ptr\n\nSubsampling Modes: 3=4:4:4, 4=4:2:2, 5=4:2:0, 6=4:1:1, 11=4:4:0, 14=4:1:0",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
