      "name": "ConvertInterleavedRgbToYCbCr",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertInterleavedRgbToYCbCr(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts interleaved RGB image data to YCbCr color space with upsampling.\nThis function handles the color space conversion for JPEG encoding when the source\ndata is in interleaved format. It performs multi-phase processing including upsampling\nsource pixels to working buffers, applying RGB to YCbCr color matrix transformation,\nthen downsampling the result to the output buffer using scale factors.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x1028 bytes of stack space for working buffers\n2. Calculate effective component dimensions based on current row/column\n3. For boundary blocks compute partial widths from image dimensions\n4. Upsample source pixels from input to working buffer\n5. Pad incomplete blocks by replicating edge pixels\n6. Apply RGB to YCbCr color transformation using BT.601 coefficients\n7. For inverted color subtract channel values from 0xFF before conversion\n8. Downsample working buffer to output using scale factors\n9. Advance output pointer and repeat for each color component\n\nParameters:\npContext - JpegImageContext pointer with dimensions and buffer pointers\npOutput - JpegOutputBuffer pointer with current write position at offset 0x2C\npScaleInfo - JpegScaleInfo pointer with scale factors per component\nnColumn - Current column block index within the image\nnRow - Current row block index within the image\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. Results written to output buffer via pContext.",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:c9530b4703dafd8f46ec6c9e457a35ffc0cf01fd945175a2312391110be4a6f2",
