      "name": "ConvertBlockRgbToYCbCr",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertBlockRgbToYCbCr(int param_1, uint param_2, ushort * param_3, int param_4)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts an 8x8 DCT block from RGB to YCbCr color space for JPEG encoding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate actual block dimensions (handles edge blocks with partial samples)\n2. Compute source data offset based on block position\n3. For 4-component images with RGB/BGR ordering:\n   a. Read RGB triplets from source buffer\n   b. Apply ITU-R BT.601 RGB to Y conversion:\n      Y = (0x4D*R + 0x96*G + 0x1D*B - 0x7F80) >> 8\n   c. Pad partial blocks by replicating edge samples\n4. For multi-component images:\n   a. Load each color plane into separate 64-sample buffers\n   b. Apply full RGB to YCbCr conversion with Cb and Cr channels\n5. Replicate last row for blocks exceeding image height\n\nParameters:\n  pEncoderCtx - Pointer to JPEG encoder context structure\n    +0x20: Image data start offset\n    +0x24: Image width\n    +0x28: Image height\n    +0x30: Row stride in bytes\n    +0x34: Color order (1=RGB, 2=BGR, other=CMY inverted)\n    +0x3C: Line pitch\n    +0x54: Number of color components\n    +0x58: Component count (4 for RGBA/BGRA)\n    +0x78: Horizontal block count\n    +0x7C: Vertical block count\n    +0x4834: Pointer to DCT coefficient buffer\n  pBlockState - Pointer to block processing state\n    +0x2C: Current source data offset (updated on return)\n  nBlockColIdx - Current block column index (0 to blocks_wide-1)\n  nBlockRowIdx - Current block row index (0 to blocks_high-1)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Updates pBlockState and fills DCT buffer with YCbCr samples\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x4D (77)  - Y coefficient for R (0.299 * 256)\n  0x96 (150) - Y coefficient for G (0.587 * 256)\n  0x1D (29)  - Y coefficient for B (0.114 * 256)\n  0x7F80     - Level shift bias (127.5 * 256)\n  0x40 (64)  - DCT block size (8x8 samples)\n  0x2B (43)  - Cb coefficient for R\n  0x55 (85)  - Cb coefficient for G\n  0x15 (21)  - Cr coefficient for B\n  0x6B (107) - Cr coefficient for G",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:8958b85958a4f40a9b3542b510e0496b44cf2bf79af0b456fe7b5e4461004796",
