      "name": "ConvertYCbCrBlockToRgb565",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYCbCrBlockToRgb565(undefined8 * param_1, ulonglong * param_2, int param_3)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YCbCr color space data to RGB565 packed pixel format using MMX SIMD instructions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize pointers to Cb block (offset +0x80) and Cr block (offset +0x100) from input\n2. Loop 8 times (iVar6 = 7 down to 0), processing 16 pixels per iteration\n3. For each iteration:\n   a. Load and left-shift Cb/Cr samples by 4 bits for fixed-point precision\n   b. Multiply Cb by g_qwCbToGreenCoeff for green contribution\n   c. Multiply Cr by g_qwCrToRedCoeff for red contribution\n   d. Compute green channel using PMADDWD with g_qwGreenCalcCoeff\n   e. Apply rounding (g_qwRoundingConst) and right-shift by 12 bits\n   f. Add Y (luma) samples to color contributions with bias subtraction\n   g. Clamp RGB values to 0-255 range using saturation arithmetic\n   h. Pack 8-bit RGB into 16-bit RGB565 format using bit masks\n   i. Store 3 qwords (24 bytes = 8 RGB565 pixels) to output\n4. Advance output pointer by stride, input by 16 bytes each iteration\n\nParameters:\npYCbCrBlock - Pointer to interleaved YCbCr DCT block data (Y at offset 0, Cb at +0x80, Cr at +0x100)\npRgb565Output - Destination buffer for packed RGB565 pixels (24 bytes per row)\nnOutputStride - Byte offset between output rows (typically 24 for contiguous, or pitch for framebuffer)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Output written directly to pRgb565Output buffer\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x80 (128 bytes) - Offset from Y block to Cb block\n0x100 (256 bytes) - Offset from Y block to Cr block\n4 - Left shift for 12.4 fixed-point representation\n0xc (12) - Right shift for fixed-point to integer conversion\n7 - Loop count (8 iterations total for 8x8 DCT block)\n0xff (255) - Maximum 8-bit color value for clamping\n0xffffffff00ff00ff - Mask for interleaving packed bytes\n\nColor Conversion Coefficients (at g_qwCbToGreenCoeff etc.):\nStandard ITU-R BT.601 YCbCr to RGB matrix in 16-bit signed fixed-point format\n\nRGB565 Packing Masks (at g_qwRgb565MaskBits0-3, g_qwRgb565PackMask):\nExtract and position R(5 bits), G(6 bits), B(5 bits) into 16-bit word",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
