      "name": "ConvertYCbCrToRgbMmx",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYCbCrToRgbMmx(undefined8 * param_1, undefined8 * param_2, undefined8 * param_3, undefined4 param_4, ulonglong * param_5, int param_6)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YCbCr color space to 32-bit ARGB using MMX SIMD instructions.\n\nPerforms color space conversion on 8x8 pixel blocks using the standard ITU-R BT.601\nconversion formula with fixed-point arithmetic. Processes 4 pixels per MMX operation\nfor high throughput.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop counter to 8 iterations for processing 8 rows\n2. Clear all MMX registers (MM0-MM7) for clean state\n3. For each iteration:\n   a. Load Cr and Cb chroma samples, shift left 4 bits for precision\n   b. Multiply by color coefficients (g_qwYCbCrCrCoeff, g_qwYCbCrCbCoeff)\n   c. Subtract bias values to center chroma range\n   d. Calculate green component from both Cr and Cb contributions\n   e. Load Y (luma) samples and add/subtract color deltas with saturation\n   f. Pack results to bytes using PACKUSWB for clamping [0,255]\n   g. Interleave R, G, B channels with alpha from Y+0x300 offset\n   h. Store packed ARGB pixels to output buffer\n4. At midpoint (iteration 4), skip 0x80 bytes in Y plane for next block\n5. Advance pointers and continue until all 8 rows processed\n\nParameters:\npqwYPlane (ulonglong*): Pointer to Y (luma) plane data, 8 bytes per row\n                        Alpha values located at offset +0x300 from Y data\npqwCbPlane (ulonglong*): Pointer to Cb (blue-difference) chroma plane\npqwCrPlane (ulonglong*): Pointer to Cr (red-difference) chroma plane  \ndwBlockWidth (uint): Block width parameter (unused in current implementation)\npqwRgbOutput (ulonglong*): Destination buffer for packed ARGB output\nnOutputStride (int): Stride in bytes between output rows\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Output written directly to pqwRgbOutput buffer\n\nColor Conversion Coefficients (at 0x60025198-0x600251D0):\ng_qwYCbCrCrCoeff (0x1670): Cr to R/B coefficient\ng_qwYCbCrCbCoeff (0x1C60): Cb to R/B coefficient  \ng_qwYCbCrCbGreenCoeff (0x0058): Cb contribution to green\ng_qwYCbCrCrGreenCoeff (0x00B7): Cr contribution to green\ng_qwYCbCrRedBias (0x00E3): Red channel bias\ng_qwYCbCrBlueBias (0x00B3): Blue channel bias\ng_qwYCbCrGreenBias (0x87F6): Green channel bias\ng_qwRgbOutputBias (0x00FF): Output level bias (128)\n\nMemory Layout:\nY Plane: 8 bytes per row, alpha at +0x300, +0x308, +0x380, +0x388\nCb/Cr Planes: 8 bytes per quadword, 16-byte stride per iteration\nOutput: 64 bytes per row pair (8 ARGB pixels * 2 rows * 4 bytes)\n\nStack Frame (0x60 bytes):\n[EBP-0x3C] to [EBP-0x64]: MMX temporary storage for color deltas\n  Offset 0x00: Blue delta low\n  Offset 0x08: Red delta low  \n  Offset 0x10: Green delta low\n  Offset 0x18: Blue delta high\n  Offset 0x20: Red delta high\n  Offset 0x28: Green delta high\n\nPerformance Notes:\n- Uses all 8 MMX registers for maximum parallelism\n- Saturating arithmetic (PADDSW/PSUBSW) for automatic clamping\n- PACKUSWB provides 0-255 range clamping\n- Unrolled loop body processes 2 output rows per iteration",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
