      "name": "ConvertYCbCrToRgb565_MMX",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYCbCrToRgb565_MMX(undefined8 * param_1, undefined8 * param_2, undefined8 * param_3, ulonglong * param_4, int param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YCbCr color space data to packed RGB565 format using MMX SIMD instructions.\n\nProcesses 32 pixels per call (8 pixels per iteration x 4 iterations) using fixed-point\narithmetic optimized for video/image decoding pipelines.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load 8 pixels of Y, Cb, Cr data from input arrays\n2. Scale chroma components (Cb, Cr) by shifting left 4 bits\n3. Apply color conversion matrix using fixed-point multiplication:\n   - R = Y + 1.402 * Cr (via g_qwCbToBlueCoeff)\n   - G = Y - 0.344 * Cb - 0.714 * Cr (via g_qwCrToGreenCoeff, g_qwYChannelCoeff)\n   - B = Y + 1.772 * Cb (via coefficient multiplication)\n4. Subtract bias values to center chroma around zero\n5. Apply 12-bit right shift for fixed-point to integer conversion\n6. Saturate RGB values to 0-255 range using PADDUSW/PSUBUSW\n7. Pack RGB channels into RGB565 format (5 red, 6 green, 5 blue bits)\n8. Store packed pixels to output buffer with configurable stride\n9. Advance pointers and repeat for remaining pixel blocks\n\nParameters:\n  pYData      - Pointer to luminance (Y) channel data, 8 bytes per block (ulonglong*)\n  pCbData     - Pointer to blue-difference chroma (Cb) data (ulonglong*)\n  pCrData     - Pointer to red-difference chroma (Cr) data (ulonglong*)\n  pRgbOut     - Pointer to output buffer for packed RGB565 pixels (ulonglong*)\n  nOutputStride - Byte offset between output rows (int)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSSA Temporaries (decompiler-generated, cannot be renamed):\n  uVar1, uVar2, uVar3 - 64-bit MMX register temporaries for intermediate calculations\n  sVar1, sVar2, sVar3 - 16-bit channel component temporaries\n\nConstants Used:\n  g_qwCrToGreenCoeff (0x600251d8) - Cr contribution to green channel\n  g_qwCbToBlueCoeff (0x600251e0)  - Cb contribution to blue channel  \n  g_qwYChannelCoeff (0x600251e8)  - Y channel scaling coefficients\n  g_qwCbBiasValue (0x600251f0)    - Cb channel bias offset\n  g_qwCrBiasValue (0x600251f8)    - Cr channel bias offset\n  g_qwRoundingOffset (0x60025200) - Rounding value for fixed-point conversion\n  g_qwRgb565Mask* (0x60025208-20) - Bit masks for RGB565 channel packing\n  g_qwSaturationLower/Upper       - Clamping bounds for RGB saturation\n\nPerformance Notes:\n  - Uses MMX registers MM0-MM7 for parallel 16-bit operations\n  - Processes 4 pixels simultaneously per MMX operation\n  - Output stride allows flexible framebuffer layouts\n\nPhantom Variables (assembly-only MMX spill slots):\n  local_18, local_20, local_28, local_30, local_38, local_40 - Stack temporaries\n  for intermediate Cb/Cr coefficients during color conversion",
