      "name": "ConvertYCbCrToRgb565Block",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYCbCrToRgb565Block(undefined8 * param_1, undefined8 * param_2, undefined8 * param_3, ulonglong * param_4, int param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YCbCr color space to RGB565 format using MMX SIMD instructions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Loop 4 times to process a 16x2 pixel block (32 pixels total)\n2. For each iteration, load Cb and Cr chroma values and shift left by 4 bits\n3. Apply color conversion coefficients using packed multiply-high (PMULHW)\n4. Subtract bias values to center the chroma channels\n5. Load Y (luminance) values and compute RGB components:\n   - Blue = Y + Cb_scaled\n   - Red = Y + Cr_scaled  \n   - Green = Y - luma_correction\n6. Clamp RGB values to 0-255 range using saturating pack\n7. Pack 8-bit RGB into 16-bit RGB565 format:\n   - Red: bits 15-11 (5 bits)\n   - Green: bits 10-5 (6 bits)\n   - Blue: bits 4-0 (5 bits)\n8. Apply channel masks and combine using bitwise operations\n9. Store 3 qwords (24 bytes) per row, advance by stride\n\nParameters:\n  pqwYChannel    - Pointer to Y luminance channel data (4 qwords per iteration)\n  pqwCbChannel   - Pointer to Cb chroma channel data (2 qwords per iteration)\n  pqwCrChannel   - Pointer to Cr chroma channel data (2 qwords per iteration)\n  pqwRgb565Out   - Pointer to output RGB565 buffer\n  nOutputStride  - Byte stride between output rows\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nGlobal Coefficients Used:\n  g_qwCrToGreenCoeff   - Cr to green channel coefficient\n  g_qwCbToBlueCoeff    - Cb to blue channel coefficient\n  g_qwYChannelCoeff    - Y luminance coefficient for RGB\n  g_qwCbBiasValue      - Cb channel bias offset (128 scaled)\n  g_qwCrBiasValue      - Cr channel bias offset (128 scaled)\n  g_qwRoundingOffset   - Rounding constant for fixed-point math\n  g_qwRgb565Mask*      - Bit masks for RGB565 channel extraction\n  g_qwGreenChannelMask - Mask for green channel isolation\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x4    - Loop count (processes 4 blocks of 8 pixels each)\n  0xc    - Right shift amount for fixed-point to integer (12 bits)\n  0x100  - Upper clamp boundary (256)\n  0xff   - Maximum valid pixel value (255)\n  0x8    - Shift for green channel positioning\n  0x10   - Shift for green2 mask positioning\n  0x28   - Shift for red channel extraction (40 bits)\n  0x20   - Shift for qword high/low separation (32 bits)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:22b6875331648bafe85753e94731b6909d235d0669800af6aef746b2220f12e1",
