      "name": "ConvertYCbCrToRgbMMX",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYCbCrToRgbMMX(undefined8 * param_1, undefined8 * param_2, undefined8 * param_3, ulonglong * param_4, int param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YCbCr color data to packed 32-bit ARGB using MMX SIMD instructions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop counter to 8 (processes 8 rows of 8-pixel blocks)\n2. Clear all MMX registers (MM0-MM7) for accumulation\n3. For each iteration:\n   a. Load Y, Cb, Cr component data from input arrays\n   b. Shift Cb/Cr values left by 4 bits for fixed-point precision\n   c. Apply color conversion matrix via PMULHW/PMULLW:\n      - Red   = Y + Cr * 1.402 (coeff at g_awYCbCrCoeffCr1)\n      - Green = Y - Cb * 0.344 - Cr * 0.714 (combined offset)\n      - Blue  = Y + Cb * 1.772 (coeff at g_awYCbCrCoeffCb1)\n   d. Saturate results using PADDSW/PSUBSW and PACKUSWB\n   e. Pack RGB bytes into 32-bit ARGB format with alpha from g_qwAlphaMask\n   f. Store 8 pixels (64 bytes) to output buffer\n4. Advance pointers by 16 bytes (8 pixels of Y/Cb/Cr)\n5. At iteration 4, skip ahead by 128 bytes in source (chroma subsampling)\n6. Continue until all 8 rows processed\n\nParameters:\n    pYData       - Pointer to Y (luma) component data, 16-bit signed values\n    pCbData      - Pointer to Cb (blue-difference chroma) data, 16-bit signed\n    pCrData      - Pointer to Cr (red-difference chroma) data, 16-bit signed\n    pRgbOutput   - Pointer to output buffer for packed 32-bit ARGB pixels\n    nOutputStride - Bytes to advance output pointer between rows\n\nReturns:\n    void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n    - Handles 4:2:0 chroma subsampling (special pointer advance at row 4)\n    - Uses saturating arithmetic to prevent overflow/underflow\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n    0x1670 (5744)  - Cr coefficient for red channel (1.402 * 4096)\n    0x1C60 (7264)  - Cb coefficient for blue channel (1.772 * 4096)\n    0x58 (88)      - Cr coefficient low for green\n    0xB7 (183)     - Cb coefficient low for green\n    0xE3 (227)     - Combined offset for color space\n    0x87F6 (-30730) - Green offset compensation (signed)\n    0xFF000000     - Alpha mask (fully opaque)\n    ECX=8          - Loop iterations (8 rows of 8x8 blocks)\n\nNotes:\n    - Uses MMX instruction set (not SSE) for compatibility\n    - Fixed-point arithmetic with 8-bit fractional precision\n    - Output format is 32-bit ARGB (0xAARRGGBB)\n    - Decompilation may fail due to complex MMX register usage",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
