      "name": "CompareRectNotEquals",
      "signature": "undefined4 CompareRectNotEquals(int * param_1, int * param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Compares two Rect structures for inequality.\n\nPerforms a field-by-field comparison of two 16-byte Rect structures,\nchecking all four integer fields (left, top, right, bottom) for equality.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compare field at offset 0x0 (left) - if different, return 1\n2. Compare field at offset 0x8 (right) - if different, return 1\n3. Compare field at offset 0x4 (top) - if different, return 1\n4. Compare field at offset 0xC (bottom) - if different, return 1\n5. All fields match - return 0\n\nParameters:\n  pRect1 - Pointer to the first Rect structure to compare\n  pRect2 - Pointer to the second Rect structure to compare\n\nReturns:\n  bool - TRUE (1) if rectangles are NOT equal (any field differs)\n         FALSE (0) if rectangles ARE equal (all fields match)\n\nStructure Layout (Rect - 16 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field   Type  Description\n  0x00    4     left    int   Left edge X coordinate\n  0x04    4     top     int   Top edge Y coordinate\n  0x08    4     right   int   Right edge X coordinate\n  0x0C    4     bottom  int   Bottom edge Y coordinate\n\nNote: Comparison order is optimized (0, 8, 4, C) - likely for cache efficiency\nor based on expected difference frequency in calling patterns.",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
