      "name": "TransformRectByOffset",
      "signature": "undefined TransformRectByOffset(int * param_1, int * param_2, int * param_3)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Transforms a source rectangle to relative coordinates by subtracting an offset point.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compare source rect with global zero rect (g_anDecodeValidationThresholds)\n2. If source equals zero rect, copy zero rect to output and return early\n3. Otherwise, compute relative coordinates:\n   - OutRect.left = SrcRect.left - Offset.x\n   - OutRect.top = SrcRect.top - Offset.y\n   - OutRect.right = SrcRect.right - Offset.x\n   - OutRect.bottom = SrcRect.bottom - Offset.y\n\nParameters:\n  pnOutRect - Pointer to output rectangle (int[4]: left, top, right, bottom)\n  pnSrcRect - Pointer to source rectangle in absolute coordinates\n  pnOffset  - Pointer to offset point (int[2]: x, y) to subtract from source\n\nReturns:\n  void - Result stored in pnOutRect\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If source rect equals zero rect, output is set to zero rect (identity case)\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field    Type  Description\n  0x0     4     left     int   Left edge X coordinate\n  0x4     4     top      int   Top edge Y coordinate\n  0x8     4     right    int   Right edge X coordinate\n  0xC     4     bottom   int   Bottom edge Y coordinate",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
