      "name": "ConvertYCbCrBlockToRGB",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYCbCrBlockToRGB(int param_1, short * param_2, int param_3, int param_4, int * param_5, int param_6)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts a YCbCr color space 8x8 block to RGB format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute destination row offset using pnRegion[1] (startY) and nRowStride\n2. Precompute color conversion delta tables (16 entries for 8x8 subsampled block):\n   - anRedDelta[i] = (Cr * 0x167 - 0xB2F5) >> 8   (R = Y + 1.402*Cr)\n   - anGreenDelta[i] = (Cr*0xB7 + Cb*0x58 - 0x87F6) >> 8   (G = Y - 0.344*Cb - 0.714*Cr)\n   - anBlueDelta[i] = (Cb * 0x1C6 - 0xE251) >> 8   (B = Y + 1.772*Cb)\n3. Iterate over rows from pnRegion[1] to pnRegion[3] (startY to endY)\n4. Iterate over columns from pnRegion[0] to pnRegion[2] (startX to endX)\n5. For each pixel, compute chroma index = col/2 + (row/2)*4 for 4:2:0 subsampling\n6. Compute RGB: R = clamp(Y + anRedDelta), G = clamp(Y - anGreenDelta), B = clamp(Y + anBlueDelta)\n7. Write RGB triplet to destination buffer\n\nParameters:\n    pnLumaData (short*) - Pointer to 8x8 block of Y (luminance) samples\n    pnCbData (short*) - Pointer to 4x4 block of Cb (blue-diff chroma) samples\n    pnCrData (short*) - Pointer to 4x4 block of Cr (red-diff chroma) samples\n    pbDstRgb (byte*) - Destination RGB buffer\n    pnRegion (int*) - Region bounds array [startX, startY, endX, endY]\n    nRowStride (int) - Bytes per row in destination buffer\n\nReturns:\n    void - Results written directly to pbDstRgb buffer\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n    0x167 (359) - Fixed-point 1.402 * 256 for Cr->R conversion\n    0xB7 (183) - Fixed-point 0.714 * 256 for Cr->G conversion\n    0x58 (88) - Fixed-point 0.344 * 256 for Cb->G conversion\n    0x1C6 (454) - Fixed-point 1.772 * 256 for Cb->B conversion\n    0xB2F5, 0x87F6, 0xE251 - Bias offsets to center conversion range",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
