      "name": "ConvertYCbCrToRgb8x16Block",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYCbCrToRgb8x16Block(short * param_1, short * param_2, short * param_3, undefined1 * param_4, int param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts an 8x16 block of YCbCr color space samples to RGB format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. For each iteration (4 total), process 2 rows of 8 pixels each\n2. Read 4 Cr samples and 4 Cb samples for each 2-row pair\n3. Compute color conversion offsets using fixed-point coefficients:\n   - Red offset = Cr * 0x167 - 0xB2F5 (scaled by 256)\n   - Green offset = Cr * 0xB7 + Cb * 0x58 - 0x87F6 (scaled by 256)\n   - Blue offset = Cb * 0x1C6 - 0xE251 (scaled by 256)\n4. For each Y sample, compute RGB:\n   - R = clamp(Y + redOffset, 0, 255)\n   - G = clamp(Y - greenOffset, 0, 255)\n   - B = clamp(Y + blueOffset, 0, 255)\n5. Write 24 bytes (8 RGB triplets) per row, advance by stride\n\nParameters:\n  pnYSamples     - Array of 128 luminance samples (16 rows x 8 samples), 16-bit signed\n  pnCbSamples    - Array of 32 Cb chrominance samples (8 groups of 4), 16-bit signed\n  pnCrSamples    - Array of 32 Cr chrominance samples (8 groups of 4), 16-bit signed\n  pbRgbOutput    - Output buffer for RGB data (at least 16 * stride bytes)\n  nOutputStride  - Bytes between output rows (typically width * 3)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x167 (359)   - Cr to R coefficient (1.402 * 256)\n  0xB7 (183)    - Cr to G coefficient (0.714 * 256) \n  0x58 (88)     - Cb to G coefficient (0.344 * 256)\n  0x1C6 (454)   - Cb to B coefficient (1.772 * 256)\n  0xB2F5        - Red bias correction\n  0x87F6        - Green bias correction\n  0xE251        - Blue bias correction\n\nNotes:\n  - Uses 4:2:0 chroma subsampling (4 Y samples share 1 Cb/Cr pair)\n  - Processes block in row pairs sharing same chrominance values\n  - Fixed-point arithmetic with 8-bit fraction (>> 8 for final result)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
