      "name": "ConvertYUVToRGB",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYUVToRGB(int param_1, short * param_2, int param_3, int param_4, int * param_5, int param_6)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YUV color space data to RGB format for video frame display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate starting output position based on pRect[1] (row offset) and stride\n2. Pre-compute color conversion deltas for 16 chroma samples:\n   - Red delta: (V * 0x167 - 0xb2f5) >> 8    (V to R contribution)\n   - Green delta: (V * 0xb7 + U * 0x58 - 0x87f6) >> 8  (U+V to G)\n   - Blue delta: (U * 0x1c6 - 0xe251) >> 8   (U to B contribution)\n3. Iterate over rectangle region defined by pRect:\n   - For each pixel, combine Y (luminance) with pre-computed chroma deltas\n   - Clamp results to [0, 255] range\n   - Write BGR triplet to output buffer\n\nParameters:\n  pYBuffer - Input luminance (Y) buffer as 16-bit signed values\n  pUBuffer - Input chroma U buffer (Cb component)\n  pVBuffer - Input chroma V buffer (Cr component)\n  pRgbOutput - Output RGB buffer (BGR byte order)\n  pRect - Rectangle struct: [x, y, width, height] defining region to convert\n  nStride - Bytes per row in output buffer\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x167 (359) - V to R conversion coefficient (scaled)\n  0xb2f5 (45813) - R bias value\n  0xb7 (183) - V to G conversion coefficient\n  0x58 (88) - U to G conversion coefficient\n  0x87f6 (34806) - G bias value\n  0x1c6 (454) - U to B conversion coefficient\n  0xe251 (57937) - B bias value\n  0xff (255) - Maximum color component value\n\nNotes:\n  - Uses 4:2:0 chroma subsampling (2x2 luma pixels share one chroma pair)\n  - Output is BGR order, not RGB\n  - Decompiler SSA names (iVar*, sVar*, etc.) are temporaries for:\n    sVar1 = chroma U value, iVar2 = chroma V or luma, iVar3 = clamped color,\n    iVar4 = row index, iVar5 = loop count/chroma index, iVar7 = column index,\n    psVar6 = chroma pointer, pbVar8 = RGB destination pointer",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:6b7daa27c2b0196ff1fac7c85b5a6102ec640e294d1aa6e5afd6dc779697245f",
