      "name": "ConvertYCbCrToRGB8x8Block",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYCbCrToRGB8x8Block(short * param_1, short * param_2, short * param_3, undefined1 * param_4, int param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts an 8x8 block of YCbCr color space samples to RGB format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. For each of 8 rows, read Cr and Cb chroma samples at current position\n2. Compute red delta = (Cb * 227 + offset) >> 8 using fixed-point arithmetic\n3. Compute green delta from combined Cr and Cb coefficients with offset\n4. Compute blue delta = (Cr * 359 - 0xB2F5) >> 8\n5. For each of 8 Y luma samples in current row:\n   5a. Calculate R = Y + red_delta\n   5b. Calculate G = Y - green_delta\n   5c. Calculate B = Y + blue_delta\n   5d. Clamp each component to [0, 255] range\n   5e. Write RGB triplet to output buffer\n6. Advance chroma pointers by 16 bytes (4 samples)\n7. Advance output pointer by row stride\n8. Repeat for all 8 rows\n\nParameters:\n  pnYSamples - Pointer to 64 short Y (luminance) samples in row-major 8x8 block\n  pnCbSamples - Pointer to 4 short Cb (blue-difference chroma) samples for 2x2 subsampled block\n  pnCrSamples - Pointer to 4 short Cr (red-difference chroma) samples for 2x2 subsampled block\n  pbRGBOutput - Destination buffer for 24-bit RGB output (3 bytes per pixel)\n  nRowStride - Bytes between consecutive output rows\n\nReturns:\n  void - RGB data written directly to pbRGBOutput buffer\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0xB2F5 (45813) - Blue channel coefficient scaling factor\n  0x780A (-34806 signed) - Green channel combined offset\n  0x1DAF (-57937 signed) - Red channel coefficient offset\n  0xFF (255) - Maximum byte value for clamping\n  SAR 8 - Divide by 256 for fixed-point to integer conversion\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  All RGB values are clamped to valid byte range [0, 255]\n  Chroma subsampling means each Cb/Cr sample covers 2x2 luma pixels",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:aacae02eabf74e6feb685f4ab85e1f9a24f276e7b8ee9610f1f29df2a9fcd341",
