      "name": "ConvertYCbCrPartialBlockToRgb888",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYCbCrPartialBlockToRgb888(int param_1, int param_2, int param_3, int param_4, int * param_5, int param_6)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YCbCr color space data to RGB888 format for a partial block region.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load block bounds from pnBlockBounds structure (x_start, y_start, x_end, y_end)\n2. Calculate starting output row position based on y_start and stride\n3. For each row from y_start to y_end:\n   a. For each column from x_start to x_end:\n      - Read Y (luminance), Cb (blue chroma), Cr (red chroma) samples\n      - Apply ITU-R BT.601 color conversion using fixed-point arithmetic\n      - Clamp RGB values to 0-255 range\n      - Write 3 bytes (R, G, B) to output buffer\n   b. Advance output pointer by stride for next row\n\nParameters:\npCrPlane - Pointer to Cr (red chrominance) plane samples (16-bit signed)\npCbPlane - Pointer to Cb (blue chrominance) plane samples (16-bit signed)\npYPlane - Pointer to Y (luminance) plane samples (16-bit signed)\npbRgbOutput - Destination buffer for RGB888 output (3 bytes per pixel)\npnBlockBounds - Block region descriptor: [0]=x_start, [1]=y_start, [2]=x_end, [3]=y_end\nnOutputStride - Output buffer row stride in bytes\n\nReturns:\nvoid - RGB data written directly to pbRgbOutput\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x167 (359) - Cr->R coefficient (1.402 * 256) for R = Y + 1.402*(Cr-128)\n0x1c6 (454) - Cb->B coefficient (1.772 * 256) for B = Y + 1.772*(Cb-128)\n0xb7 (183) - Cr->G coefficient (0.714 * 256) for G adjustment\n0x58 (88) - Cb->G coefficient (0.344 * 256) for G adjustment\n0xb2f5 (45813) - Cr bias (128 * 1.402 * 256) for R channel offset\n0x87f6 (34806) - Combined G bias for green channel offset\n0xe251 (57937) - Cb bias (128 * 1.772 * 256) for B channel offset\n\nStructure Layout (pnBlockBounds):\nOffset | Size | Field   | Type | Description\n0x00   | 4    | x_start | int  | Starting X coordinate in block\n0x04   | 4    | y_start | int  | Starting Y coordinate in block\n0x08   | 4    | x_end   | int  | Ending X coordinate (exclusive)\n0x0C   | 4    | y_end   | int  | Ending Y coordinate (exclusive)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
