      "name": "ConvertYCbCrBlockToRgb",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYCbCrBlockToRgb(int param_1, short * param_2, int param_3, int param_4, int param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts an 8x8 block of YCbCr color space samples to RGB pixels.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize outer loop counter to 8 (rows)\n2. For each row:\n   a. Initialize inner loop counter to 8 (columns)\n   b. For each pixel in the row:\n      - Read Cb (chrominance blue) value from pnCbPlane\n      - Read Cr (chrominance red) value from pnBasePlane\n      - Read Y (luminance) value from pnYPlane\n      - Calculate Red: Y + (Cr * 359 - 45813) >> 8, clamp to [0,255]\n      - Calculate Green: Y - (Cb * 183 - 34806 + Cr * 88) >> 8, clamp to [0,255]\n      - Calculate Blue: Y + (Cr * 454 - 57937) >> 8, clamp to [0,255]\n      - Write R, G, B bytes to output buffer (3 bytes per pixel)\n   c. Advance output pointer by nOutputStride\n3. Repeat for all 8 rows\n\nParameters:\n- pnYPlane: Pointer to Y (luminance) plane samples (short array, 64 samples)\n- pnBasePlane: Pointer to Cr (chrominance red) plane samples (short array, 64 samples)\n- pnCbPlane: Pointer to Cb (chrominance blue) plane samples (short array, 64 samples)\n- pbRgbOutput: Pointer to output RGB buffer (8x8 pixels x 3 bytes = 192 bytes minimum)\n- nOutputStride: Bytes per row in output buffer (allows for padding/larger image)\n\nReturns:\n- void (output written directly to pbRgbOutput)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x167 (359): Red coefficient for Cr (scaled by 256)\n- 0xb7 (183): Green coefficient for Cb (scaled by 256)\n- 0x58 (88): Green coefficient for Cr (scaled by 256)\n- 0x1c6 (454): Blue coefficient for Cb (scaled by 256)\n- 0xb2f5 (45813): Red offset = 359 * 128 - 1 (centering adjustment)\n- 0x87f6 (34806): Green offset = 183 * 128 + 88 * 128 - combined adjustment\n- 0xe251 (57937): Blue offset = 454 * 128 - 1 (centering adjustment)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
