      "comment": "Converts a YCbCr color block to RGB pixel data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract image dimensions from pnImageInfo structure (width at +0x0, height at +0x4, bounds at +0x8, +0xc)\n2. Calculate starting offset in destination buffer using stride and height\n3. Iterate over each row (outer loop checks against field +0xc)\n4. For each pixel in row (inner loop checks against field +0x8):\n   a. Read Y (luminance) sample from pbYPlane\n   b. Read Cb (blue chrominance) from pbCbPlane\n   c. Read Cr (red chrominance) from pbCrPlane\n   d. Apply YCbCr to RGB conversion using fixed-point arithmetic:\n      - R = Y + 1.402 * Cr (scaled by 256, magic: 0xb2f5 offset)\n      - G = Y - 0.344 * Cb - 0.714 * Cr (scaled, magic: 0x780a offset)\n      - B = Y + 1.772 * Cb (scaled by 256, magic: 0x1daf offset)\n   e. Clamp each channel to [0, 255] range\n   f. Write RGB triplet to destination buffer\n5. Advance pointers by stride for next row\n\nParameters:\n  pbYPlane - Pointer to Y (luminance) plane data\n  pbCbPlane - Pointer to Cb (blue-difference chrominance) plane data\n  pbCrPlane - Pointer to Cr (red-difference chrominance) plane data\n  pbRgbDest - Destination buffer for RGB output (3 bytes per pixel)\n  pnImageInfo - Pointer to image info structure with dimensions\n  nStride - Bytes per row in destination buffer\n\nReturns:\n  void - Writes RGB data directly to pbRgbDest\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0xb2f5 - Offset for Cr to R conversion (scaled 1.402 coefficient)\n  0x780a - Offset for Cb/Cr to G conversion (negated, scaled)\n  0x1daf - Offset for Cb to B conversion (scaled 1.772 coefficient)\n  0xff - Maximum byte value for clamping (255)",
