      "name": "ConvertYCbCrBlockToRgb",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYCbCrBlockToRgb(int param_1, int param_2, short * param_3, int param_4, int param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts an 8x8 block of YCbCr color space data to RGB format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize outer loop counter to 8 (8 rows)\n2. For each row, initialize inner loop counter to 8 (8 pixels)\n3. For each pixel:\n   a. Read Y (luminance), Cb (blue chrominance), Cr (red chrominance) samples\n   b. Compute Blue:  B = Y + ((Cr * 454 - 57937) >> 8)\n   c. Compute Green: G = Y - ((Y * 183 + Cb * 88 - 34806) >> 8)\n   d. Compute Red:   R = Y + ((Cb * 359 - 45813) >> 8)\n   e. Clamp each channel to [0, 255] range\n   f. Store RGB triplet to destination buffer\n4. Advance destination pointer by stride for next row\n\nParameters:\n  nYOffset      - Byte offset from pYCbCrData to Y sample array\n  nCbOffset     - Byte offset from pYCbCrData to Cb sample array\n  pYCbCrData    - Pointer to interleaved YCbCr sample buffer (16-bit samples)\n  nRgbDestOffset - Starting offset in RGB destination buffer\n  nRgbStride    - Bytes per row in RGB destination buffer\n\nReturns:\n  void - RGB data written directly to destination buffer\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x1c6 (454)   - Cr to Blue conversion coefficient\n  0xb7 (183)    - Y coefficient for Green channel\n  0x58 (88)     - Cb coefficient for Green channel\n  0x167 (359)   - Cb to Red conversion coefficient\n  0xe251 (57937) - Blue channel bias (454 * 128)\n  0x87f6 (34806) - Green channel bias\n  0xb2f5 (45813) - Red channel bias (359 * 128)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:81304c94dbb6e991a42989c43dfb9f5ac781ced60f9c7b5c21567df46cec966e",
