      "name": "ConvertYCbCr420ToRgb888WithClipping",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYCbCr420ToRgb888WithClipping(int param_1, short * param_2, int param_3, int param_4, int * param_5, int param_6)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts 4:2:0 subsampled YCbCr data to RGB888 format with clipping support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Precompute chroma conversion coefficients for 8x8 pixel region\n   - Process 4 chroma samples per inner iteration, 8 iterations total (32 samples)\n   - For each Cb/Cr pair, calculate R/G/B conversion offsets using fixed-point math\n   - Store scaled coefficients in three local arrays (red, green, blue)\n2. Offset output pointer by clip rectangle top row * stride\n3. For each row in clip rectangle [y1, y3):\n   a. For each column in clip rectangle [x0, x2):\n      - Calculate chroma index (col/2 + row) for 4:2:0 upsampling\n      - Read Y luma sample\n      - Add red coefficient to Y, clamp to [0, 255], store R\n      - Subtract green coefficient from Y, clamp to [0, 255], store G\n      - Add blue coefficient to Y, clamp to [0, 255], store B\n   b. Advance output pointer by stride\n\nParameters:\n   pYPlane - Pointer to 8x8 luma (Y) sample buffer, 16-bit signed per sample\n   pCbPlane - Pointer to 4x4 Cb chroma buffer (4:2:0 subsampled), 16-bit signed\n   pCrPlane - Pointer to 4x4 Cr chroma buffer (4:2:0 subsampled), 16-bit signed\n   pRgbOutput - Destination buffer for RGB888 packed pixels (3 bytes per pixel)\n   pClipRect - Clip rectangle as int[4]: {left, top, right, bottom}\n   nOutputStride - Byte stride between output rows\n\nReturns:\n   void\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n   0x167 (359) - Cr to R conversion coefficient (1.402 * 256)\n   0xB7 (183) - Cr to G conversion coefficient (0.714 * 256)\n   0x58 (88) - Cb to G conversion coefficient (0.344 * 256)\n   0x1C6 (454) - Cb to B conversion coefficient (1.772 * 256)\n   0xB2F5 (-19723) - Cr to R bias offset\n   0x87F6 (-30726) - Combined Cr+Cb to G bias offset\n   0xE251 (-7599) - Cb to B bias offset\n   0x40 (64) - Total chroma coefficient entries (32 samples * 2 bytes)\n   0xFF (255) - Maximum RGB channel value for clamping\n   8 - Luma block width (8x8 DCT block standard)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n   - Empty clip rectangle (y1 >= y3): Early exit, no output\n   - Empty row (x0 >= x2): Skip row processing\n\nStructure Layout (pClipRect):\n   Offset  Size  Field   Type  Description\n   0x00    4     left    int   Left column (x0)\n   0x04    4     top     int   Top row (y1)\n   0x08    4     right   int   Right column exclusive (x2)\n   0x0C    4     bottom  int   Bottom row exclusive (y3)\n\nContext:\n   Part of Intel JPEG Library (IJL) color space conversion routines.\n   Used for YCbCr 4:2:0 to RGB888 conversion with partial block clipping.\n   Scalar implementation for CPU fallback path.",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
