      "name": "ConvertYCbCrToRgb8x8",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYCbCrToRgb8x8(short * param_1, short * param_2, short * param_3, undefined1 * param_4, int param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YCbCr color space samples to RGB for an 8x8 DCT block (JPEG-style).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. For each of 8 rows in the block:\n   a. Load 4 pairs of Cr/Cb samples (subsampled 4:2:0 assumed)\n   b. Compute fixed-point color conversion offsets for each sample pair:\n      - nRedOffset = Cr * 0x167 - 0xB2F5 (scaled by 256, ~1.402 coefficient)\n      - nGreenOffset = Cr * 0xB7 + Cb * 0x58 - 0x87F6 (scaled, ~-0.714, -0.344)\n      - nBlueOffset = Cb * 0x1C6 - 0xE251 (scaled by 256, ~1.772 coefficient)\n   c. For each of 8 Y samples in the row:\n      - R = clamp(Y + nRedOffset, 0, 255)\n      - G = clamp(Y - nGreenOffset, 0, 255)\n      - B = clamp(Y + nBlueOffset, 0, 255)\n   d. Write 24 bytes (8 RGB triplets) to output, advance by stride\n2. Process 8 rows total (64 pixels output)\n\nParameters:\n  pnY       - Pointer to 64 signed 16-bit Y (luminance) samples in row-major order\n  pnCb      - Pointer to 32 signed 16-bit Cb (blue chrominance) samples (4 per row)\n  pnCr      - Pointer to 32 signed 16-bit Cr (red chrominance) samples (4 per row)\n  pbRgbOut  - Output buffer for RGB data (8*nRowStride bytes minimum)\n  nRowStride - Byte stride between output rows (typically 24 for packed RGB)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x167 (359/256 = 1.402) - Cr to R coefficient\n  0xB7  (183/256 = 0.715) - Cr to G coefficient (negated in formula)\n  0x58  (88/256 = 0.344)  - Cb to G coefficient (negated in formula)\n  0x1C6 (454/256 = 1.773) - Cb to B coefficient\n  0xB2F5 (45813)          - Red offset constant = 179 * 256 (level shift)\n  0x87F6 (34806)          - Green offset constant (combined shift)\n  0xE251 (57937)          - Blue offset constant = 226 * 256 (level shift)\n\nNotes:\n  - Input Y/Cb/Cr are typically post-IDCT values centered around 0 or 128\n  - Output RGB bytes are clamped to [0, 255] range\n  - Chrominance is upsampled 2:1 horizontally (4 Cb/Cr pairs cover 8 Y samples)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
