      "name": "ConvertYCbCrToRgba32",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYCbCrToRgba32(short * param_1, short * param_2, short * param_3, undefined1 * param_4, int param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YCbCr color space data to RGBA32 pixel format with alpha set to 0xFF.\n\nProcesses an 8x8 block of pixels (2 rows at a time, 4 iterations) using fixed-point\nYCbCr to RGB conversion coefficients. Chroma components (Cb/Cr) are subsampled 2:1\nhorizontally, so each pair of Y values shares the same chroma.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. For each pair of rows (4 iterations total):\n   a. Calculate RGB offsets from Cr (red) and Cb (blue) chroma components\n   b. Red offset = Cr * 0x167 - 0xB2F5 >> 8 (approx 1.402 * Cr - 179)\n   c. Green offset = Cr * 0xB7 + Cb * 0x58 - 0x87F6 >> 8 (approx -0.714 * Cr - 0.344 * Cb)\n   d. Blue offset = Cb * 0x1C6 - 0xE251 >> 8 (approx 1.772 * Cb - 226)\n2. For each Y sample in the row:\n   a. R = clamp(Y + RedOffset, 0, 255)\n   b. G = clamp(Y - GreenOffset, 0, 255)\n   c. B = clamp(Y + BlueOffset, 0, 255)\n   d. A = 0xFF (fully opaque)\n3. Write RGBA pixel to output, advance by stride for next row\n\nParameters:\n- pnYLuma: Array of 128 signed 16-bit Y (luma) values for 8x16 block\n- pnCbBlue: Array of 32 signed 16-bit Cb (blue chroma) values, 2:1 subsampled\n- pnCrRed: Array of 32 signed 16-bit Cr (red chroma) values, 2:1 subsampled\n- pbRgbaOut: Output buffer for RGBA32 pixels (4 bytes per pixel)\n- nStride: Bytes per output row (for advancing to next scanline)\n\nReturns:\n- void: Function modifies pbRgbaOut buffer in-place\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x167 (359): Fixed-point 1.402 for Cr to R conversion\n- 0xB7 (183): Fixed-point 0.714 for Cr to G conversion\n- 0x58 (88): Fixed-point 0.344 for Cb to G conversion\n- 0x1C6 (454): Fixed-point 1.772 for Cb to B conversion\n- 0xB2F5 (45813): Offset for R channel centering\n- 0x87F6 (34806): Offset for G channel centering\n- 0xE251 (57937): Offset for B channel centering\n- >> 8: Fixed-point scaling (divide by 256)\n\nOutput Layout:\n- Each iteration writes 32 bytes (8 RGBA pixels) to current row\n- Then writes 32 bytes to next row (at pbRgbaOut + nStride)\n- Processes 2 rows per iteration, 4 iterations = 8 rows total",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
