      "name": "ConvertYCbCrToInvertedRgba",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYCbCrToInvertedRgba(short * param_1, short * param_2, short * param_3, char * param_4, char * param_5, int param_6)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YCbCr color space to inverted RGBA (CMYK-like output format).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Pre-compute chroma-to-RGB conversion factors for 4 Cr/Cb sample pairs per iteration\n2. For each of 4 iterations (8 rows total, processing 2 rows per iteration):\n   a. Read 16 Y samples (8 per row, indices 0-7 and 8-15)\n   b. Apply YCbCr-to-RGB matrix transformation using fixed-point coefficients:\n      - Red = Y + Cr*0x167 - 0xB2F5 (after >>8)\n      - Green = Y - (Cr*0xB7 + Cb*0x58 - 0x87F6) (after >>8)\n      - Blue = Y + Cb*0x1C6 - 0xE251 (after >>8)\n   c. Clamp each RGB channel to [0, 255] range\n   d. Invert output: byte_out = 255 - clamped_value (for CMYK-style printing)\n   e. Copy alpha channel directly from input (stride 2 samples)\n   f. Write 8 RGBA pixels per row (32 bytes), advance output by stride\n3. Advance input pointers: Y by 16, Cb/Cr by 8, Alpha by 32\n\nParameters:\n  pnYSamples - Luminance samples (16-bit signed, 128 total: 16 per iteration * 8 rows)\n  pnCbSamples - Blue-difference chroma samples (16-bit signed, 32 total: 4 per iteration * 8 rows)\n  pnCrSamples - Red-difference chroma samples (16-bit signed, 32 total: 4 per iteration * 8 rows)\n  pbAlphaChannel - Alpha channel values (8-bit, stride 2 between samples, 32 bytes per 2 rows)\n  pbOutputRgba - Output buffer for inverted RGBA pixels (32 bytes per row)\n  nOutputStride - Bytes between output rows (allows for padding/alignment)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Writes 8x8 block (256 RGBA pixels, 2048 bytes at 32 bytes/row * 8 rows stride) to pbOutputRgba\n\nColor Space Coefficients (Fixed-Point 8.8 format):\n  Red:   Cr * 0x167 (1.402) with bias offset -0xB2F5 (-178.96)\n  Green: Cr * 0xB7 (0.714) + Cb * 0x58 (0.344) with bias offset -0x87F6 (-135.96)\n  Blue:  Cb * 0x1C6 (1.772) with bias offset -0xE251 (-226.32)\n\nOutput Inversion:\n  Each RGB component is inverted (255 - value) for CMYK-compatible output.\n  This is typical for print-oriented image processing where 0=white, 255=black.",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
