      "name": "ConvertRgbBlockToRgba",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertRgbBlockToRgba(int param_1, undefined1 * param_2, int param_3, int param_4, int param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts an 8x8 block of planar RGB pixel data to interleaved RGBA format.\n\nCopies pixel data from three separate color channel planes (Red, Green, Blue)\ninto a packed RGBA destination buffer, setting alpha to 0xFF (fully opaque).\nThe source channels are accessed via offsets from a base pixel pointer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize destination row pointer to nBlueOffset + 1 (start of dest buffer)\n2. For each of 8 rows:\n   a. Reset column counter to 8\n   b. For each of 8 columns:\n      - Copy Red channel byte to dest[0] (offset by nBlueOffset - destRow)\n      - Copy Green channel byte to dest[1] (direct from source)\n      - Copy Blue channel byte to dest[2] (offset by nGreenOffset)\n      - Set Alpha byte to 0xFF\n      - Advance source by 2 bytes, dest by 4 bytes\n   c. Advance destination row by nDestPitch\n\nParameters:\n  nRedOffset - Byte offset from pbSrcPixels to red channel data\n  pbSrcPixels - Base pointer to source pixel data (green channel)\n  nGreenOffset - Byte offset from pbSrcPixels to green/blue channel data\n  nBlueOffset - Starting address of destination RGBA buffer (minus 1)\n  nDestPitch - Bytes per row in destination buffer (stride)\n\nReturns: void\n\nDecompiler Variables:\n  puVar1 (pbDestPixel) - Current destination pixel pointer (inner loop)\n  puVar2 (pbDestRow) - Destination row start pointer (outer loop)\n  puVar3 (pbSrcPixel) - Current source pixel pointer\n  nRowCounter - Outer loop counter (8 rows)\n  nColCounter - Inner loop counter (8 pixels per row)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  8 - Block dimension (8x8 pixel tile)\n  0xFF - Alpha channel value (fully opaque)\n  2 - Source pixel stride (planar format)\n  4 - Destination pixel stride (RGBA packed format)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
