      "name": "CopyInterleavedPixelRect",
      "signature": "undefined CopyInterleavedPixelRect(int param_1, int param_2, int param_3, int param_4, int param_5, int * param_6, int param_7)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Copies pixel data from 4 separate source planes into an interleaved destination buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate starting destination row using Y bounds and destination stride\n2. Iterate over rows from pnBounds[1] (startY) to pnBounds[3] (endY)\n3. For each row, iterate over columns from pnBounds[0] (startX) to pnBounds[2] (endX)\n4. Copy 4 bytes per pixel: one from each source plane to consecutive dest bytes\n5. Source planes use 16-byte row stride (8 elements * 2 bytes), 2-byte column stride\n6. Destination uses 4-byte pixel stride (interleaved RGBA or similar)\n\nParameters:\n  pbSrcPlane0 - Source plane 0 (e.g., Red channel), 2-byte element stride\n  pbSrcPlane1 - Source plane 1 (e.g., Green channel), base for offset calculation\n  pbSrcPlane2 - Source plane 2 (e.g., Blue channel)\n  pbSrcPlane3 - Source plane 3 (e.g., Alpha channel)\n  pbDest      - Destination buffer for interleaved pixel data\n  pnBounds    - Rectangle bounds: [0]=startX, [1]=startY, [2]=endX, [3]=endY\n  nDestStride - Bytes per row in destination buffer\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nStructure Layout (pnBounds):\n  Offset  Size  Field    Description\n  0x00    4     startX   First column to copy (inclusive)\n  0x04    4     startY   First row to copy (inclusive)\n  0x08    4     endX     Last column to copy (exclusive)\n  0x0C    4     endY     Last row to copy (exclusive)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
