      "name": "CopyInterleavedBlock8x8",
      "signature": "undefined CopyInterleavedBlock8x8(int param_1, undefined1 * param_2, int param_3, int param_4, int param_5, int param_6)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Copies an 8x8 block from 4 interleaved source planes to a destination buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize destination row pointer to nDstBase + 1\n2. Outer loop: iterate 8 rows\n   a. Inner loop: iterate 8 columns (2 source bytes per iteration)\n      - Copy byte from plane 0 (nSrcPlane0 offset) to dst[0]\n      - Copy byte from plane 1 (pbSrcPlane1) to dst[1]  \n      - Copy byte from plane 2 (nSrcPlane2 offset) to dst[2]\n      - Copy byte from plane 3 (nSrcPlane3 offset) to dst[3]\n      - Advance source by 2, destination by 4\n   b. Advance destination row by nDstStride\n3. Return after processing 64 source bytes (8x8) into 256 destination bytes\n\nParameters:\n- nSrcPlane0: Base address offset for source plane 0\n- pbSrcPlane1: Pointer to source plane 1 data (base for relative offsets)\n- nSrcPlane2: Base address offset for source plane 2\n- nSrcPlane3: Base address offset for source plane 3\n- nDstBase: Base address of destination buffer\n- nDstStride: Row stride in destination buffer (bytes per row)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Source planes are at fixed 0x80 byte intervals (128 bytes apart)\n- Each source byte from 4 planes produces 4 consecutive destination bytes\n- Total: 8 rows x 8 cols x 2 src bytes = 128 bytes read from each plane\n- Output: 8 rows x 32 bytes per row = 256 bytes written\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 8: Block dimension (8x8 block processing)\n- 4: Destination stride per source pair (4 bytes output per iteration)\n- 2: Source advancement per iteration (processes 2 bytes per plane)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:9ee4211c395a4c8340c59fb82933e137cb2638529a49d545a99422fdc6b4c65e",
