      "name": "ConvertRgbBlockToYCbCrMMX",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertRgbBlockToYCbCrMMX(undefined8 * param_1, undefined8 * param_2, undefined4 param_3, undefined8 * param_4, int param_5, int param_6)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts an 8x8 RGB pixel block to YCbCr 4:2:0 color space using MMX SIMD instructions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop counters: outer loop runs 4 times (row pairs), inner loops 8 times (pixels)\n2. For each of 8 pixel pairs in current row:\n   a. Load 8 bytes (2 RGBA pixels) from source into MM0\n   b. Extract alpha channel: mask with 0xFF000000, shift right 24, saturate subtract threshold\n   c. Compute inverse RGB: subtract from saturation constant (0xFFFFFFFF) for color inversion\n   d. Unpack low/high bytes to words for 16-bit arithmetic (PUNPCKLBW/PUNPCKHBW with MM7=0)\n   e. Multiply-add with Y coefficients: R*77 + G*150 + B*29 (BT.601 scaled by 256)\n   f. Sum horizontal pairs, subtract bias (128<<8=32768), shift right 8 for Y output\n   g. Multiply-add with Cb coefficients: -43*R - 85*G + 128*B\n   h. Multiply-add with Cr coefficients: 128*R - 107*G - 21*B\n   i. Accumulate Cb and Cr for 4:2:0 subsampling (average of 2x2 block)\n3. Process second row with stride offset (for 4:2:0 vertical subsampling)\n4. Store Y values directly to output (8 values per row, 2 rows = 16 Y per pass)\n5. Pack and store Cb/Cr with rounding (+512), shift right 10 (divide by 1024 = scale + avg 4)\n6. Store alpha values to separate output buffer (no subsampling, full resolution)\n7. Advance pointers by stride*2 for next 2-row pair, repeat 4 times for 8 rows total\n\nParameters:\n  pqwYOutput     - Destination buffer for Y (luma) values, 64 shorts per 8x8 block\n  pqwCbOutput    - Destination buffer for Cb (blue chroma) values, 16 shorts (4:2:0 subsampled)\n  pdwAlphaOutput - Destination buffer for extracted alpha channel values (full resolution)\n  pqwCrOutput    - Destination buffer for Cr (red chroma) values, 16 shorts (4:2:0 subsampled)\n  pbRgbSource    - Source RGBA pixel data, 8 bytes per 2 pixels (32-bit RGBA format)\n  nRowStride     - Byte offset between source image rows\n\nReturns:\n  void - Outputs written directly to destination buffers\n\nCoefficient Tables (BT.601/CCIR-601 standard, Q8 fixed-point):\n  Y  = (77*R + 150*G + 29*B) >> 8        = 0.299*R + 0.587*G + 0.114*B\n  Cb = (-43*R - 85*G + 128*B) >> 10 + 128 = -0.169*R - 0.331*G + 0.500*B + 128\n  Cr = (128*R - 107*G - 21*B) >> 10 + 128 =  0.500*R - 0.419*G - 0.081*B + 128\n\nGlobal Constants:\n  g_qwYCoeffRgb      (0x600252e8) - Y luma coefficients packed for PMADDWD\n  g_qwCbCoeffRgb     (0x600252f0) - Cb blue chroma coefficients\n  g_qwCrCoeffRgb     (0x600252f8) - Cr red chroma coefficients\n  g_qwYBiasOffset    (0x60025300) - Y bias (32768 = 128<<8) for rounding\n  g_qwChromaRounding (0x60025308) - Chroma rounding constant (512)\n  g_qwAlphaThreshold (0x60025310) - Alpha saturation threshold\n  g_qwAlphaSaturation(0x60025318) - Alpha saturation value (0xFFFFFFFF)\n  g_qwAlphaChannelMask(0x60025320) - Alpha channel mask (0xFF000000FF000000)\n\nOutput Layout:\n  Y buffer:  [Y00-Y07] [Y10-Y17] ... [Y70-Y77] (64 values, sequential 8x8 block)\n  Cb buffer: [Cb00 Cb02 Cb04 Cb06] [Cb20...] [Cb40...] [Cb60...] (16 values, 4x4 subsampled)\n  Cr buffer: Same layout as Cb (4:2:0 subsampling averages 2x2 pixel groups)\n  Alpha:     Full resolution, same layout as Y\n\nStack Frame Layout (256 bytes, -0x100 to -0x08):\n  Offset      Size  Description\n  -0x104      64    qwY0-qwY7: Y luma accumulator array (8 qwords)\n  -0xC4       64    qwCbAccum0-7: Cb chroma accumulator array\n  -0x84       64    qwCrAccum0-7: Cr chroma accumulator array\n  -0x44       64    qwAlpha0-7: Alpha channel values array\n\nDecompiler Limitations (HASH-based virtual variables):\n  qwMmxResult - Virtual variable for chroma rounding constant (g_qwChromaRounding).\n                Ghidra creates this as a HASH-based temporary that regenerates with\n                undefined8 type on each decompilation. Type is ulonglong (64-bit MMX).",
