      "name": "DownscaleBilinear8x8BlockMMX",
      "signature": "undefined DownscaleBilinear8x8BlockMMX(undefined8 * param_1, undefined8 * param_2, undefined8 * param_3, undefined4 param_4, int param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Performs bilinear downscaling on an 8x8 pixel block using MMX SIMD instructions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop counter (ECX=3) for processing 3 row pairs\n2. Load bilinear interpolation coefficients from g_qwBilinearCoeffBase\n3. For each row pair:\n   a. Load 8 source pixels (24 bytes per row: 3x MOVQ from ESI, ESI+8, ESI+10)\n   b. Unpack bytes to words using PUNPCKLBW for 16-bit precision\n   c. Apply horizontal weighted interpolation via PMADDWD with coefficients\n   d. Accumulate results in stack variables qwAccum0-3 for vertical pass\n   e. Pack results back to bytes using PACKSSDW\n   f. Toggle inner loop flag (XOR EDX,1) for alternating passes\n4. After 3 iterations, perform final vertical interpolation pass\n5. Apply rounding bias (g_qwBilinearRounding) and channel mask (g_qwChannelMask)\n6. Store horizontal results to pDstInterpH (EDI)\n7. Store combined H+V results to pDstInterpHV (EBX) at offset +0x80\n\nParameters:\n  pSrcPixels   [EBP+0x08] - Source pixel buffer (24 bytes per row, 8 pixels packed)\n  pDstInterpH  [EBP+0x0C] - Destination for horizontal interpolation results (16 bytes)\n  pDstInterpHV [EBP+0x10] - Destination for horizontal+vertical interp results\n  dwSrcStride  [EBP+0x14] - Source buffer stride (unused in current impl)\n  nSrcPitch    [EBP+0x18] - Source row pitch in bytes (typically 24)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Results written directly to destination buffers\n\nStack Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Variable     Description\n  -0x08   8     qwAccum0     Vertical accumulator for pixels 0-1\n  -0x10   8     qwAccum1     Vertical accumulator for pixels 2-3\n  -0x18   8     qwAccum2     Vertical accumulator for pixels 4-5\n  -0x20   8     qwAccum3     Vertical accumulator for pixels 6-7\n\nGlobal Constants Used:\n  0x60025328 g_qwBilinearCoeffBase   - Base interpolation weights [0x4D,0x96,0x1D,0x00]\n  0x60025330 g_qwBilinearPackCoeff0  - Packing coefficients for vertical pass\n  0x60025338 g_qwBilinearPackCoeff1  - Secondary packing coefficients\n  0x60025358 g_qwBilinearBias        - Bias subtraction for rounding (0x7F80)\n  0x60025360 g_qwBilinearRounding    - Rounding constant for final scaling\n  0x60025368 g_qwPackedByteConst     - Zero constant for PUNPCKLBW\n  0x60025370 g_qwChannelMask         - Channel isolation mask (0x00FF00FF)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x18 (24)  - Right shift for extracting pixel bytes 3-4\n  0x30 (48)  - Right shift for extracting pixel bytes 6-7\n  0x08       - Scale factor shift for 8-bit precision\n  0x0A (10)  - Final scale shift for vertical pass\n  0x10 (16)  - Left shift for channel packing\n  0x80 (128) - Offset between H and HV result buffers\n\nRegister Usage:\n  ESI - Source pointer (advances by nSrcPitch each row)\n  EDI - Horizontal destination pointer (advances by 16)\n  EBX - H+V destination pointer (advances by 16)\n  ECX - Row loop counter (3 to 0)\n  EDX - Toggle flag for inner loop alternation\n  EAX - nSrcPitch parameter\n  MM0-MM7 - SIMD computation registers\n\nPerformance Notes:\n  - Uses MMX for parallel 8-bit to 16-bit conversion\n  - PMADDWD provides efficient weighted sum of adjacent pixels\n  - Unrolled inner loop reduces branch overhead\n  - Stack accumulators enable multi-row vertical filtering",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
