      "name": "DownscaleBilinear4x4BlockMMX",
      "signature": "undefined DownscaleBilinear4x4BlockMMX(undefined8 * param_1, undefined8 * param_2, undefined8 * param_3, undefined4 param_4, int param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Performs MMX-accelerated bilinear downscaling of a 4x4 pixel block to 2x2.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 4 row accumulators (qwAccumRow0-3) to zero\n2. Load 24 bytes (3 qwords) of source pixels per row\n3. Unpack 8-bit pixels to 16-bit words using PUNPCKLBW\n4. Apply horizontal bilinear coefficients via PMADDWD multiply-accumulate\n5. Subtract bias constant and normalize (>>8) for intermediate precision\n6. Pack results back to 16-bit words with PACKSSDW\n7. Accumulate weighted sums for 3 row pairs (main loop counter=3)\n8. Toggle between odd/even row processing (XOR EDX, 1)\n9. Apply Y-direction coefficients (Y0 and Y1 sets) for vertical averaging\n10. Add rounding constant and final normalize (>>10)\n11. Mask to 8-bit per channel (AND with 0x00FF00FF pattern)\n12. Store results: row A at pqwDstRowA, row B at +0x80 offset\n\nParameters:\n  pqwSrcPixels - Source pixel buffer (24 bytes per row, 4 rows accessed)\n  pqwDstRowA - First destination row output buffer\n  pqwDstRowB - Second destination row output buffer (written at +0x80)\n  dwUnused - Reserved parameter (not used in current implementation)\n  nSrcStride - Byte stride between consecutive source rows\n\nReturns:\n  void - Results written directly to destination buffers\n\nMMX Register Usage:\n  MM0-MM5: Working registers for pixel processing\n  MM6: Zero register for PUNPCKLBW zero-extension\n  MM7: Holds coefficient constants during processing\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  3 (0x3) - Main loop iteration count (3 row pairs)\n  0x80 (128) - Offset between destination row pairs (16 qwords)\n  >>8 (0x8) - Intermediate normalization shift\n  >>10 (0xa) - Final normalization shift for 10-bit precision\n  0x18, 0x30, 0x38 - Bit shift offsets for pixel extraction\n  0x00FF00FF - Channel mask pattern for 8-bit extraction\n\nCoefficient Constants (loaded from data section):\n  g_qwBilinearCoeffX (0x60025340) - Horizontal interpolation weights\n  g_qwBilinearCoeffY0 (0x60025348) - Vertical coefficient set 0\n  g_qwBilinearCoeffY1 (0x60025350) - Vertical coefficient set 1\n  g_qwBilinearBias (0x60025358) - Bias subtraction constant\n  g_qwBilinearRounding (0x60025360) - Rounding addition constant\n  g_qwChannelMask (0x60025370) - 8-bit channel extraction mask\n\nDecompiler Notes:\n  SSA temporaries (uVar1-4) are regenerated during decompilation of complex\n  CONCAT operations for MMX byte manipulation. These intermediates represent\n  packed pixel data during unpacking and repacking operations.\n\nPerformance Notes:\n  - Uses MMX SIMD for parallel 8-pixel processing\n  - Avoids memory stalls via register-based accumulation\n  - Bilinear filter produces smooth 2:1 downscale",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
