      "name": "ConvertRgbBlockToYCbCr",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertRgbBlockToYCbCr(int param_1, int param_2, int param_3, int param_4, int param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts an RGB image block to YCbCr color space with 4:2:0 chroma subsampling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. For each row (up to nHeight):\n   a. Convert RGB triplets to YCbCr using ITU-R BT.601 coefficients\n   b. Y  = (0.299*R + 0.587*G + 0.114*B) - 128\n   c. Cb = 128 + (-0.169*R - 0.331*G + 0.500*B)\n   d. Cr = 128 + (0.500*R - 0.419*G - 0.081*B)\n   e. If width < 16, pad with edge replication\n2. If height < 16, replicate last row to fill 16x16 block\n3. Subsample Cb and Cr planes by 2x2 averaging (4:2:0)\n4. Store output: Y(8x8), Y(8x8), Y(8x8), Y(8x8), Cb(8x8), Cr(8x8)\n\nParameters:\n  pbSrcRgb    - Source RGB pixel data (BGR byte order, 3 bytes/pixel)\n  psDstYCbCr  - Destination buffer for YCbCr MCU block (384 shorts: 4*64 Y + 64 Cb + 64 Cr)\n  nWidth      - Source image width in pixels (1-16)\n  nHeight     - Source image height in pixels (1-16)\n  nSrcStride  - Source row stride in bytes\n\nReturns: void\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x96 (150) = 0.587 * 256 (G coefficient for Y)\n  0x4d (77)  = 0.299 * 256 (R coefficient for Y)\n  0x1d (29)  = 0.114 * 256 (B coefficient for Y)\n  0x55 (85)  = 0.331 * 256 (G coefficient for Cb)\n  0x2b (43)  = 0.169 * 256 (R coefficient for Cb)\n  0x6b (107) = 0.419 * 256 (G coefficient for Cr)\n  0x15 (21)  = 0.081 * 256 (B coefficient for Cr)\n  0x7f80     = 128 * 256 (level shift for signed YCbCr)\n\nStructure Layout (local buffers):\n  Offset  Size   Field       Description\n  0x030   0x010  asYPlane    Y plane 16x16 shorts (row 0-7)\n  0x230   0x200  asCbPlane   Cb plane 16x16 shorts\n  0x430   0x200  asCrPlane   Cr plane 16x16 shorts",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:6b5c5ac92c1c0942e853340e5fba48a93dfcdb01bba583d403086ca2b341e4d1",
