      "name": "ConvertRgbBlockToYCbCr420",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertRgbBlockToYCbCr420(undefined2 * param_1, undefined2 * param_2, undefined2 * param_3, byte * param_4, int param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts an 8x8 block of RGB pixels to YCbCr 4:2:0 format for JPEG encoding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Process 4 row pairs (8 rows total) in outer loop (nRowCounter = 4 iterations)\n2. For each row pair, compute 8 Y (luma) samples from row 0 using BT.601 formula:\n   Y = (R*0x4d + G*0x96 + B*0x1d - 0x7f80) >> 8\n3. Compute 8 Y samples from row 1 using same formula\n4. For Cb/Cr, downsample 2x2 pixel blocks by averaging RGB components from both rows\n5. Compute Cb = ((B_avg + 4)*0x80 - G_avg*0x55 - R_avg*0x2b) >> 10\n6. Compute Cr = ((R_avg + 4)*0x80 - G_avg*0x6b - B_avg*0x15) >> 10\n7. Advance Y output by 16 shorts, Cb/Cr by 8 shorts each iteration\n\nParameters:\n  pnYOutput - Output buffer for 64 signed 16-bit Y samples (8x8 block)\n  pnCbOutput - Output buffer for 16 signed 16-bit Cb samples (4x4 block after 2x2 subsampling)\n  pnCrOutput - Output buffer for 16 signed 16-bit Cr samples (4x4 block after 2x2 subsampling)\n  pbRgbInput - Input RGB data, 24 bytes per pixel triplet, 8 pixels per row\n  nRgbStride - Bytes between consecutive rows in input buffer\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x4d (77)  - R coefficient for Y = 0.299 * 256 (BT.601)\n  0x96 (150) - G coefficient for Y = 0.587 * 256 (BT.601)\n  0x1d (29)  - B coefficient for Y = 0.114 * 256 (BT.601)\n  0x7f80     - Bias offset (128 << 8) to center Y around 0\n  0x80 (128) - Scale factor for chroma calculation\n  0x55 (85)  - G coefficient for Cb = 0.331 * 256\n  0x2b (43)  - R coefficient for Cb = 0.169 * 256\n  0x6b (107) - G coefficient for Cr = 0.419 * 256\n  0x15 (21)  - B coefficient for Cr = 0.081 * 256\n\nNotes:\n  - Part of JPEG MCU (Minimum Coded Unit) processing pipeline\n  - Called 4 times per 16x16 MCU to process four 8x8 Y blocks\n  - Chroma is subsampled 4:2:0 (2x horizontal, 2x vertical)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
