      "name": "ConvertRgbToYCbCrBlocks",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertRgbToYCbCrBlocks(int param_1, int param_2, int param_3, int param_4, int param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts RGB pixel data to YCbCr color space for JPEG encoding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Iterate over MCU rows (16 pixels high each)\n2. For each row, iterate over MCU columns (16 pixels wide)\n3. Convert RGB triplets to YCbCr using ITU-R BT.601 coefficients:\n   Y  = 0.299*R + 0.587*G + 0.114*B\n   Cb = -0.169*R - 0.331*G + 0.500*B + 128\n   Cr = 0.500*R - 0.419*G - 0.081*B + 128\n4. Store Y, Cb, Cr components in separate 16x16 short arrays\n5. Pad incomplete rows/columns to 16-pixel boundary\n6. Perform 4:2:0 chroma subsampling by averaging 2x2 Cb/Cr blocks\n\nParameters:\n  nRowCount (param_1): Number of valid pixel rows to process\n  pbRgbSource (param_2): Pointer to source RGB pixel data (3 bytes per pixel)\n  nWidth (param_3): Width of source image in pixels (stride = nWidth * 3)\n  nMcuHeight (param_4): Height of current MCU block (usually 16)\n  pnYCbCrDest (param_5): Destination buffer for YCbCr component data\n\nReturns:\n  void - Results written to pnYCbCrDest buffer\n\nStack Layout (0x620 bytes):\n  Offset    Size    Description\n  0x030     0x200   Y component buffer (16x16 shorts)\n  0x230     0x200   Cb component buffer (16x16 shorts)\n  0x430     0x200   Cr component buffer (16x16 shorts)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xffff8080 (-32640): Bias for Y calculation (128*256)\n  0x10: MCU block dimension (16 pixels)\n  0x20: Row stride in short array (16 * 2 bytes)\n  0x200: Component buffer size (16*16*2 bytes)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:d2e5cfce77063738db5087aa3c39b24c79283a62ef67f04c75ec1b6d972d760a",
