      "name": "ConvertYCbCrComponentsToChroma",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYCbCrComponentsToChroma(undefined2 * param_1, undefined2 * param_2, undefined2 * param_3, byte * param_4, int param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YCbCr sample triplets to chroma-downsampled output components.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop counter to 8 iterations (processes 8 rows)\n2. For each iteration, read 24 bytes (8 triplets of 3 bytes each) from input\n3. Convert each triplet using fixed-point ITU-R BT.601 coefficients:\n   - Multiply byte values by scaling factors using LEA chains\n   - Apply centering offset (-0x7f80 = -32640)\n   - Right-shift by 8 for fixed-point to integer conversion\n4. Write Y component to pnYOutput (8 values per row)\n5. Compute Cb chroma using horizontal pair sums with coefficients\n6. Compute Cr chroma using horizontal pair sums with coefficients\n7. Advance input pointer by nInputStride bytes\n8. Advance output pointers by 16 bytes (8 shorts)\n9. Decrement loop counter and repeat until zero\n\nParameters:\n  pnYOutput - Output buffer for Y (luma) component samples (short array)\n  pnCbOutput - Output buffer for Cb (blue chroma) component samples\n  pnCrOutput - Output buffer for Cr (red chroma) component samples\n  pbInputSamples - Input buffer with interleaved YCbCr byte triplets\n  nInputStride - Byte stride between input rows\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x8 - Loop count (8 rows processed)\n  0xffff8080 (-0x7f80) - Fixed-point centering offset (127.5 * 256)\n  SAR 8 - Divide by 256 for fixed-point to integer conversion\n  LEA x*8-x = x*7 (coefficient multiplier)\n  LEA x+x*4 = x*5 (coefficient multiplier)\n  LEA x+x*4+x*4+x*2 = x*25 (coefficient multiplier)\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field       Type    Description\n  +0x0    8     Y values    short   8 luma samples per row\n  +0x2    8     Cb values   short   4 chroma blue samples (2:1 subsample)\n  +0x4    8     Cr values   short   4 chroma red samples (2:1 subsample)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
