      "comment": "Converts an 8x8 block of RGB pixels to YCbCr color space for JPEG/MPEG encoding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize row counter to 8 (processes 8 rows)\n2. For each row, process 8 pixels (24 bytes RGB data):\n   a. Compute 8 Y (luminance) values using: Y = 0.114*B + 0.587*G + 0.299*R\n      Uses fixed-point: Y = (0x1d*R + 0x96*G + 0x4d*B - 0x7f80) >> 8\n   b. Compute 4 Cb (blue chroma) values with 2:1 horizontal subsampling\n      Cb = 128 + 0.5*(B-Y) approximated with integer math\n   c. Compute 4 Cr (red chroma) values with 2:1 horizontal subsampling\n      Cr = 128 + 0.5*(R-Y) approximated with integer math\n3. Advance output pointers by 8 shorts (16 bytes), input by stride\n4. Repeat until all 8 rows processed\n\nParameters:\n  pnYOut - Output buffer for 64 luminance values (8x8 block, 128 bytes)\n  pnCbOut - Output buffer for 32 Cb chrominance values (4x8 subsampled, 64 bytes)\n  pnCrOut - Output buffer for 32 Cr chrominance values (4x8 subsampled, 64 bytes)\n  pbRgbData - Input RGB pixel data (24 bytes per row = 8 pixels x 3 bytes)\n  nStride - Bytes to advance per row in source image (typically image_width * 3)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Results written to output buffers\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1d (29) - Fixed-point coefficient for Blue: 0.114 * 256 = 29.2\n  0x96 (150) - Fixed-point coefficient for Green: 0.587 * 256 = 150.3\n  0x4d (77) - Fixed-point coefficient for Red: 0.299 * 256 = 76.5\n  0x7f80 (32640) - Offset for signed conversion: 127.5 * 256\n  0x80 (128) - Chrominance calculation multiplier\n  0x55 (85) - Cb formula coefficient\n  0x2b (43) - Cb formula coefficient\n  0x6b (107) - Cr formula coefficient\n  0x15 (21) - Cr formula coefficient\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Assumes valid, aligned input buffers\n  - Output is 16-bit signed shorts in range [-128, 127] shifted\n  - 4:2:2 chroma subsampling (2:1 horizontal)",
