      "name": "ConvertYCbCrToRgbBlock",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYCbCrToRgbBlock(undefined2 * param_1, undefined2 * param_2, undefined2 * param_3, short * param_4, byte * param_5, int param_6)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YCbCr color data to RGB using fixed-point arithmetic for JPEG decoding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop counter to 4 (processes 4 blocks per call)\n2. For each iteration, read 32 bytes of interleaved YCbCr data\n3. Extract Y (luminance) samples at byte offsets 0,1,2,4,5,6,8,9,10,12,13,14,16,17,18,20,21,22,24,25,26,28,29,30\n4. Extract Cb/Cr (chroma) samples at byte offsets 3,7,11,15,19,23,27,31\n5. Apply inverse transform: RGB = Y + weighted(Cb) + weighted(Cr)\n6. Store converted RGB values as 16-bit shorts to output arrays\n7. Store centered chroma values (byte - 0x80) to chroma output\n8. Advance input pointer by stride, output pointers by 16 bytes\n9. Decrement counter and repeat until zero\n\nParameters:\n    pnRedOut    - Output array for red channel (16-bit signed)\n    pnGreenOut  - Output array for green channel (16-bit signed)\n    pnBlueOut   - Output array for blue channel (16-bit signed)\n    pnChromaOut - Output array for chroma residual (16-bit signed)\n    pbYCbCrIn   - Input packed YCbCr byte data (32 bytes per block)\n    nStride     - Bytes between successive input blocks\n\nReturns:\n    void - Results written to output arrays\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n    0xFF     - Inversion mask for color component\n    0x80     - Chroma centering offset (shifts 0-255 to -128-127)\n    0xFFFF8080 - Fixed-point offset for RGB calculation\n    0x3FC    - Initial accumulator value (1020 = 4 * 255)\n    0x4      - Loop iterations (4 blocks)\n    0x10     - Output stride (16 bytes = 8 shorts per block)\n\nFixed-Point Coefficients (via LEA sequences):\n    Y coefficient:  ~19 (x + x*8 + x*2) = 19x for luminance scaling\n    Cb coefficient: ~29 (x*8 - x) * 4 = 28x for blue difference\n    Cr coefficient: ~150 (x + x*2)(x + x*4)(x + x*4)*2 for red difference\n\nNote: This function is called 4 times from the JPEG decoder at different \n      block positions to process complete MCU (Minimum Coded Unit).",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:805f0091fb9195a8b47a0ab8adbcdc04baa4df72f3010b66ab82c9ffc8eae00f",
