      "name": "NormalizeQuantizationTable",
      "signature": "undefined NormalizeQuantizationTable(undefined2 * param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Normalizes a 64-element JPEG quantization table using DCT normalization coefficients.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Enforce minimum quality factor of 2 at element 63 (index 0x3F)\n2. Loop through all 64 elements of the quantization table\n3. For each element: normalize = (value / dctCoeff[i]) * 32768.0 + 0.5\n4. Convert floating-point result to integer via __ftol\n5. Store normalized value back to the quantization table\n\nParameters:\n  pnQuantTable - Pointer to 64-element short array (quantization table)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Table is modified in-place\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x40 (64) - DCT block size (8x8 = 64 elements)\n  0x3F (63) - Last element index, used for quality floor\n  2 - Minimum quality factor to prevent divide-by-zero\n  32768.0 (0x40E0...) - Fixed-point scaling factor (2^15)\n  0.5 (0x3FE0...) - Rounding constant for float-to-int\n\nGlobal Data:\n  0x60025378 - g_adDctNormCoeffs: 64-element double array of DCT normalization coefficients\n  0x60025580 - g_dQuantScale: 32768.0 fixed-point multiplier\n  0x60025578 - g_dRoundingConst: 0.5 for rounding\n\nCalled By:\n  InitializeQuantizationAndHuffmanTables",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
