      "name": "ComputeDctCoefficientsZigzag",
      "signature": "undefined ComputeDctCoefficientsZigzag(undefined4 * param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Computes DCT coefficients and stores them in zigzag scan order.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize pointers to zigzag order table and DCT coefficient table\n2. Loop 64 times (8x8 block): multiply DCT coefficients, truncate to short, store at zigzag index\n3. Copy 128 bytes (64 shorts) from temporary buffer to output block\n4. Zero out the trailing 32 bytes (8 dwords / 16 shorts) for padding\n\nParameters:\n  pnOutputBlock (short*) - Output buffer for 80 shorts: 64 DCT coefficients + 16 zero padding\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nStructure Layout (Output Block):\n  Offset  Size  Field             Description\n  0x00    0x80  anCoefficients    64 DCT coefficients in zigzag order (short[64])\n  0x80    0x20  anPadding         16 zero-padded shorts (short[16])\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x60027354 - g_anZigzagOrder: JPEG zigzag scan order lookup table (int[64])\n  0x60025588 - g_adDctCoefficients: DCT normalization coefficients (double[64])\n  0x60025788 - Loop terminator (end of coefficient array)\n  0x60025580, 0x60025578 - Additional DCT scaling factors\n\nNotes:\n- Uses __ftol() for floating-point to integer conversion\n- JPEG zigzag ordering optimizes run-length encoding by grouping zeros\n- Total output size is 160 bytes (0xA0)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:514de2e3d89c303a65f920b6281692c4d216a6af33dc9bdac92d809284bed64c",
