      "name": "PerformInverseDiscreteCosineTransform8x8",
      "signature": "undefined PerformInverseDiscreteCosineTransform8x8(int param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Performs an 8x8 Inverse Discrete Cosine Transform (IDCT) for JPEG/MPEG decoding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Apply 1D column IDCT to 8 columns of the 8x8 DCT coefficient block\n2. Apply 1D row IDCT to 8 rows with level shift and clamping\n3. Each 1D transform uses butterfly stages with fixed-point cosine multipliers\n4. Output values are scaled, DC-shifted by +128, and clamped to [0,255]\n\nParameters:\n  pDctBlock - Pointer to 64-element short array (8x8 DCT coefficients)\n              Modified in-place: input coefficients replaced with pixel values\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nMagic Number Reference:\n  0x14e7b (85627) - cos(pi/16) * sqrt(2) * 32768, 1D stage rotation\n  0xb505  (46341) - sqrt(2) * 32768, even-odd butterfly rotation\n  0x8a8c  (35468) - cos(3*pi/16) * sqrt(2) * 32768, odd stage scaling\n  0x61f8  (25080) - (cos(pi/16) - cos(3*pi/16)) * sqrt(2) * 32768\n  0x4000  (16384) - Rounding constant for 15-bit right shift\n  0x80    (128)   - DC level shift for unsigned pixel output\n  0xff    (255)   - Maximum clamped pixel value\n\nStructure Layout (8x8 block addressing):\n  Offset    Size    Field           Description\n  0x00      16      Row 0           First row of 8 short coefficients\n  0x10      16      Row 1           Second row\n  0x20      16      Row 2           Third row\n  ...\n  0x70      16      Row 7           Last row\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Input values outside coefficient range produce clamped output\n  - All outputs guaranteed in range [0, 255]",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:4b4f707db58a67aeaa8ccdafaa59c4a6dbc7f6414b871e1c0253b2a48d1c63fb",
