      "name": "PerformIdctOnBlock",
      "signature": "undefined PerformIdctOnBlock(int param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Performs Inverse Discrete Cosine Transform (IDCT) on an 8x8 coefficient block for JPEG decoding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Column pass: Process 8 columns using 4-point IDCT butterfly operations (skips column 4 for DC optimization)\n2. Row pass: Process 4 rows using 4-point IDCT butterfly with scaling and rounding\n3. Level shift: Add 128 (0x80) DC offset and clamp output values to 0-255 range\n4. In-place transformation: Results overwrite the input coefficient block\n\nParameters:\n  psBlock - Pointer to 8x8 block of 16-bit DCT coefficients (64 shorts = 128 bytes)\n\nReturns: void (in-place transformation)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0xB505 - cos(pi/4) * 2^15 / sqrt(2) = 46341 (butterfly scaling factor)\n  0xEC84 - cos(3*pi/8) * 2^15 = 60548 (primary rotation coefficient)\n  0xEC83 - same coefficient, alternate representation\n  0x61F8 - sin(3*pi/8) * 2^15 = 25080 (complementary rotation)\n  0x4000 - Rounding bias (2^14 for 15-bit right shift)\n  0x80   - DC level shift (128) for unsigned output\n\nBlock Layout (16-bit coefficients, 2 bytes each):\n  Offset  Content\n  0x00    DC coefficient (column 0, row 0)\n  0x02    Row 0, columns 1-7\n  0x10    Row 1\n  ...\n  0x70    Row 7\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Column 4 is skipped in column pass (DC-only optimization)\n  - Output clamped to [0, 255] for 8-bit pixel range",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
