      "name": "PerformIdctColumnPassAndClamp",
      "signature": "undefined PerformIdctColumnPassAndClamp(short * param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Performs the final column pass of inverse DCT and clamps output values to valid 8-bit range.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Apply butterfly rotation using fixed-point DCT coefficients (0x8a8c, 0x14e7b)\n2. Process five coefficient pairs in the first stage (rows 0-4)\n3. Compute second-stage rotation on accumulated results\n4. Scale output values by right-shifting and adding DC offset (0x80)\n5. Clamp each result to [0, 255] for valid pixel values\n\nParameters:\n    pnDctCoeffs - Pointer to array of 64 short DCT coefficients (8x8 block)\n\nReturns:\n    void - Results stored in-place in coefficient array\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n    0x8a8c (35468) - Fixed-point representation of cos(3*pi/16) * sqrt(2)\n    0x14e7b (85627) - Fixed-point representation of sin(3*pi/16) * sqrt(2)\n    0x10000 - Rounding bias for 17-bit right shift\n    0x80 (128) - DC level shift to center output on [0, 255]\n    0xff (255) - Maximum valid pixel value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n    - Values below 1 are clamped to 0\n    - Values above 254 are clamped to 255",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:4fd8b04161e57da1d739baf14c156afcf0bac9800dddf413ffe91f95aec26e48",
