      "name": "PerformDCT8x8Transform",
      "signature": "undefined PerformDCT8x8Transform(undefined8 * param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Performs an in-place 8x8 2D Discrete Cosine Transform using MMX SIMD instructions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Transpose rows 4-7 of 8x8 matrix using PUNPCK word/dword interleave operations\n2. Transpose rows 0-3 of 8x8 matrix for column-major access\n3. Perform 1D DCT on columns via butterfly add/subtract operations\n4. Apply cosine coefficient rotations (W1, W2, W3, W4) using PMULHW\n5. Transpose result matrix for row-wise processing\n6. Perform 1D DCT on rows using same butterfly and rotation pattern\n7. Store final 2D DCT coefficients back to input buffer\n\nParameters:\n  pnCoefficients - short* - Pointer to 64-element array of signed 16-bit DCT\n                            coefficients (128 bytes, 8x8 matrix layout)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Coefficients are transformed in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Input buffer MUST be 8-byte aligned for MMX MOVQ operations\n  - Uses all 8 MMX registers (MM0-MM7) - no register sparing\n  - Caller MUST execute EMMS instruction after return before any FPU operations\n  - Fixed-point arithmetic uses Q15 format (15 fractional bits)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  - 0x5A80 (W1): cos(pi/4) * 32768 = 23168 (45-degree diagonal rotation)\n  - 0x6200 (W2): cos(pi/8) * 32768 = 25088 (22.5-degree coarse rotation)\n  - 0x4580 (W3): cos(3*pi/8) * 32768 = 17792 (67.5-degree fine rotation)\n  - 0x5380 (W4): Additional DCT scaling coefficient = 21376\n\nButterfly Operations:\n  - PADDW: Parallel add of 4 packed 16-bit words (even DCT terms)\n  - PSUBW: Parallel subtract of 4 packed 16-bit words (odd DCT terms)\n  - PSLLW: Left shift for precision before fixed-point multiply\n  - PMULHW: Packed multiply high word - extracts high 16 bits of 32-bit product\n\nGlobal Data Dependencies:\n  - g_qwDCT_CosCoeff_W1 @ 0x600257a0: cos(pi/4) coefficient qword\n  - g_qwDCT_CosCoeff_W2 @ 0x60025798: cos(pi/8) coefficient qword\n  - g_qwDCT_CosCoeff_W3 @ 0x60025790: cos(3pi/8) coefficient qword\n  - g_qwDCT_CosCoeff_W4 @ 0x600257a8: W4 scaling coefficient qword\n\nDecompiler Notes:\n  This function contains 700+ lines of heavily unrolled MMX SIMD code performing\n  matrix transpose and butterfly operations. The decompiler generates many SSA\n  temporary variables (uVar*, sVar*, qw*, dw*) representing intermediate packed\n  values. These are all ulonglong (64-bit qword for MMX) or uint (32-bit dword)\n  or short (16-bit word extracted from packed values). The variable naming\n  follows Hungarian notation: qw=quadword, dw=dword, n=short, prefix indicates\n  MMX register contents.",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
