      "name": "PerformIdctBlock8x8Mmx",
      "signature": "undefined PerformIdctBlock8x8Mmx(ulonglong * param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Performs an 8x8 Inverse Discrete Cosine Transform using MMX instructions.\n\nNOTE: This function operates entirely in MMX registers (MM0-MM7) with no stack locals.\nDecompiler-generated SSA variables (uVar*, sVar*) are register state representations\nthat cannot be renamed. See disassembly comments for detailed register tracking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load 8 rows of 16-bit DCT coefficients from the input block\n2. Perform 1D IDCT on columns using butterfly operations:\n   - Even coefficients: rows 0, 2, 4, 6 (DC and cosine terms)\n   - Odd coefficients: rows 1, 3, 5, 7 (sine terms)\n3. Apply cosine multiplication factors for frequency reconstruction\n4. Transpose the 8x8 matrix using PUNPCKL/PUNPCKH word/dword shuffles\n5. Perform 1D IDCT on rows (same butterfly algorithm)\n6. Final scaling: arithmetic right shift by 4 (divide by 16)\n7. Add 128 bias (DC level shift for unsigned output)\n8. Saturate and pack results to 16-bit signed values\n\nParameters:\n  pBlock (short*): Pointer to 64-element array of 16-bit DCT coefficients.\n                   Input: frequency-domain coefficients from quantization.\n                   Output: spatial-domain pixel values (overwritten in-place).\n\nReturns:\n  void - Results are written back to pBlock in-place.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Assumes valid 128-byte aligned block (8x8 * 16-bit = 128 bytes)\n  - Uses saturating arithmetic to prevent overflow\n  - EMMS instruction clears MMX state before return\n\nRegister Usage:\n  MM0-MM7: All used for intermediate IDCT calculations\n  EAX: Block pointer (preserved from parameter)\n  EBX, ESI, EDI: Callee-saved (pushed/popped)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  g_awIdctCosCof1 (0x600257b0): W1 = cos(pi/16) * sqrt(2) * 2^14 = 0x5A00\n  g_awIdctCosCof2 (0x600257b8): W2 = cos(3*pi/16) * sqrt(2) * 2^14\n  g_awIdctCosCof3 (0x600257c0): W3 = cos(5*pi/16) * sqrt(2) * 2^14\n  g_awIdctCosCof4 (0x600257c8): W4 = cos(7*pi/16) * sqrt(2) * 2^14\n  g_awIdctRoundBias (0x600257d0): 128 (0x80) for DC level shift\n\nBlock Layout (8x8 DCT coefficients, 16-bit each):\n  Offset  Row   Description\n  0x00    0     DC + horizontal low freq\n  0x10    1     Vertical freq band 1\n  0x20    2     Horizontal freq band 1\n  0x30    3     Diagonal freq band 1\n  0x40    4     Vertical freq band 2\n  0x50    5     Mixed freq band 1\n  0x60    6     Horizontal freq band 2\n  0x70    7     High frequency components\n\nCalled From:\n  - InitializeMmxDecodeFunctionTable (function pointer registration)\n  - InitializeMmx2DecodeFunctionTable (enhanced MMX path)",
