      "name": "FillBitBuffer",
      "signature": "undefined4 FillBitBuffer(uint * param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Fills the bit buffer with bytes from the JPEG input stream until sufficient bits are available.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if bit count (offset 0x0C) >= 25 bits, return 0 if sufficient\n2. Check for pending marker byte at offset 0x30, handle if present\n3. If input buffer empty (offset 0x24 <= 0), call RefillInputBuffer (0x60001050)\n4. Read byte from input pointer (offset 0x10), decrement remaining count (offset 0x24)\n5. If byte is 0xFF (JPEG marker prefix):\n   a. Read next byte - if 0x00, it's byte-stuffed 0xFF (use 0xFF as data)\n   b. If non-zero, store as pending marker and return 100 (marker found)\n6. Shift 64-bit accumulator left 8 bits using __allshl, OR in new byte\n7. Increment bit count by 8, loop until >= 25 bits available\n8. Return 0 on success\n\nParameters:\n  pBitState - Pointer to bit reader state structure:\n    +0x00: dword - Low 32 bits of bit accumulator\n    +0x04: dword - High 32 bits of bit accumulator\n    +0x0C: dword - Current bit count in accumulator\n    +0x10: dword - Current input buffer pointer\n    +0x1C: dword - Total bytes read counter\n    +0x24: dword - Remaining bytes in input buffer\n    +0x30: byte  - Pending JPEG marker byte (0 if none)\n    +0x3C: dword - Refill callback pointer (0 if no refill available)\n  nMinBits - Minimum number of bits required in buffer\n\nReturns:\n  0   - Success, bit buffer has >= 25 bits\n  100 - JPEG marker encountered (marker stored at offset 0x30)\n  -21 - Error, unable to refill input buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Handles JPEG byte stuffing where 0xFF 0x00 represents literal 0xFF\n  - Non-zero byte after 0xFF indicates JPEG marker, halts reading",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:57d3306008f15829f54fe1b5a2fdc77e4567cbcbd133e18801f4c35d58981e9c",
