      "name": "DecodeHuffmanSymbolSlow",
      "signature": "longlong DecodeHuffmanSymbolSlow(uint * param_1, int param_2, uint * param_3, int param_4)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "longlong",
      "comment": "Decodes a Huffman symbol using bit-by-bit slow path when fast 8-bit lookup fails.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if bit buffer has sufficient bits for initial code length\n  2. If not, call FillBitBuffer to refill; return error on failure\n  3. Consume initial bits and extract code value with bitmask\n  4. Look up code limit at table offset 0x62a + codeLen*2\n  5. While code value exceeds limit:\n     a. Refill bit buffer if needed (1 bit minimum)\n     b. Shift code value left and append next bit\n     c. Advance to next code length limit\n     d. Increment code length counter\n  6. If code length exceeds 16 bits: return error with symbol=0\n  7. Compute symbol index from table offsets 0x64e, 0x608, and 0x408\n  8. Store decoded symbol and return success\n\nParameters:\n  pBitBuffer      - Pointer to bit buffer context (uint[4]):\n                    [0-1] qwBits: 64-bit accumulated bit buffer\n                    [3] nBitsRemaining: count of valid bits in buffer\n  pHuffmanTable   - Pointer to Huffman decode table structure:\n                    [+0x408] Symbol lookup table (ushort[])\n                    [+0x608] Code base offsets per length (ushort[17])\n                    [+0x62a] Code limit values per length (ushort[17])\n                    [+0x64e] Symbol offset base per length (ushort[17])\n  pdwSymbol       - Output pointer for decoded Huffman symbol value\n  nInitialCodeLen - Initial code length to start decoding (typically 9 or 1)\n\nReturns:\n  Low 32 bits (EAX):\n    0        - Success, symbol stored in *pdwSymbol\n    Non-zero - Error from FillBitBuffer (bit underflow)\n  High 32 bits (EDX):\n    Contains last bits remaining value (internal state)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x10   - Maximum Huffman code length (16 bits)\n  0x408  - Offset to symbol lookup table\n  0x608  - Offset to code base offset table  \n  0x62a  - Offset to code limit table\n  0x64e  - Offset to symbol offset base table\n\nRelated Functions:\n  FillBitBuffer - Refills bit buffer from input stream\n  DecodeHuffmanSymbol - Fast path caller, uses 8-bit lookup first",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:4b40a7bfde79a56e8d282a588adf449ddaff54f0404790f96028932b0a968b9f",
