      "name": "DecodeProgressiveDctBlock",
      "signature": "uint DecodeProgressiveDctBlock(uint * param_1, int param_2, int param_3, int * param_4, short * param_5, int param_6)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Decodes a progressive JPEG 8x8 DCT block with Huffman entropy coding.\n\nReads variable-length coded AC/DC coefficients from the bitstream, applies zig-zag\nordering, sign extension, and dequantization to produce a 64-coefficient output block.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear the 128-byte coefficient output buffer via runtime shift function\n2. Decode the DC coefficient using Huffman symbol table at nStartIndex\n3. If DC category non-zero, extract additional bits for sign/magnitude\n4. Apply coefficient extend table for negative value reconstruction\n5. Accumulate DC value with previous block's DC (differential coding)\n6. Loop through up to 63 AC coefficient positions:\n   a. Decode Huffman symbol (RRRRSSSS format: run/size nibbles)\n   b. If size=0 and run=15 (ZRL), skip 16 zeros\n   c. If size=0 and run!=15 (EOB), break early\n   d. Skip run zeros via zig-zag pointer advancement\n   e. Extract size bits for coefficient magnitude\n   f. Apply extend table for negative coefficients\n   g. Store coefficient at zig-zag ordered position\n7. Call DequantizeCoefficients to multiply by quantization table\n\nParameters:\n  pBitStream     - Pointer to bit stream reader state structure\n  nStartIndex    - Huffman table index for DC coefficient decoding\n  nEndIndex      - Huffman table index for AC coefficient decoding\n  pnDcValue      - Pointer to accumulated DC value (differential DPCM)\n  pCoefficients  - Output array of 64 dequantized DCT coefficients\n  pQuantTable    - Pointer to 64-entry quantization table\n\nReturns:\n  0              - Success, block fully decoded\n  Non-zero       - Error code from Huffman decode or bit buffer fill\n  Positive value - Partial decode (end of scan segment)\n\nStructure Layout (BitStream State at pBitStream):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Description\n  0x00    4     dwBits        Current bit buffer (32 bits)\n  0x04    4     dwBitsHigh    Extended bit buffer high dword\n  0x08    4     dwBytePos     Current byte position in stream\n  0x0C    4     nBitsLeft     Number of valid bits remaining\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x80           - Size of coefficient buffer in bytes (64 * 2)\n  0x3F           - Initial AC coefficient counter (63 positions)\n  0x0F           - Mask for extracting 4-bit run/size fields\n  0x10           - ZRL (Zero Run Length) skip count increment\n\nError Handling:\n  Returns immediately if Huffman decode fails\n  Calls DequantizeCoefficients before early return on positive errors",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
