      "name": "DequantizeCoefficients",
      "signature": "undefined DequantizeCoefficients(short * param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Dequantizes 64 DCT coefficients by multiplying with quantization table values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Iterate through 64 coefficient-quantizer pairs (8x8 DCT block)\n2. For each pair: result = (coefficient * quantizer + 64) >> 7\n3. The +64 provides rounding for the division by 128\n4. Store dequantized value back to coefficient array\n\nParameters:\n  pnCoefficients - Pointer to 64-element array of 16-bit DCT coefficients (modified in place)\n  pnQuantTable   - Pointer to 64-element quantization table with scaled values\n\nReturns:\n  void - Coefficients are modified in place\n\nCalled By:\n  DecodeProgressiveDctBlock - During progressive JPEG decoding\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x40 (64)  - Loop count for 8x8 DCT block (64 coefficients)\n  0x40 (64)  - Rounding bias for division by 128\n  0x7 (>>7)  - Right shift by 7 = division by 128",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:35c081767d7025780abc8109ba3713e80f41020685b6d7415c3d0853272a8100",
