      "name": "DecodeAndDequantizeDcCoefficient",
      "signature": "uint DecodeAndDequantizeDcCoefficient(uint * param_1, int param_2, undefined2 * param_3, int * param_4, byte param_5, short param_6)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Decodes and dequantizes a DC coefficient for progressive JPEG decoding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Decode Huffman symbol to get coefficient bit count\n2. If symbol is non-zero, extract raw bits from bit buffer\n3. Convert unsigned raw bits to signed coefficient using offset table\n4. Add differential coefficient to DC predictor (DPCM decoding)\n5. Apply successive approximation shift and quantization scaling\n6. Store final dequantized coefficient\n\nParameters:\n  pBitBuffer - Bit buffer context (uint[4]: qwBits, dwBitsHi, dwBitsLo, nBitsRemaining)\n  nHuffmanTable - Index of Huffman table for DC coefficient decoding\n  pnOutputCoeff - Output pointer for dequantized coefficient value\n  pnDcPredictor - DC predictor value for DPCM differential decoding (updated in-place)\n  bSuccessiveApproxLow - Successive approximation low bit position (progressive JPEG)\n  nQuantValue - Quantization table value for dequantization scaling\n\nReturns:\n  0 on success\n  Non-zero error code on Huffman decode or bit buffer fill failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xf - Mask for coefficient bit count (low 4 bits of Huffman symbol)\n  0x40 - Rounding bias for dequantization (0.5 * 128 for 7-bit shift)\n  7 - Final right shift for dequantization scaling\n\nRelated:\n  DecodeHuffmanSymbol - Decodes variable-length Huffman code\n  FillBitBuffer - Refills bit buffer when insufficient bits remain\n  g_anDctCoefficientOffsets - Lookup table for signed coefficient conversion",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:2f03b5024b4902e11928c089849b4ab2e12c9bf4f6c0adf75ada31e727271a7d",
