      "name": "DecodeProgressiveAcCoefficients",
      "signature": "uint DecodeProgressiveAcCoefficients(uint * param_1, int param_2, int param_3, int param_4, int param_5, undefined4 param_6, int param_7)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Decodes and dequantizes AC coefficients for progressive JPEG DCT scans.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if end-of-block (EOB) run counter is active; if so, decrement and return\n2. Loop through coefficient indices from nStartIndex to nEndIndex\n3. Decode Huffman symbol to get run-length (high nibble) and coefficient size (low nibble)\n4. If coefficient size is zero, handle run-of-zeros or EOB patterns\n5. For non-zero coefficients: extract raw bits, apply sign extension\n6. Use zigzag order table to map linear index to 2D DCT position\n7. Dequantize coefficient: multiply by quantization value, scale by approximation bits\n8. Add 0x40 (rounding) and shift right by 7 for fixed-point adjustment\n\nParameters:\n    pBitstream - Pointer to bitstream decoder context structure\n    pnOutputCoeffs - Output buffer for dequantized coefficients (16-bit values)\n    nHuffmanTable - Huffman table selector for AC coefficient decoding\n    nStartIndex - First coefficient index in spectral range (usually 1-63)\n    nEndIndex - Last coefficient index in spectral range (usually 63)\n    dwApproxBitShift - Successive approximation bit position (progressive refinement)\n    pnQuantTable - Pointer to quantization table (16-bit values)\n\nReturns:\n    0 - Success, all coefficients in range decoded\n    Non-zero - Error code from bitstream read (propagated from FUN_60013d90/FUN_60013ba0)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n    Run-length of 0xF with size 0: Skip 15 zeros (ZRL - zero run length)\n    Run-length != 0xF with size 0: End of block, set EOB counter\n    Negative coefficients use sign extension from high bit\n\nMagic Numbers:\n    0x40 - Rounding constant for fixed-point division (0.5 in Q7 format)\n    7 - Right shift for Q7 to integer conversion\n    0xF - Mask for nibble extraction (run-length / coefficient size)\n    10 - Offset to EOB counter in bitstream context (pBitstream[10])\n\nStructure Layout (pBitstream context, partial):\n    Offset  Size  Field           Description\n    0x00    4     Data buffer     Current bit buffer value\n    0x04    4     Bit position    Current bit position in buffer\n    0x0C    4     Bits remaining  Number of bits left in buffer\n    0x28    4     EOB counter     End-of-block run counter",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:0a1c0fc18589d1f483bc495e71c6ff6be9dc4832f3b3db909cbc7cca6dee7a94",
