      "name": "RefineProgressiveAcCoefficients",
      "signature": "uint RefineProgressiveAcCoefficients(uint * param_1, int param_2, int param_3, uint param_4, int param_5, byte param_6, int param_7)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Refines AC coefficients for JPEG progressive scan successive approximation passes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate refinement masks from successive approximation bit position\n   - dwPosMask = 1 << bSuccessiveApprox (positive delta mask)\n   - dwNegMask = -1 << bSuccessiveApprox (negative delta mask)\n2. Check if EOB run counter (pBitstream[10]) is zero\n   - If non-zero, skip to refinement-only phase (step 5)\n3. Main decode loop (while spectral position <= nSpectralEnd):\n   a. Call FUN_60013d90 to decode next Huffman-coded run/size value\n   b. Parse RRRRSSSS byte: RRRR = zero run length, SSSS = size category\n   c. If SSSS == 0: Check for EOB or ZRL marker\n   d. If SSSS != 0: Read correction bit and calculate delta\n4. Iterate through zigzag positions, refining non-zero coefficients:\n   - Skip zero coefficients (decrement run counter)\n   - For non-zero coefficients: read bit, apply refinement if not already set\n5. EOB run refinement phase: if EOB run > 0, refine remaining non-zero coefficients\n\nParameters:\n- pBitstream: Bitstream reader state structure (uint *)\n  - [0]: Current bit buffer\n  - [1]: Bit buffer shift position\n  - [3]: Bits remaining in buffer\n  - [10]: EOB run counter for progressive refinement\n- psCoefficients: Pointer to 64-element short array (8x8 DCT block)\n- nDctBufferIndex: Huffman table index for AC coefficient decoding\n- dwSpectralStart: Starting spectral position (Ss from SOS marker)\n- nSpectralEnd: Ending spectral position (Se from SOS marker)\n- bSuccessiveApprox: Successive approximation bit position (Al from SOS)\n- psQuantTable: Quantization table values for dequantization\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Success - all coefficients refined within spectral range\n- Non-zero: Error from FUN_60013d90 or FUN_60013ba0 (bitstream underflow)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x40 (64): Rounding bias for quantization ((val + 64) >> 7 = (val + 0.5) / 128)\n- 0xF (15): ZRL marker in RRRRSSSS byte (16 consecutive zeros)\n- 7: Right shift for quantization rounding (divide by 128)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- EOB run counter > 0 at entry: Skip decoding, only refine existing non-zero coefficients\n- RRRR = 0xF and SSSS = 0: ZRL marker, skip 16 zeros\n- RRRR != 0 and SSSS = 0: EOB with run count = (1 << RRRR) + extra bits",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
