      "name": "BuildHuffmanDecodeTable",
      "signature": "undefined BuildHuffmanDecodeTable(undefined4 * param_1, undefined4 param_2, undefined4 param_3, int param_4, int param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Builds a Huffman decoding lookup table for JPEG decompression.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output table with tree index and max symbols at first two entries\n2. Build bit length map: for each bit length (1-16), fill buffer with repeated length value\n3. Generate canonical Huffman codes: assign sequential codes starting from minimum length\n4. Initialize symbol offset tables at output offsets 0x608, 0x62A, 0x64E (3 x 17 entries)\n5. Populate symbol value table at offset 0x408 for each bit length group\n6. Set end marker 0xFFFF at offset 0x64C\n7. Clear 256-entry decode lookup table at offset 0x8\n8. Build fast 8-bit decode table: for each symbol, fill lookup entries with (bitlen << 16) | symbol\n\nParameters:\n  pDecodeTable (uint*) - Output buffer for Huffman decode table structure (min 0x650 bytes)\n  dwTreeIndex (uint) - Tree identifier stored at table[0]\n  dwMaxSymbols (uint) - Maximum symbol count stored at table[1]\n  pbCodeLengths (byte*) - Array of 16 bytes, count of codes per bit length\n  pbSymbolValues (byte*) - Symbol values ordered by code length then code value\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset   Size   Field                    Description\n  0x000    4      dwTreeIndex              Tree identifier\n  0x004    4      dwMaxSymbols             Max symbols in table\n  0x008    0x400  adwDecodeLookup[256]     8-bit fast decode (bitlen<<16|symbol)\n  0x408    0x200  awSymbolValues[256]      Symbol values by canonical order\n  0x608    0x22   awOffsets1[17]           First offset table (base codes)\n  0x62A    0x22   awOffsets2[17]           Second offset table (counts)\n  0x64C    2      wEndMarker               End marker (0xFFFF)\n  0x64E    0x22   awOffsets3[17]           Third offset table (indices)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x10 (16) - Maximum Huffman code bit length per JPEG spec\n  0x100 (256) - Decode lookup table entry count (8-bit fast path)\n  0xFFFF - End of table marker sentinel\n\nSSA Variables (Decompiler Artifacts - Cannot Be Renamed):\n  piVar1 (int*) - Pointer iterator for canonical code assignment\n  iVar2 (int) - Temporary index accumulator\n  puVar3 (uint*) - Output table pointer walker\n  uVar4 (uint) - Symbol index counter\n  uVar5 (uint) - Inner loop counter / code count\n  bVar6 (byte) - Current bit length byte value\n  iVar7 (int) - Outer loop counter / Huffman code value\n  iVar8 (int) - Inner loop counter / entry count\n  pbVar9 (byte*) - Byte pointer for STOSD/STOSB operations\n\nLocal Variables:\n  bBitLengthMap (byte) - Start of bit length mapping buffer\n  abStack_507[255] (byte) - Continuation of bit length buffer\n  awSymbolBuffer[2] (ushort) - Intermediate symbol lookup buffer\n  anCanonicalCodes[257] (int) - Canonical Huffman code values\n  dwCodeLen (uint) - Current bit length being processed\n  pTableEntry (uint*) - Current symbol table write position\n  dwSymbolCount (uint) - Count of symbols at current bit length\n  nBitLength (int) - Current bit length (1-16)\n  nShiftBits (int) - Shift amount for code expansion (7 down to 0)\n  pnCodeTable (int*) - Pointer into canonical codes array\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty bit length groups are skipped\n  - Fast lookup only handles 8-bit codes (lengths 1-8)\n  - Longer codes require secondary table lookup via offset tables",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
