      "name": "MultiplyQ15VectorInPlace",
      "signature": "undefined MultiplyQ15VectorInPlace(int param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Multiplies two 64-element Q15 fixed-point vectors element-wise in place.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Iterate through 64 elements (indices 0 to 63)\n2. For each element, multiply pnDest[i] by pnSrc[i]\n3. Add 0x4000 (half-bit rounding for Q15)\n4. Right shift by 15 to normalize back to Q15 format\n5. Store result back to pnDest[i]\n\nParameters:\n    pnDest - Pointer to destination/first operand short[64] array (modified in place)\n    pnSrc - Pointer to source/second operand short[64] array (read-only)\n\nReturns:\n    void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n    - Q15 fixed-point format: values represent fractions in range [-1.0, ~0.99997]\n    - Rounding: 0x4000 (16384) added before shift for proper rounding\n    - Overflow: Product may saturate if both inputs are near \u00b132768\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n    0x40 (64) - Array element count\n    0x4000 (16384) - Half-LSB rounding bias for Q15\n    0xF (15) - Q15 fractional bit count\n\nUsed by decode function table initialization (Scalar, SSE, SSE2 variants).",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
