      "name": "EncodeAcCoefficientsBlock",
      "signature": "undefined EncodeAcCoefficientsBlock(undefined8 * param_1, int param_2, int param_3, short * param_4, short * param_5, uint * param_6)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Encodes AC DCT coefficients for a single 8x8 block using Huffman encoding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate DC difference (current DC - previous DC) for differential encoding\n2. Swap values: store current DC to pnPreviousDc for next block\n3. Process coefficients through zigzag reordering via ProcessZigzagDctCoefficients\n4. Save output buffer state (MMX register MM7 preserves qword)\n5. Check if byte stuffing is required (restart markers active and buffer threshold)\n6. Encode DC coefficient with appropriate Huffman table\n7. For each AC coefficient with non-zero value:\n   a. If run length exceeds 0xF0 (15 zeros), write ZRL (zero run length) codes\n   b. Write combined run/size code followed by coefficient bits\n8. Write EOB (end of block) marker when remaining coefficients are zero\n9. Restore output buffer state\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputBuffer - JPEG output buffer for bit stream writing\n  nDcHuffmanTable - Pointer to DC Huffman encoding table (offset +0x408 = codes, +0x8 = bit counts)\n  nAcHuffmanTable - Pointer to AC Huffman encoding table (offset +0x408 = codes, +0x8 = bit counts)\n  pnPreviousDc - Pointer to previous block's DC value for differential encoding\n  pnCoefficients - Pointer to 64 DCT coefficients in raster order (converted to zigzag)\n  pqwEncodingState - Encoding state array (+0x20 = run lengths, +0x40 = bit lengths)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Encoded bits are written directly to pOutputBuffer\n\nStructure Layout (Huffman Tables):\n  Offset  Size  Field              Description\n  0x008   0x400 anBitCounts[256]   Bit count per symbol (int array)\n  0x408   0x200 awCodes[256]       Huffman codes (ushort array)\n  0x5E8   2     wZrlCode           Zero Run Length code (16 zeros)\n  0x3C8   4     nZrlBitCount       ZRL code bit count\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x601 - Buffer threshold for byte stuffing decision\n  0xF0  - Maximum run-length threshold (15 zeros << 4)\n  0x100 - Run length decrement per ZRL code\n  0x3C  - Offset to restart marker flag in output buffer",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:e51b6e237ef54ab5002bf4bfb1aaf6d1c5ed2f5d19e213f459eafed3ab212bea",
