      "name": "WriteBitsToStream",
      "signature": "undefined4 WriteBitsToStream(uint * param_1, uint param_2, int param_3)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Writes a specified number of bits to a JPEG bitstream buffer with byte stuffing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if bits fit in remaining accumulator space (nBitCount <= pBitStream[3])\n2. If fits: mask input bits, shift to position, OR into accumulator, return success\n3. If overflow: increment byte counter, calculate remaining bits after partial write\n4. Combine partial bits with accumulator, write to output buffer\n5. Check for 0xFF marker byte - if found, insert 0x00 stuffing byte (JPEG escape)\n6. Advance output pointer, reset accumulator to 0, reset bit count to 8\n7. Loop until all bits written or buffer overflow detected (pBitStream[4] >= pBitStream[6])\n\nParameters:\n  pBitStream - Pointer to bitstream state array:\n               [0] dwAccumulator: Current bit accumulator (low 32 bits)\n               [1] dwAccumulatorHigh: High bits for sign extension\n               [3] nBitsRemaining: Bits available in current byte (0-8)\n               [4] pOutputPtr: Current output buffer write position\n               [6] pBufferEnd: End of output buffer (boundary check)\n               [7] dwBytesWritten: Total bytes written counter\n  dwBitsToWrite - Bit value to write (only lower nBitCount bits used)\n  nBitCount - Number of bits to write from dwBitsToWrite (1-32)\n\nReturns:\n  0 - Success, all bits written\n  -24 (0xFFFFFFE8) - Buffer overflow, output buffer exhausted\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xFF (-1 as char) - JPEG marker prefix requiring byte stuffing\n  0x00 - Stuffing byte inserted after 0xFF to escape marker\n  8 - Bits per byte, reset value for nBitsRemaining after byte output\n\nError Handling:\n  Returns -24 when output pointer reaches or exceeds buffer end boundary",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
