      "name": "WriteBitsToBitStream",
      "signature": "int WriteBitsToBitStream(uint * param_1, uint param_2, int param_3)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Writes a specified number of bits to a JPEG bitstream buffer with byte stuffing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize result code to success (0)\n2. Loop while bits remain to write:\n   a. If remaining bits fit in current byte accumulator:\n      - Subtract bit count from available bits\n      - Mask and shift input value, OR into accumulator\n      - Return success\n   b. Otherwise (bits span multiple bytes):\n      - Increment byte counter\n      - Calculate remaining bits after filling current byte\n      - Flush buffer if write position exceeds limit\n      - Write accumulated byte with upper bits from input\n      - Check for 0xFF byte (JPEG marker prefix)\n      - If 0xFF written, insert 0x00 stuffing byte\n      - Reset accumulator and set available bits to 8\n3. Return result code (0=success, non-zero=flush error)\n\nParameters:\n  pBitStream - Pointer to bitstream structure with fields:\n               [0x00] dwAccumulatorLow - Low bits of accumulator\n               [0x04] dwAccumulatorHigh - High bits of accumulator\n               [0x0C] dwBitsRemaining - Bits available in current byte (0-8)\n               [0x10] dwWritePosition - Current write pointer\n               [0x18] dwBufferLimit - Buffer end position\n               [0x1C] dwByteCount - Total bytes written\n  dwBitValue - Value containing bits to write (right-aligned)\n  nBitCount - Number of bits to write from dwBitValue\n\nReturns:\n  0 - Success, bits written to buffer\n  Non-zero - Error from FlushBitStreamBuffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - 0xFF byte stuffing: JPEG requires 0x00 after 0xFF to distinguish from markers\n  - Buffer overflow: Calls FlushBitStreamBuffer when write position exceeds limit\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xFF (-1 as char) - JPEG marker byte requiring stuffing\n  0x1F (31) - Mask for shift count (5 bits for 0-31 range)\n  8 - Bits per byte, reset value for dwBitsRemaining",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
