      "name": "FlushBitStreamBuffer",
      "signature": "undefined4 FlushBitStreamBuffer(int param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Flushes the bit stream buffer to the output file.\n\nWrites the 0x1000 byte buffer from the BitstreamContext structure to the \nassociated file handle. On success, resets the buffer pointers for continued\nwriting. Called by bit-writing functions when the buffer becomes full.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize result to success (0)\n2. Call WriteFile wrapper to write 0x1000 bytes from buffer at offset 0x40\n3. If write failed or bytes written != 0x1000, return error -23\n4. On success, reset pCurrent (offset 0x10) to buffer start\n5. Set pEnd (offset 0x18) to buffer end (base + 0x1040)\n6. Return success (0)\n\nParameters:\n  pBitStream - Pointer to BitstreamContext structure containing:\n    +0x10: pCurrent - Current write position pointer\n    +0x18: pEnd - End of buffer pointer  \n    +0x3C: hFile - File handle for output\n    +0x40: abBuffer[0x1000] - 4KB write buffer\n\nReturns:\n  0 on success\n  -23 (0xFFFFFFE9) on write failure or incomplete write\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1000 - Buffer size (4KB)\n  0x1040 - Buffer end offset (0x40 + 0x1000)\n  0xFFFFFFE9 - Error code for write failure (-23)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:49591ada02ba65eab889f33d91a17ed1cc434e8d07a4b39a3d02fd15ba9b5b25",
