      "name": "DecodeAcCoefficientsSkip",
      "signature": "undefined DecodeAcCoefficientsSkip(ulonglong * param_1, int param_2, int param_3, int * param_4)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Decodes and skips JPEG AC coefficients without writing to output block.\n\nThis function is a variant of DecodeAcCoefficientsBlock that only updates the\nDC coefficient accumulator without storing coefficient values. Used when\ncoefficient data needs to be parsed but not retained (e.g., skipping blocks).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save bitstream state (marker, positions) for potential restoration\n2. If insufficient bits (<8), call RefillBitBufferFromStream to refill buffer\n3. Decode DC coefficient using Huffman table lookup from nDcHuffmanTable\n4. Apply coefficient threshold/offset correction from g_anCoefficientThresholds\n5. Accumulate decoded DC value into *pnDcCoefficient\n6. Loop decoding AC coefficients (up to 63 per 8x8 block):\n   a. Extract run-length coded value from nAcHuffmanTable\n   b. Handle zero runs (skip positions) and EOB markers\n   c. Refill bit buffer as needed via RefillBitBufferFromStream/DecodeHuffmanCodeSlow\n7. Restore bitstream state and return via RestoreRegistersAndReturn\n\nParameters:\n  pBitstream (ulonglong*) - Pointer to 64-byte bitstream state structure\n      [0x00] qword: Current bit buffer (MM1 register)\n      [0x0C] dword: Bits remaining in buffer\n      [0x10] dword: Stream position\n      [0x1C] dword: Saved state 1\n      [0x24] dword: Saved state 2\n      [0x30] byte: Saved marker byte\n  nDcHuffmanTable (int) - DC Huffman decode table base address (+8 for lookup)\n  nAcHuffmanTable (int) - AC Huffman decode table base address (+8 for lookup)\n  pnDcCoefficient (int*) - Pointer to DC coefficient accumulator (updated in place)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function updates bitstream state and DC coefficient in place\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x40 (64) - Bit width constant for shift calculations\n  0x38 (56) - Shift to extract top 8 bits of 64-bit buffer\n  0x10000 - Threshold for extended Huffman code lookup\n  0xFFFF - Mask for code length extraction\n  0x3F (63) - Maximum AC coefficient index (64 coefficients per block)\n  0xF0 (240) - Zero run-length 16 (ZRL) marker\n  0x0F (15) - Mask for run length extraction\n\nStructure Layout (Bitstream State):\n  Offset  Size  Field              Type\n  0x00    8     qwBitBuffer        ulonglong (MM register)\n  0x0C    4     nBitsRemaining     int\n  0x10    4     dwStreamPos        uint\n  0x1C    4     dwSavedState1      uint\n  0x24    4     dwSavedState2      uint\n  0x30    1     bMarkerByte        byte\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Insufficient bits for lookup triggers slow path via DecodeHuffmanCodeSlow\n  - ZRL marker (0xF0) skips 16 zero coefficients without terminating\n  - EOB marker terminates AC coefficient loop early\n  - Hash-based variable bSavedMarker cannot be typed by decompiler (Ghidra limitation)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
