      "name": "RefillBitBufferFromStream",
      "signature": "undefined4 RefillBitBufferFromStream(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Refills the 64-bit MMX bit buffer from the input stream for JPEG Huffman decoding.\n\nThis function reads bytes from the JPEG bitstream into the MM1 register, handling\nJPEG marker byte stuffing (0xFF followed by 0x00 is decoded as 0xFF data byte).\nUses parent function's stack frame via implicit EBP register.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if marker byte already stored in [EBP-0x10] (previous escape sequence)\n2. Fast path: If 4+ bytes available and none are 0xFF, read DWORD directly\n3. Slow path: Read bytes one at a time, checking for marker escape sequences\n4. On 0xFF byte: read next byte to determine if stuffed (0x00) or marker\n5. If stuffed zero, continue reading; if marker, save and exit loop\n6. Update bit position (EDI) by 8 for each byte read\n7. Continue until 57+ bits buffered or buffer exhausted\n8. Call FUN_60015a20 to refill input buffer if exhausted\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT unaff_EBP - Parent stack frame pointer\n    [EBP+0x08] dword: Pointer to bitstream state structure\n    [EBP-0x08] dword: Bytes remaining in input buffer\n    [EBP-0x10] byte:  Saved marker byte from escape sequence\n    [EBP-0x14] dword: Stream position counter\n  IMPLICIT unaff_ESI - Current position in input buffer (char*)\n  IMPLICIT unaff_EDI - Current bit position in MM1 buffer (0-56)\n  IMPLICIT in_MM1 - 64-bit bit buffer accumulator\n  IMPLICIT in_MM4 - Contains 0x40 (64) for shift calculations\n\nReturns:\n  int - 0xFF (255) on success, bits refilled\n      - 0x00 (0) on error or end of stream\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0xFF (-1) - JPEG marker prefix / escape byte\n  0x00 - Stuffed zero following 0xFF in data\n  0x38 (56) - Maximum bit position before buffer considered full\n  0x39 (57) - Bit position check threshold\n  0x08 - Bits per byte increment\n\nBitstream Structure Layout (at [EBP+0x08]):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Type\n  0x10    4     pStreamBuffer   char* (current read position)\n  0x24    4     nBytesInBuffer  int (bytes remaining in buffer)\n  0x3C    4     hInputHandle    HANDLE (source file/stream handle)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
