      "name": "DecodeHuffmanCodeSlow",
      "signature": "longlong DecodeHuffmanCodeSlow(undefined4 param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "longlong",
      "comment": "Decodes a Huffman code using slow bit-by-bit extraction when fast 8-bit lookup fails.\n\nThis function performs canonical Huffman decoding by extracting bits one at a time\nfrom the 64-bit buffer in MM1 register. Called when there aren't enough bits (< 8)\nfor the fast lookup path, or when the initial 8-bit lookup returns a code requiring\nmore bits to decode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save table index from EBX to stack at [EBP-0x1C]\n2. If bits remaining (EDI) < table index, call FUN_60015852 to refill buffer\n3. Calculate initial code bits by shifting MM1 right by (64 - table index)\n4. Enter decode loop:\n   a. Compare current code against max code for this bit length (table+0x62A)\n   b. If code <= max, look up decoded value from table+0x408\n   c. Otherwise, shift in next bit from buffer and increment bit length\n   d. Call FUN_60015852 to refill if bits exhausted\n5. Return decoded value in low dword, caller state preserved in high dword\n\nParameters:\n  nHuffmanTableBase (ECX) - Not directly used, passed through to FUN_60015852\n  dwCallerState (EDX) - Preserved and returned in high dword of result\n  IMPLICIT unaff_EBX - Initial code length / table index\n  IMPLICIT unaff_EDI - Bits remaining in buffer\n  IMPLICIT unaff_EBP - Frame pointer for stack variable access\n  IMPLICIT in_MM1 - 64-bit bit buffer (MMX register)\n  IMPLICIT in_MM4 - Contains 64 (0x40) for shift calculations\n\nReturns:\n  longlong - Low dword: decoded symbol value (0-255) or 0 on length overflow\n                        or 1 on buffer refill failure\n           - High dword: preserved dwCallerState value\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x62A - Offset to max code table (short array indexed by code length)\n  0x608 - Offset to code offset table (short array)\n  0x64E - Offset to value offset table (short array)\n  0x408 - Offset to decoded value table (short array)\n  0x11 (17) - Maximum valid Huffman code length\n  0x3F - Mask to extract high bit from 64-bit buffer (shift by 63)\n\nHuffman Table Layout:\n  Offset  Size   Field                   Description\n  0x408   N*2    awDecodedValues        Decoded symbol values (shorts)\n  0x608   32     awCodeOffsets          Code offset per bit length\n  0x62A   32     awMaxCodes             Maximum code per bit length\n  0x64E   32     awValueOffsets         Value table offset per bit length",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:bcf86fa89b6f29a66ca1dc7d799546a3da129ab0d3fcde0b1e20a44661e47230",
