      "name": "RestoreRegistersAndReturn",
      "signature": "void RestoreRegistersAndReturn(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Shared function epilogue that restores callee-saved registers and returns.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Restore EDI from stack (callee-saved)\n2. Restore ESI from stack (callee-saved)\n3. Restore EBX from stack (callee-saved)\n4. Tear down stack frame (MOV ESP,EBP)\n5. Restore caller's EBP\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  None - Uses registers and stack state set up by caller\n\nReturns:\n  void - Control returns to address on stack\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  This is a shared epilogue block jumped to from DecodeAcCoefficientsSkip\n  at both normal completion (0x6001575b) and error exit (0x6001584d) paths.\n  The function does not have its own prologue - it is the tail of another\n  function's execution flow.\n\nRegister Restoration Order:\n  POP EDI  - Restore destination index register\n  POP ESI  - Restore source index register\n  POP EBX  - Restore base register\n  MOV ESP,EBP - Collapse stack frame\n  POP EBP  - Restore caller's frame pointer\n  RET      - Return to caller",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
