      "name": "RefillStreamBufferFromFile",
      "signature": "undefined4 RefillStreamBufferFromFile(int param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Refills the bitstream input buffer by reading data from the associated file handle.\n\nThis function is called when the JPEG bitstream processing functions exhaust\nthe current input buffer and need more data from the source file. It reads\nup to 4096 bytes (0x1000) into the internal buffer at offset +0x40.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Call ReadFile wrapper (FUN_600180f0) to read 0x1000 bytes from file handle\n  2. Store bytes read count at offset +0x24 (nBytesRemaining)\n  3. Check read result:\n     a. If read failed (nReadResult == 0) AND bytes read == 0, return error\n     b. Otherwise, update buffer pointer at +0x10 to point to internal buffer\n  4. Return 0 on success, 0xFFFFFFF5 (-11) on EOF/failure\n\nParameters:\n  pBitstreamContext - Pointer to BitstreamContext structure containing file handle and buffer\n\nReturns:\n  int - 0 on success (buffer refilled)\n      - 0xFFFFFFF5 (-11) on failure (ReadFile failed with no bytes read)\n\nStructure Layout (BitstreamContext at pBitstreamContext):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Description\n  +0x10   4     pInputBuffer    Current buffer read position\n  +0x24   4     nBytesRemaining Bytes available in buffer\n  +0x3C   4     hFileHandle     Windows file HANDLE for reading\n  +0x40   4096  abInputBuffer   Internal 4KB read buffer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1000      - Buffer read size (4096 bytes)\n  0xFFFFFFF5  - Return code for EOF/read failure (-11 signed)\n\nRelated Functions:\n  FUN_600180f0                    - ReadFile wrapper called by this function\n  RefillBitBufferFromStream       - Primary caller during Huffman decoding\n  RefillBitBufferWithMarkerHandling - Caller during marker-aware bit reading",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:7014529fd6df0b88da1bb4cc8cba543c02334f84104f869d5092d995c2b1a406",
