      "name": "DecodeAndDequantizeAcBlock",
      "signature": "undefined DecodeAndDequantizeAcBlock(undefined4 param_1, uint param_2, ulonglong * param_3, int param_4, int param_5, uint * param_6, int * param_7, uint * param_8)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Decodes and dequantizes a single 8x8 DCT block from a JPEG bitstream.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output buffer (64 coefficients) to zero using MMX registers\n2. Extract DC coefficient using Huffman table lookup from pDcHuffTable\n3. Apply DC prediction differential and update DC predictor\n4. Dequantize DC coefficient using quantization table entry and scaling\n5. Loop to decode up to 64 AC coefficients:\n   a. Read Huffman code from bitstream using pAcHuffTable\n   b. Extract run-length (zeros to skip) and coefficient size from code\n   c. Read raw coefficient bits and apply sign extension using threshold table\n   d. Look up zigzag order position from g_anZigzagOrder\n   e. Dequantize using corresponding quantization table entry\n   f. Store scaled result in output buffer at zigzag position\n6. Handle bitstream refill when buffer runs low (calls FUN_60015f05)\n7. Handle extended Huffman decode for large codes (calls FUN_60015fcb)\n8. Save updated bitstream state back to pBitstream structure\n\nParameters:\n  pUnused - IMPLICIT ECX: Unused parameter (reserved)\n  dwParam - IMPLICIT EDX: Parameter passed to subroutines\n  pBitstream - Pointer to bitstream state structure containing:\n               +0x00: 64-bit bit buffer (ulonglong)\n               +0x0C: Bits remaining in buffer (int)\n               +0x10: Pointer to next input byte (uint*)\n               +0x1C: Bytes consumed count (int)\n               +0x24: Bytes remaining in input (int)\n               +0x30: EOF/marker flag (byte)\n  nDcHuffTable - Pointer to DC Huffman decode table (+8 offset)\n  nAcHuffTable - Pointer to AC Huffman decode table (+8 offset)\n  pDcPredictor - Pointer to DC prediction accumulator\n  pDequantOutput - Output buffer for 64 dequantized coefficients (int[64])\n  pQuantTable - Quantization scaling table for this component\n\nReturns:\n  0 on success (via FUN_60016137 tail call)\n  Non-zero on error (premature end of stream, invalid marker)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x40 (64) - Number of coefficients in 8x8 DCT block\n  0x38 (56) - Bit shift for extracting top byte from 64-bit buffer\n  0x20 (32) - Bits added when refilling buffer with 4 bytes\n  0x07 (7)  - Right shift for dequantization scaling (divide by 128)\n  0xf0 (240) - Mask for detecting ZRL (zero run length = 16)\n  0x0f (15) - Mask for coefficient bit size\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  g_anCoefficientThresholds - Threshold for sign extension decision\n  g_anCoefficientOffsets - Offset for negative coefficient adjustment\n  g_anZigzagOrder - Zigzag scan order mapping (index to position)\n  g_qwQuantMask - MMX mask for quantization (0x0000FFFF0000FFFF)\n  g_qwRoundingConstant - Rounding bias for dequantization (0x40)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
