      "name": "RefillBitBufferWithMarkerHandling",
      "signature": "undefined4 RefillBitBufferWithMarkerHandling(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Refills the 64-bit bit buffer from the input stream with JPEG marker handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Save current bit count from MM4 register into ECX\n  2. Decrement remaining bits counter; if exhausted, jump to refill from stream\n  3. Read next byte from input stream (ESI points to input buffer)\n  4. Check for 0xFF marker byte - if found, handle JPEG byte stuffing:\n     a. Read following byte to check for stuffed zero (0x00)\n     b. If 0x00 follows 0xFF, it's a stuffed byte - use 0xFF as data\n     c. If non-zero follows 0xFF, it's a real marker - handle specially\n  5. Shift new byte into MM1 bit buffer (PSLLQ by 8, then POR)\n  6. Increment bit position counter (EDI) by 8\n  7. If bit position exceeds 56 (0x38), buffer is full - normalize and return\n  8. If more bytes needed and buffer not full, continue reading\n  9. On stream exhaustion, call FUN_60015a20 to refill from file handle\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT ESI     - Pointer to current position in input byte stream\n  IMPLICIT EDI     - Current bit position in 64-bit buffer (0-63)\n  IMPLICIT ECX     - Bytes remaining counter\n  IMPLICIT MM1     - 64-bit accumulated bit buffer\n  IMPLICIT MM4     - Constant 64 (0x40) for bit position calculation\n  IMPLICIT [EBP+8] - Pointer to BitstreamContext structure\n\nReturns:\n  EAX = 0          - Success, buffer refilled\n  EAX = 0x40       - End of stream reached (sets MM4 = 0x40, EAX = 0)\n  EAX != 0         - Error from stream read operation\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xFF   - JPEG marker prefix byte (requires special handling)\n  0x00   - Stuffed zero byte following 0xFF (escape sequence)\n  0x08   - Bits per byte for shift operations\n  0x38   - Maximum bit position before buffer overflow (56 bits)\n  0x40   - Total bit buffer capacity (64 bits)\n\nStructure Layout (BitstreamContext at [EBP+8]):\n  Offset  Size  Field              Description\n  +0x08   4     pBitContext        Pointer to bit buffer state\n  +0x10   4     pInputBuffer       Current input buffer pointer\n  +0x24   4     nBytesRemaining    Bytes left in current buffer\n  +0x3C   4     hFileHandle        File handle for stream refill\n\nRelated Functions:\n  FUN_60015a20             - Reads more data from file handle into buffer\n  DecodeHuffmanSymbol      - Primary caller for Huffman decoding\n  DecodeAndDequantizeAcBlock - Caller during AC coefficient decoding",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:7caec400a39eb66667171d937f952efc3b55aeb12abff6e6cec1316278d0898e",
