      "name": "DecodeHuffmanSymbol",
      "signature": "longlong DecodeHuffmanSymbol(undefined4 param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "longlong",
      "comment": "Decodes a Huffman symbol from the bitstream using canonical Huffman decoding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store initial code length from EBX register to stack frame [EBP-0x1c]\n2. If bits remaining (EDI) less than initial length, refill bitstream buffer\n3. Extract initial code bits from 64-bit MMX register (MM1) into ECX\n4. Loop: Compare extracted code value against Huffman table max value at awMaxCode[len]\n5. If code value <= table max, decode symbol:\n   a. If length < 17, compute symbol index from awCodeBase, awSymbolOffset, awSymbolValues\n   b. Return decoded symbol value\n6. If no match, shift in one more bit and increment code length\n7. If buffer exhausted, call FUN_60015f05 to refill from stream\n8. Continue until match found or error\n\nParameters:\n  pHuffmanTable (ECX): Pointer to HuffmanDecodeTable structure containing decode tables\n  dwUnused (EDX): Unused parameter preserved for caller\n\nIMPLICIT Registers:\n  EBX: Initial code length to test (1-16 typically)\n  EDI: Bits currently available in MM1 buffer\n  ESI: Pointer to current position in input bytestream\n  EBP: Frame pointer accessing decoder state at -0x4, -0xc, -0x10, -0x14, -0x1c\n  MM1: 64-bit bit buffer containing upcoming bits (MSB-first)\n  MM4: Constant 0x40 (64) for shift calculations\n\nReturns:\n  Success: Decoded symbol value (sign-extended from short to int)\n  Error: Returns 1 if stream exhausted or refill fails\n  High 32-bits: Preserved dwUnused value\n\nStructure Layout (HuffmanDecodeTable):\n  Offset   Size    Field           Type        Description\n  0x000    0x408   abReserved      byte[1032]  Reserved/padding\n  0x408    0x200   awSymbolValues  short[256]  Decoded symbol values\n  0x608    0x22    awCodeBase      short[17]   Base code value per length\n  0x62a    0x22    awMaxCode       ushort[17]  Maximum code per length\n  0x64e    0x22    awSymbolOffset  short[17]   Symbol index offset per length\n\nNotes:\n  - Uses BSWAP for big-endian to little-endian byte conversion\n  - PCMPEQB with 0xFF bytes detects JPEG marker sequences\n  - MMX register MM4 holds constant 64 for bit position math",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:c14bb55a350c60eb669927eb11880bd3a54129bf9029944443f3bc36edfd521c",
