      "name": "DecodeAcCoefficientsBlock",
      "signature": "undefined DecodeAcCoefficientsBlock(ulonglong * param_1, int param_2, int param_3, uint * param_4, undefined8 * param_5, undefined4 * param_6)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Decodes AC coefficients from a JPEG bitstream into an 8x8 DCT block.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save bitstream state for potential restoration on error\n2. Clear output block (128 bytes = 64 shorts for 8x8 block)\n3. Load MMX constants for dequantization (scale mask, base offset, rounding)\n4. Decode DC coefficient difference using DC Huffman table\n5. Apply Huffman run-length decoding for each AC coefficient:\n   a. Read top 8 bits as Huffman lookup index\n   b. Extract run-length (upper 4 bits) and code length (lower 4 bits)\n   c. Refill bit buffer if fewer than 8 bits remain (call FUN_6001645a)\n   d. Decode coefficient value using magnitude and sign extension\n6. Dequantize each coefficient using PMADDWD multiply-add instruction\n7. Store coefficient at zigzag-reordered position in output block\n8. Repeat until 64 coefficients decoded or EOB marker encountered\n9. Restore bitstream state and finalize via FUN_600165ce\n\nParameters:\n  pBitstream: Pointer to bitstream state structure (contains bit buffer, position, flags)\n              Offset 0x00: 64-bit bit buffer (qword)\n              Offset 0x0C: Bits remaining count (dword)\n              Offset 0x10: Stream position (qword)\n              Offset 0x1C: State field 1 (dword)\n              Offset 0x24: State field 2 (dword)\n              Offset 0x30: Marker byte (byte)\n  nDcHuffmanTable: Pointer to DC Huffman decode table (base + 8 = lookup array)\n  nAcHuffmanTable: Pointer to AC Huffman decode table (base + 8 = lookup array)\n  pnDcCoefficient: Pointer to DC coefficient accumulator (differential coding)\n  pawOutputBlock: Pointer to 64-element short array for dequantized coefficients\n  pdwQuantTable: Pointer to quantization table entries\n\nReturns:\n  void - Results written to pawOutputBlock and bitstream state updated\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - EOB (End of Block): AC run with 0xF0 code signals 16 zero runs\n  - ZRL (Zero Run Length): Run count in upper 4 bits of AC symbol\n  - Bit buffer refill: FUN_6001645a called when < 8 bits remain\n  - Error condition: On decode failure, state restored and early exit\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x40 (64): Number of DCT coefficients in 8x8 block\n  0x38 (56): Bit shift for top 8 bits of 64-bit buffer\n  0xFFFF: Huffman code threshold for slow-path decoding\n  0xF0: EOB marker with 16 zero-run extension\n  0x3F (63): Maximum coefficient index (0-63)\n  0x10000: Threshold for valid Huffman lookup vs slow decode\n  >> 7: Division by 128 for dequantization rounding",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:7cfe2618c6fa3b65cc04217fb714ae15d49ab15b304e5eee855aadc55051fa93",
