      "name": "RefillBitBufferSlow",
      "signature": "undefined4 RefillBitBufferSlow(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Refills the 64-bit MMX bit buffer using slow byte-by-byte path with JPEG marker handling.\n\nCalled when the fast 4-byte read path cannot be used (fewer than 4 bytes available or\n0xFF marker bytes detected). Reads bytes one at a time from the input stream, handling\nJPEG byte stuffing where 0xFF followed by 0x00 represents a literal 0xFF data byte.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if marker byte already stored from previous escape sequence\n  2. If no saved marker, enter byte reading loop:\n     a. If buffer exhausted, call RefillStreamBufferFromFile to reload\n     b. Read next byte from input stream (ESI pointer)\n     c. If byte is 0xFF, enter marker handling:\n        - Read following byte\n        - If 0x00, treat 0xFF as data (stuffed byte)\n        - If non-zero, save as marker byte and exit loop\n     d. Shift byte into MM1 bit buffer, increment bit position by 8\n  3. Continue until bit position exceeds 56 (0x38) or marker found\n  4. Update bytes remaining counter and return success\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT unaff_EBP - Parent stack frame pointer\n    [EBP+0x08] - Pointer to BitstreamContext structure\n    [EBP-0x08] - Bytes remaining in input buffer (dword)\n    [EBP-0x10] - Saved marker byte from escape sequence (byte)\n    [EBP-0x14] - Stream position counter (dword)\n  IMPLICIT unaff_ESI - Current position in input buffer (byte*)\n  IMPLICIT unaff_EDI - Current bit position in MM1 buffer (0-56)\n  IMPLICIT in_MM1    - 64-bit bit buffer accumulator\n  IMPLICIT in_MM4    - Constant 64 (0x40) for bit calculations\n\nReturns:\n  0xFF (255) - Success, bit buffer refilled with data\n  0x00 (0)   - End of stream or error from buffer refill\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xFF  - JPEG marker prefix byte requiring special handling\n  0x00  - Stuffed zero byte following 0xFF (escape sequence)\n  0x08  - Bits per byte for shift operations\n  0x38  - Maximum bit position (56) before buffer considered full\n  0x39  - Bit position threshold (57) for loop exit condition\n\nBitstreamContext Structure (at [EBP+0x08]):\n  Offset  Size  Field              Description\n  +0x10   4     pbWritePos         Current buffer position pointer\n  +0x20   4     dwReserved20       Bytes remaining in buffer\n  +0x38   4     dwReserved38       File handle validity flag\n\nRelated Functions:\n  RefillStreamBufferFromFile - Reloads buffer from file when exhausted\n  DecodeHuffmanCodeSlow      - Primary caller during Huffman decoding\n  DecodeAcCoefficientsBlock  - Caller during AC coefficient decoding",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
