      "name": "DecodeHuffmanCodeSlow",
      "signature": "longlong DecodeHuffmanCodeSlow(undefined4 param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "longlong",
      "comment": "Decodes a Huffman code using the slow bit-by-bit path when fast lookup fails.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if enough bits remain in buffer (EDI vs EBX), refill if needed via FUN_6001645a\n2. Calculate remaining bits count and extract initial code value from MM1/MM4\n3. Loop: compare extracted code against threshold table at [EBP-4]+0x62A\n4. If code <= threshold and code length < 17, perform table lookup:\n   a. Subtract base offset from table at [EBP-4]+0x608\n   b. Add symbol index offset from table at [EBP-4]+0x64E\n   c. Return decoded symbol from table at [EBP-4]+0x408\n5. If code > threshold, shift in next bit and increment code length\n6. If bits exhausted mid-decode, refill and continue\n7. On refill failure or invalid code length (>=17), return error\n\nParameters:\n  nBitsRemaining (ECX): Number of bits remaining in bit buffer (from caller's EDI)\n  dwBitBuffer (EDX): Current bit buffer state (passed through to return)\n  IMPLICIT EBX: Current code length being tested\n  IMPLICIT EDI: Bits remaining count in caller's context\n  IMPLICIT MM1: 64-bit bit buffer containing bitstream data\n  IMPLICIT MM4: Bit position offset constant (64)\n  IMPLICIT [EBP-4]: Pointer to Huffman decode table structure\n  IMPLICIT [EBP-0x1C]: Storage for code length during iteration\n\nReturns:\n  longlong (EDX:EAX packed):\n    Success: EDX = original dwBitBuffer, EAX = decoded Huffman symbol (signed short)\n    Invalid: EDX = dwBitBuffer, EAX = 0 (code length >= 17)\n    Error: EDX = dwBitBuffer, EAX = 1 (bit buffer refill failed)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Code length >= 17 (0x11): Invalid Huffman code, returns 0\n  - Refill failure: Returns 1 to signal decode error\n  - Uses MMX registers for 64-bit bit buffer manipulation\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x408: Symbol lookup table offset in Huffman structure\n  0x608: Base offset table for code length\n  0x62A: Threshold table for code length comparison\n  0x64E: Symbol index offset table\n  0x11 (17): Maximum valid Huffman code length\n  0x3F: Bit shift for extracting top bit from 64-bit buffer",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
