      "name": "DequantizeDctBlockMMX",
      "signature": "undefined DequantizeDctBlockMMX(undefined8 * param_1, undefined8 * param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Dequantizes a complete 8x8 DCT coefficient block using MMX SIMD instructions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize MMX constant registers (bias, saturation, rounding, correction)\n2. For each of 8 rows (processed in pairs of 4 shorts = 64 bits):\n   a. Load coefficient pair from pnDctCoeffs[row]\n   b. Load quantization value pair from pnQuantTable[row]\n   c. Apply signed saturation clamping using bias/unsigned saturation trick\n   d. Scale coefficients left by 2 (PSLLW x2)\n   e. Multiply by quantization values (PMULHW - high word of 16x16->32)\n   f. Add rounding bias (0x0001) and shift right by 1 (PSRAW 1)\n   g. Store dequantized result back to pnDctCoeffs[row]\n3. Process rows 7->0 in descending order for cache efficiency\n\nParameters:\npnDctCoeffs - Pointer to 64-element short array (8x8 DCT block, 128 bytes)\n              Input: quantized coefficients; Output: dequantized coefficients\npnQuantTable - Pointer to 64-element short array (quantization matrix, 128 bytes)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Results written in-place to pnDctCoeffs\n\nLocal Variables (MMX Registers):\nllMmxCoeffsHigh - Coefficient pair high half (MM0)\nllMmxCoeffsLow - Coefficient pair low half (MM2)\nllMmxQuantHigh - Quantization pair high half (MM0)\nllMmxQuantLow - Quantization pair low half (MM0)\nllMmxSaturated0 - Saturated values pair 0 (MM2)\nllMmxSaturated1 - Saturated values pair 1 (MM2)\nllMmxScaledHigh - Scaled values high (MM0)\nllMmxScaledLow - Scaled values low (MM2)\nllMmxResultHigh - Result high half (MM0)\nllMmxResultLow - Result low half (MM0)\nllMmxRoundedHigh - Rounded result high (MM2)\nllMmxRoundedLow - Rounded result low (MM2)\n\nStack Constants (ulonglong, assembly-only):\nqwBias [EBP-0x10] - 0x8000800080008000 (signed-to-unsigned bias)\nqwSaturateLow [EBP-0x28] - 0x6000600060006000 (low clamp threshold)\nqwSaturateHigh [EBP-0x18] - 0xC000C000C000C000 (high clamp threshold)\nqwCorrection [EBP-0x08] - 0xE000E000E000E000 (saturation correction)\nqwRounding [EBP-0x20] - 0x0001000100010001 (rounding bias)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x80008000 - Bias constant for signed-to-unsigned conversion (4 packed 0x8000)\n0x60006000 - Low saturation threshold (packed 0x6000)\n0xC000C000 - High saturation threshold (packed 0xC000)\n0xE000E000 - Correction constant after saturation (packed 0xE000)\n0x00010001 - Rounding bias (packed 0x0001)\n\nStructure Layout (8x8 block, row-major, 16 bytes/row):\nOffset | Size | Field     | Description\n0x00   | 16   | Row 0     | DC coefficient + 7 AC coefficients\n0x10   | 16   | Row 1     | 8 AC coefficients (low frequency)\n0x20   | 16   | Row 2     | 8 AC coefficients\n0x30   | 16   | Row 3     | 8 AC coefficients\n0x40   | 16   | Row 4     | 8 AC coefficients\n0x50   | 16   | Row 5     | 8 AC coefficients\n0x60   | 16   | Row 6     | 8 AC coefficients\n0x70   | 16   | Row 7     | 8 AC coefficients (high frequency)\n\nNotes:\n- Uses signed saturation via unsigned saturation trick: add 0x8000 bias,\n  use PADDUSW/PSUBUSW for clamping, then subtract correction\n- PMULHW returns high 16 bits of 16x16 multiply, effectively dividing by 65536\n- Pre-shift left by 2 compensates for quantization table scaling\n- Rounding bias (+1) before right shift implements proper rounding vs truncation\n- Stack constants are phantom variables (assembly-only, not in decompiled view)",
