      "name": "StoreHighWordCoefficientAndIncrementRunLength",
      "signature": "void StoreHighWordCoefficientAndIncrementRunLength(uint dwUnused, int nRunLengthCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Stores a high-word coefficient value and increments the run-length counter.\n\nThis is a code fragment jumped to from sparse coefficient encoding routines.\nIt extracts the high 16 bits from EBX (the packed coefficient value), stores\nit to the output buffer, increments the run-length count, and advances the\ncoefficient pointer before tail-calling the finalization routine.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current coefficient pointer from caller's stack frame [EBP-0x3C]\n2. Set encoding state to 2 at [EBP-0x38]\n3. Extract high word: dwCoefficient = EBX >> 16\n4. Store coefficient to output buffer at [ESI]\n5. Store incremented run length (nRunLengthCount + 1) at [ESI + 0x100]\n6. Advance coefficient pointer by 4 bytes\n7. Jump to FinalizeCoefficientStorageAndComputeRunLengths\n\nParameters:\n  dwUnused (ECX): Unused in this fragment, passed for thunk signature compatibility\n  nRunLengthCount (EDX): Current run-length count, incremented and stored\n  IMPLICIT EBX: Packed coefficient value, high word extracted via SHR 16\n  IMPLICIT ESI: Pointer to coefficient output buffer\n  IMPLICIT [EBP-0x3C]: Pointer to end of coefficient buffer (caller's stack)\n  IMPLICIT [EBP-0x38]: Encoding state variable (set to 2)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Tail calls FinalizeCoefficientStorageAndComputeRunLengths\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x10 (16) - Bit shift to extract high word from packed coefficient\n  0x100 (256) - Offset to run-length storage within output structure\n  0x4 - Coefficient pointer increment (sizeof DWORD)\n  2 - Encoding state value indicating high-word storage path",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
