      "name": "StoreTwoCoefficientsState2AndFinalize",
      "signature": "undefined StoreTwoCoefficientsState2AndFinalize(undefined4 param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Stores two DCT coefficients with state=2 and finalizes coefficient encoding.\n\nThis is a jump target (not called directly) that is part of the sparse coefficient\nencoding state machine for JPEG DCT compression. It handles the case where exactly\ntwo non-zero coefficients remain to be stored.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set final encoding state to 2 at caller's [EBP-0x38] (indicates 2 coefficients stored)\n2. Load current coefficient buffer end offset from caller's [EBP-0x3C]\n3. Store packed coefficient value (EDX/param_2) to buffer at [ESI+0x100] (run-length slot)\n4. Clear upper run-length slot at [ESI+0x104] to 0\n5. Split EBX coefficient pair into low word at [ESI] and high word at [ESI+4]\n6. Advance coefficient buffer end offset by 8 bytes (2 coefficients * 4 bytes each)\n7. Jump to FinalizeCoefficientStorageAndComputeRunLengths for run-length bit counting\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT pCoefficientBuffer (ECX): Not used directly - buffer passed via caller's ESI\n  dwPackedCoefficients (EDX): Packed coefficient value to store at run-length slot\n  IMPLICIT unaff_EBX: Contains two 16-bit coefficients packed as low:high words\n  IMPLICIT unaff_ESI: Pointer to coefficient storage buffer structure\n  IMPLICIT [EBP-0x38]: Caller's final state output location\n  IMPLICIT [EBP-0x3C]: Caller's coefficient buffer end offset\n\nReturns:\n  void - Does not return to caller; continues via JMP to finalization epilogue.\n  Outputs are written to caller's stack frame and coefficient buffer.\n\nStructure Layout (Coefficient Buffer at ESI):\n  Offset  Size  Field              Description\n  0x000   4     dwCoeffLo          Low 16-bit coefficient (sign-extended to 32-bit)\n  0x004   4     dwCoeffHi          High 16-bit coefficient (sign-extended to 32-bit)\n  0x100   4     dwRunLengthValue   Run-length encoded coefficient value\n  0x104   4     dwRunLengthExtra   Additional run-length data (cleared to 0)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  2 - State value indicating two coefficients stored\n  8 - Byte advancement for two 32-bit coefficient entries\n  0x100 (256) - Offset to run-length value slot in buffer\n  0x104 (260) - Offset to run-length extra data slot\n  0x10 (16) - Bit shift to extract high word from packed pair",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
