      "name": "StoreSparseCoefficientsState3",
      "signature": "void StoreSparseCoefficientsState3(int nCoefficient0, int nCoefficient1)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Stores two sparse DCT coefficients and sets encoding state 3.\n\nThis function is a jumptable target for sparse coefficient encoding. It is called\nindirectly from the sparse_encoding_jump_table when processing DCT coefficients\nthat require state 3 encoding (two non-zero coefficients in a group of 4).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set encoding state to 3 at [EBP-0x38] indicating two-coefficient pattern\n2. Load current coefficient buffer pointer from [EBP-0x3C]\n3. Store first coefficient (EBX) to output buffer at [ESI]\n4. Store second coefficient (EDX) to output buffer at [ESI+0x100]\n5. Advance coefficient pointer by 4 bytes\n6. Update pointer at [EBP-0x3C] with new position\n7. Jump to FinalizeCoefficientStorageAndComputeRunLengths for completion\n\nParameters:\n  nCoefficient0 (ECX): First DCT coefficient value (passed via EBX at store)\n  nCoefficient1 (EDX): Second DCT coefficient value for offset 0x100\n\nIMPLICIT Register Inputs:\n  EBX: Contains actual first coefficient value to store\n  ESI: Pointer to coefficient output buffer\n  EBP: Caller's frame pointer for accessing stack variables\n\nIMPLICIT Stack Frame (via caller's EBP):\n  [EBP-0x38]: dwFinalState - Encoding state value (set to 3)\n  [EBP-0x3C]: pCoefficientEnd - Pointer tracking coefficient buffer position\n\nReturns:\n  void - Does not return; jumps to FinalizeCoefficientStorageAndComputeRunLengths\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x3 - Encoding state indicating two non-zero coefficients in group\n  0x4 - Byte increment for coefficient pointer advancement\n  0x100 - Offset between first and second coefficient storage (256 bytes)\n\nNote: This is part of the Intel JPEG Library (IJL) DCT coefficient encoding\nsystem. State 3 represents the case where exactly 2 of 4 coefficients in a\nprocessing group are non-zero.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
