      "name": "InitSingleCoefficientBlock",
      "signature": "undefined InitSingleCoefficientBlock(uint param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes a single DCT coefficient block and jumps to finalization routine.\n\nThis function is entered via JMP from coefficient encoding routines when a single\ncoefficient block needs to be stored. It sets up the coefficient storage structure\nand then jumps to FinalizeCoefficientStorageAndComputeRunLengths for processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear the run-length flag at offset 0x104 in coefficient buffer (pBuffer[0x41] = 0)\n2. Store packed coefficient value to buffer slot 1 (pBuffer[1] = dwPackedCoefficient)\n3. Increment coefficient index and store to count field (pBuffer[0x40] = nCoefficientIndex + 1)\n4. Extract high 16 bits from caller's EBX and store to buffer slot 0\n5. Set processing flag at [EBP-0x38] to 1 (indicates single coefficient mode)\n6. Advance coefficient end pointer by 8 bytes ([EBP-0x3c] += 8)\n7. Jump to FinalizeCoefficientStorageAndComputeRunLengths for run-length computation\n\nParameters:\n  dwPackedCoefficient (ECX): Packed DCT coefficient value (lower 32 bits)\n  nCoefficientIndex (EDX): Current coefficient index in the encoding sequence\n  IMPLICIT EBX: Contains high coefficient data; upper 16 bits extracted and stored\n  IMPLICIT ESI: Pointer to coefficient storage buffer structure\n  IMPLICIT EBP: Caller's stack frame base; used to access shared stack variables\n\nReturns:\n  void - Control transfers to FinalizeCoefficientStorageAndComputeRunLengths via JMP\n\nStructure Layout (ESI points to coefficient buffer):\n  Offset  Size  Field              Description\n  0x000   4     dwHighCoefficient  Upper 16 bits of packed coefficient (from EBX >> 16)\n  0x004   4     dwPackedCoeff      Packed coefficient value (param_1)\n  0x100   4     dwCoefficientCount Coefficient index + 1\n  0x104   4     dwRunLengthFlag    Run-length encoding flag (cleared to 0)\n\nStack Frame Usage (via caller's EBP):\n  [EBP-0x38]: Processing mode flag (set to 1 for single coefficient)\n  [EBP-0x3c]: Coefficient buffer end pointer (advanced by 8)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
