      "name": "InitializeFourCoefficientStorage",
      "signature": "undefined InitializeFourCoefficientStorage(uint param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes coefficient storage for a group of 4 non-zero DCT coefficients.\n\nThis is an entry point jumped to from the sparse coefficient encoding switch table\nwhen exactly 4 coefficients in a group are non-zero. It populates the coefficient\nstorage structure and then falls through to FinalizeCoefficientStorageAndComputeRunLengths.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save EDI = EBX (preserves packed coefficient 0/1 value)\n2. Set state flag [EBP-0x38] = 1 (indicates coefficients stored)\n3. Advance coefficient end pointer [EBP-0x3c] by 12 bytes\n4. Initialize bit count fields in structure to zero:\n   - [ESI+0x108] = 0 (bit count slot 3)\n   - [ESI+0x104] = 0 (bit count slot 2)\n5. Store coefficient values to structure:\n   - [ESI+0x100] = EDX (dwCoeff3, param_2)\n   - [ESI+0x008] = ECX (dwPackedCoeff2, param_1)\n   - [ESI+0x004] = EBX >> 16 (coefficient 1, high word)\n   - [ESI+0x000] = EDI (coefficient 0, low word from EBX)\n6. Jump to shared finalization at FinalizeCoefficientStorageAndComputeRunLengths\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT EBX dwPackedCoeffs01: Packed coefficients 0 and 1 (low/high words)\n  IMPLICIT ESI pCoefficientStorage: Pointer to coefficient storage structure\n  IMPLICIT EBP pCallerFrame: Caller's stack frame for state access\n  dwPackedCoeff2 (ECX): Third coefficient value\n  dwCoeff3 (EDX): Fourth coefficient value\n\nReturns:\n  void - Execution continues at FinalizeCoefficientStorageAndComputeRunLengths\n\nStructure Layout (ESI-relative):\n  Offset  Size  Field              Description\n  0x000   4     dwCoeff0           First coefficient (low word of packed)\n  0x004   4     dwCoeff1           Second coefficient (high word >> 16)\n  0x008   4     dwCoeff2           Third coefficient (param_1/ECX)\n  0x100   4     dwCoeff3           Fourth coefficient (param_2/EDX)\n  0x104   4     dwBitCount2        Bit count for coefficient 2 (init 0)\n  0x108   4     dwBitCount3        Bit count for coefficient 3 (init 0)\n\nNote: This function has no return instruction; it ends with JMP to shared epilogue.",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:9f9d1cc6d7e95d844cd9b505fea58dedb141ac1ddd014bbe5eaecc797ce4a373",
