      "name": "StorePackedCoefficientAndAdvance",
      "signature": "void StorePackedCoefficientAndAdvance(uint dwPackedValue, int nStorageOffset)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Stores a packed DCT coefficient and advances the storage pointer.\n\nThis is a shared code block entered via JMP from coefficient encoding functions.\nIt handles the case where a non-zero coefficient value needs to be stored during\nsparse JPEG-style DCT coefficient encoding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current coefficient end pointer from caller's stack frame [EBP-0x3C]\n2. Clear the encoding state at [EBP-0x38] to zero (reset for next iteration)\n3. Store adjusted offset (nStorageOffset + 3) to coefficient storage at [ESI+0x100]\n4. Extract high 16 bits of packed value (dwPackedValue >> 16) and store at [ESI]\n5. Advance coefficient end pointer by 4 bytes\n6. Jump to FinalizeCoefficientStorageAndComputeRunLengths for final processing\n\nParameters:\n  dwPackedValue (ECX): Packed coefficient data; high 16 bits contain the value to store\n  nStorageOffset (EDX): Base storage offset; +3 adjustment applied before storing\n  IMPLICIT [EBP-0x3C] pCoefficientEnd: Pointer to end of coefficient buffer (caller's stack)\n  IMPLICIT [EBP-0x38] dwEncodingState: Encoding state value (cleared to 0)\n  IMPLICIT ESI pCoefficientStorage: Pointer to coefficient storage structure\n\nReturns:\n  void - Control transfers to FinalizeCoefficientStorageAndComputeRunLengths\n\nStructure Layout (ESI points to):\n  Offset  Size  Field               Description\n  0x000   4     dwCoefficientValue  Extracted coefficient (high 16 bits of input)\n  0x100   4     dwStorageOffset     Adjusted offset value (input + 3)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x10 (16) - Bit shift to extract high 16 bits from packed DWORD\n  3 - Offset adjustment for storage alignment\n  4 - Coefficient pointer advancement size (one DWORD)\n  0x40 - Array index for storage offset (0x100 / 4 = 64)\n\nNote: This function accesses caller's stack frame via unaffected EBP register.\nAll stack-relative accesses use the caller's frame, not a local frame.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:9e9990fbdde4bf52dc7bb40ed027c87bacef6392370a35b84a4ca2c5addf0d14",
