      "name": "StoreTwoCoefficientsAndFinalize",
      "signature": "undefined StoreTwoCoefficientsAndFinalize(uint param_1, undefined4 param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Stores two DCT coefficients and finalizes encoding block processing.\n\nThis is a specialized entry point for storing exactly 2 coefficients extracted from\na packed value. It is called via thunk from the main encoding loop when the current\nblock contains 2 non-zero coefficients that need to be stored.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract high 16 bits from dwPackedCoefficient (SHR ECX, 0x10)\n2. Store first coefficient (from EBX register) at pdwCoefficientStorage[0]\n3. Store extracted high word at pdwCoefficientStorage[1]\n4. Store coefficient mask at pdwCoefficientStorage[0x40] (metadata offset 0x100)\n5. Store coefficient count (2) at pdwCoefficientStorage[0x41] (offset 0x104)\n6. Advance buffer end pointer by 8 bytes (2 coefficients * 4 bytes each)\n7. Clear final state value to 0\n8. Jump to FinalizeCoefficientStorageAndComputeRunLengths for run-length encoding\n\nParameters:\n  dwPackedCoefficient (ECX): Packed 32-bit value; high 16 bits contain second coefficient\n  dwCoefficientMask (EDX): Bit mask indicating which coefficient positions are non-zero\n  IMPLICIT pdwCoefficientStorage (ESI): Pointer to coefficient storage structure\n  IMPLICIT dwFirstCoefficient (EBX): First coefficient value to store\n  IMPLICIT nCallerEBP (EBP): Caller's stack frame base for accessing stack variables\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; jumps directly to finalization routine\n\nStructure Layout (pdwCoefficientStorage):\n  Offset   Size   Field           Description\n  0x000    4      dwCoeff0        First coefficient value (from EBX)\n  0x004    4      dwCoeff1        Second coefficient (high 16 bits of ECX)\n  0x100    4      dwMask          Coefficient position mask\n  0x104    4      dwCount         Number of coefficients stored (always 2)\n\nStack Frame Variables (caller's EBP-relative):\n  [EBP-0x3C]  pBufferEnd    Pointer to end of coefficient buffer (advanced by 8)\n  [EBP-0x38]  dwFinalState  Final encoding state (cleared to 0)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x10   - Bit shift to extract high 16 bits from packed value\n  0x40   - DWORD index for mask field (0x40 * 4 = 0x100 bytes)\n  0x41   - DWORD index for count field (0x41 * 4 = 0x104 bytes)\n  8      - Buffer advancement in bytes (2 coefficients * 4 bytes)\n  2      - Fixed coefficient count for this variant",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
