      "name": "StoreFourPackedCoefficientsAndFinalize",
      "signature": "undefined StoreFourPackedCoefficientsAndFinalize(uint param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Stores four packed DCT coefficients and jumps to finalization routine.\n\nThis is a shared epilogue block jumped to from coefficient encoding functions. It unpacks\nfour 16-bit coefficient values from packed 32-bit registers and stores them into a coefficient\nblock structure, then continues to the finalization routine.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract high word from dwPackedCoeff01 (param_1 >> 16) -> coefficient 2\n2. Extract low word from dwPackedCoeff45 (EBX) -> coefficient 0\n3. Extract high word from dwPackedCoeff45 (EBX >> 16) -> coefficient 1\n4. Store dwPackedCoeff23 (param_2) to run-length table offset [0x100]\n5. Initialize run-length flags at offsets [0x104] and [0x108]\n6. Advance coefficient end pointer by 12 bytes (3 DWORDs)\n7. Clear final state flag at [EBP-0x38]\n8. Jump to FinalizeCoefficientStorageAndComputeRunLengths\n\nParameters:\n  dwPackedCoeff01 (ECX): Packed coefficients 0-1 (low word: coeff0, high word: coeff1)\n  dwPackedCoeff23 (EDX): Packed coefficients 2-3 stored to run-length table\n  IMPLICIT dwPackedCoeff45 (EBX): Packed coefficients from caller\n  IMPLICIT pCoefficientBlock (ESI): Pointer to coefficient storage structure\n  IMPLICIT nCallerEBP (EBP): Caller's frame pointer for stack variable access\n  IMPLICIT [EBP-0x3C]: Pointer to coefficient end position\n  IMPLICIT [EBP-0x38]: Final encoding state flag\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value. Control flows to FinalizeCoefficientStorageAndComputeRunLengths.\n\nStructure Layout (pCoefficientBlock via ESI):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Description\n  0x000   4     dwCoeff0        First coefficient (low word of EBX)\n  0x004   4     dwCoeff1        Second coefficient (high word of EBX)\n  0x008   4     dwCoeff2        Third coefficient (high word of ECX)\n  0x100   4     dwRunLength0    Run-length table entry 0 (from EDX)\n  0x104   4     dwRunLength1    Run-length flag 1 (set to 0)\n  0x108   4     dwRunLength2    Run-length flag 2 (set to 1)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x0C (12)  - Size of 3 coefficient DWORDs to advance pointer\n  0x100      - Offset to run-length table in coefficient block (256 bytes)\n  0x104      - Offset to run-length flag 1\n  0x108      - Offset to run-length flag 2",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
