      "name": "StoreSingleCoefficientEntry",
      "signature": "undefined StoreSingleCoefficientEntry(uint param_1, undefined4 param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Stores a single DCT coefficient entry into the coefficient buffer and calls finalization.\n\nThis is a shared code block entered via JMP from multiple coefficient encoding paths.\nIt stores one coefficient entry (12 bytes) into the coefficient buffer structure and\nthen jumps to FinalizeCoefficientStorageAndComputeRunLengths for final processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear final encoding state at [EBP-0x38] to 0\n2. Read current buffer end pointer from [EBP-0x3C]\n3. Store previous coefficient (from EBX) at buffer[0x00]\n4. Store packed coefficient value (param_1) at buffer[0x04]\n5. Store encoding state (param_2) at buffer[0x100]\n6. Set entry valid flag at buffer[0x104] to 1\n7. Store high word of packed coefficient at buffer[0x08]\n8. Clear buffer[0x108] to 0\n9. Advance buffer pointer by 12 bytes (0x0C)\n10. Jump to FinalizeCoefficientStorageAndComputeRunLengths\n\nParameters:\n  dwPackedCoefficient (ECX): Packed 32-bit coefficient with value in low 16 bits\n                             and extended info in high 16 bits\n  dwEncodingState (EDX): Encoding state/flags for this coefficient entry\n  IMPLICIT EBX: Previous coefficient value from prior encoding step\n  IMPLICIT ESI: Pointer to coefficient buffer structure\n  IMPLICIT [EBP-0x38]: Final encoding state output location\n  IMPLICIT [EBP-0x3C]: Current buffer write position\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; continues to FinalizeCoefficientStorageAndComputeRunLengths\n\nCoefficient Buffer Structure Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field         Description\n  0x000   4     dwPrevCoeff   Previous coefficient (from EBX)\n  0x004   4     dwPackedVal   Packed coefficient value (param_1)\n  0x008   4     wHighWord     High word of packed coefficient\n  0x100   4     dwState       Encoding state (param_2)\n  0x104   4     dwValid       Entry valid flag (always 1)\n  0x108   4     dwReserved    Reserved/padding (always 0)\n\nNote: Entry size is 12 bytes (0x0C). The 0x100 offset indicates the encoding\nstate is stored in a parallel array 256 bytes (64 entries * 4 bytes) ahead.",
