      "name": "StoreThreeCoeffsAndFinalize",
      "signature": "undefined StoreThreeCoeffsAndFinalize(uint param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Stores three DCT coefficients to the sparse coefficient buffer and finalizes.\n\nThis is a case handler for the sparse coefficient encoding jump table, handling\nthe scenario where exactly 3 non-zero coefficients are found in the current\nprocessing window.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract high word from EBX (third coefficient) and store to output[0]\n2. Store full param_1 (dwPackedCoeffs01) to output[1]\n3. Extract high word from param_1 and store to output[2]\n4. Set run-length count at output[0x40] to (nZeroRunCount + 1)\n5. Clear zero-count fields at output[0x41] and output[0x42]\n6. Advance coefficient buffer pointer by 12 bytes (3 DWORDs)\n7. Clear state variable at [EBP-0x38]\n8. Jump to FinalizeCoefficientStorageAndComputeRunLengths\n\nParameters:\n  dwPackedCoeffs01 (ECX): Packed coefficients - low word is coeff[1], high word is coeff[2]\n  nZeroRunCount (EDX): Number of preceding zero coefficients in the run\n  IMPLICIT EBX: Contains third coefficient in high word (coeff[0])\n  IMPLICIT ESI: Pointer to output coefficient structure (264 bytes per entry)\n  IMPLICIT EBP: Caller's stack frame base pointer\n\nReturns:\n  void - Falls through to FinalizeCoefficientStorageAndComputeRunLengths\n\nStructure Layout (output at ESI):\n  Offset  Size  Field              Description\n  0x000   4     dwCoeff0           Third coefficient (from EBX >> 16)\n  0x004   4     dwCoeff1           First coefficient (from ECX low word)\n  0x008   4     dwCoeff2           Second coefficient (from ECX >> 16)\n  0x100   4     dwRunLengthCount   Run-length count (nZeroRunCount + 1)\n  0x104   4     dwZeroCount1       Zero count field 1 (cleared to 0)\n  0x108   4     dwZeroCount2       Zero count field 2 (cleared to 0)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xC (12) - Structure stride for 3 coefficients (3 * 4 bytes)\n  0x100 (256) - Offset to run-length count field\n  0x104 (260) - Offset to first zero count field\n  0x108 (264) - Offset to second zero count field\n\nNote: This function has no formal prologue as it is entered via JMP from the\nsparse coefficient encoding jump table. All stack frame access uses caller's EBP.",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
