      "name": "FinalizeCoefficientStorageAndComputeRunLengths",
      "signature": "undefined FinalizeCoefficientStorageAndComputeRunLengths(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Finalizes DCT coefficient storage and computes run-length encoding bit counts.\n\nThis is a shared epilogue block jumped to from multiple coefficient encoding\nfunctions (store_all_coefficients variants). It performs the final processing\nstep for JPEG-style DCT coefficient encoding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Decrement loop counter at [EBP-0x4]; if non-zero, jump back to main loop\n2. Calculate coefficient count: (pCoefficientEnd - pCoefficientStart) >> 2\n3. Store coefficient count to output parameter at [EBP+0x18]\n4. For each group of 4 coefficients (16 bytes input -> 8 bytes output):\n   a. Load 4 DWORDs from source, sign-extend to 16-bit via PSLLD/PSRAD\n   b. Pack to 8 signed 16-bit values using PACKSSDW\n   c. Compute absolute values using PXOR/PCMPGTW/PSUBW pattern\n   d. Store absolute values to destination at [EDI]\n   e. Compute bit counts using binary search algorithm:\n      - Compare against thresholds (128, 16, 4, 1)\n      - Accumulate bit positions for each significant bit\n   f. Store accumulated bit counts to [EDI+0x1F8] (run-length table offset)\n5. Store final state to output at [EBP+0x14]\n6. Restore registers and return\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT [EBP-0x04] nLoopCounter: Outer loop iteration count\n  IMPLICIT [EBP-0x0C] qwThreshold128: MMX comparison threshold (128, packed)\n  IMPLICIT [EBP-0x14] qwBitMask2: Bit mask for 2-bit positions\n  IMPLICIT [EBP-0x1C] qwThreshold1: MMX comparison threshold (1, packed)\n  IMPLICIT [EBP-0x24] qwBitMask4: Bit mask for 4-bit positions\n  IMPLICIT [EBP-0x2C] qwThreshold4: MMX comparison threshold (4, packed)\n  IMPLICIT [EBP-0x34] qwBitMask8: Bit mask for 8-bit positions\n  IMPLICIT [EBP-0x38] dwFinalState: Final encoding state value\n  IMPLICIT [EBP-0x3C] pCoefficientEnd: Pointer to end of coefficient buffer\n  IMPLICIT [EBP-0x44] qwThreshold16: MMX comparison threshold (16, packed)\n  IMPLICIT [EBP+0x10] pCoefficientStart: Pointer to start of coefficient buffer\n  IMPLICIT [EBP+0x14] pnStateOutput: Output pointer for final state\n  IMPLICIT [EBP+0x18] pnCountOutput: Output pointer for coefficient count\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value. Outputs are written to caller-provided pointers:\n  - *pnCountOutput receives the coefficient count\n  - *pnStateOutput receives the final encoding state\n\nMMX Register Usage:\n  MM0-MM4: Working registers for coefficient processing\n  MM5-MM6: Bit count accumulation\n  MM7: Zero register / temporary\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1F8 - Offset to run-length bit count table (504 bytes)\n  0xFC - Mask to ensure 4-byte alignment of count\n\nNote: This function has no formal parameters as it is entered via JMP from\ncaller functions that have already set up the stack frame. All data access\nis via caller's EBP-relative addressing.",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
