      "name": "ValidateJpegFrameComponents",
      "signature": "int ValidateJpegFrameComponents(byte * param_1, uint * param_2, int param_3)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Validates JPEG frame component table entries after parsing the frame header.\n\nParses the JPEG frame header (SOF marker) and validates that all components\nhave properly assigned quantization, DC Huffman, and AC Huffman tables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if decode context already initialized (flag at +0x37dc)\n2. Call ParseJpegFrameHeader to parse SOF marker data\n3. Clear marker data status field (dword at offset 0x28)\n4. For each component in frame:\n   a. Validate quantization table pointer exists (offset -0x4)\n   b. Validate DC Huffman table pointer exists (offset 0x0)\n   c. Validate AC Huffman table pointer exists (offset 0x4)\n5. Return 0 on success or error code on failure\n\nParameters:\n  pbMarkerData - Pointer to JPEG marker data buffer, status written at +0x28\n  pFrameInfo - Frame info structure: [0]=component count, [0xd]=component array ptr\n  pDecodeContext - Decode context structure with init flag at +0x37dc\n\nReturns:\n  0 - Success, all component tables validated\n  -0x11 (-17) - Invalid quantization or DC Huffman table assignment\n  -0x12 (-18) - Invalid AC Huffman table assignment\n  -0x13 (-19) - Decode context already initialized\n\nStructure Layout - Component Entry (stride 0x18 = 24 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field              Description\n  -0x04   4     pQuantTable        Quantization table pointer\n  0x00    4     pDcHuffTable       DC Huffman table pointer\n  0x04    4     pAcHuffTable       AC Huffman table pointer\n  0x08    16    (unknown)          Remaining component fields",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:e78aef268796baf8ef18573d4b0b7ea0e99f3fd9f188c8f6684bba61a43857f1",
