      "name": "InitializeQuantizationAndHuffmanTables",
      "signature": "undefined4 InitializeQuantizationAndHuffmanTables(int param_1, undefined4 param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes quantization tables and Huffman encoding tables for JPEG compression.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. For each quantization table (count at pJpegEncoder+0x84):\n   a. Free existing table via AtoiMbcsWrapper if allocated\n   b. Allocate 136-byte (0x88) quantization table via operator_new\n   c. On allocation failure, cleanup partial allocations and return -5\n   d. Call FUN_6001ee70 to compute scaled quantization values\n   e. Call FUN_6001bac0 to write DQT marker segment\n   f. Call FUN_60012290 to process quantization coefficients\n   g. Copy coefficients using zigzag order (g_anZigzagOrder)\n2. Call FUN_6001bb40 to write DHT marker segments\n3. For each Huffman table pair (DC/AC per component):\n   a. Set AC table pointer at offset 0x3704\n   b. Set DC table pointer at offset 0x36f4\n   c. Call FUN_6001ef10 to build AC and DC tables\n\nParameters:\n    pJpegEncoder - Pointer to JPEG encoder context structure\n    pOutputBuffer - Pointer to output buffer for JPEG markers\n\nReturns:\n    0 - Success\n    -5 (0xFFFFFFFB) - Memory allocation failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n    0x88 - Quantization table size (136 bytes)\n    0x40 - DCT coefficients count (64)\n    0x84 - Quant table count offset\n    0x90 - Huffman table count offset\n    0x36e4 - Quant table ptr array offset\n    0x3704 - AC Huffman table ptr array\n    0x36f4 - DC Huffman table ptr array\n    0xce0 - Huffman table stride (3296 bytes)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:0b8e0332c97c7786f0fca1a59294d90463f6653402e4b0cf99ceb815b8d115c4",
