      "name": "InitializeCpuInfo",
      "signature": "undefined InitializeCpuInfo(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes CPU identification information using CPUID instruction.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear CPU vendor string buffer (12 bytes) with spaces\n2. Null-terminate the vendor string\n3. Execute CPUID with EAX=0 to get vendor string (EBX:EDX:ECX)\n4. Store vendor string parts in g_szCpuVendorString (e.g., \"GenuineIntel\")\n5. If CPUID supports function 1, execute CPUID with EAX=1\n6. Extract and store CPU signature fields from returned EAX:\n   - Type (bits 12-13) -> g_dwCpuType\n   - Family (bits 8-11) -> g_dwCpuFamily  \n   - Model (bits 4-7) -> g_dwCpuModel\n   - Stepping (bits 0-3) -> g_dwCpuStepping\n7. Store feature flags from EDX -> g_dwCpuFeatureFlags\n\nParameters:\n  None - This function takes no parameters.\n\nReturns:\n  void - Results stored in global variables.\n\nGlobal Variables Written:\n  g_dwCpuType - CPU type (0-3)\n  g_dwCpuFamily - CPU family (0-15)\n  g_dwCpuModel - CPU model (0-15)\n  g_dwCpuStepping - CPU stepping revision (0-15)\n  g_dwCpuFeatureFlags - CPU feature flags bitmap (EDX from CPUID.1)\n  g_szCpuVendorString[13] - Null-terminated vendor ID string\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x0C (12) - Length of CPU vendor string\n  0x20 (' ') - Space character for clearing buffer\n  0x3FFF - Mask for signature bits (type:family:model:stepping)\n\nError Handling:\n  If CPUID function 1 not supported, CPU info globals remain zero.\n  Exception handler at 0x60017e1d clears all globals on failure.",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
