      "name": "GetCpuInfoPointer",
      "signature": "uint * GetCpuInfoPointer(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined *",
      "comment": "Returns a pointer to the CPU type information global variable.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load address of g_dwCpuType global (0x60028748)\n2. Return pointer to caller\n\nParameters:\n  None - This function takes no parameters.\n\nReturns:\n  uint * - Pointer to g_dwCpuType, the first element of the CPU info globals block.\n           The CPU info block contains sequential DWORDs:\n           +0x00: g_dwCpuType (CPU type, bits 12-13 of CPUID signature)\n           +0x04: g_dwCpuFamily (CPU family, bits 8-11)\n           +0x08: g_dwCpuModel (CPU model, bits 4-7)\n           +0x0C: g_dwCpuStepping (CPU stepping, bits 0-3)\n           +0x10: g_dwCpuFeatureFlags (EDX from CPUID.1)\n\nCallers:\n  DetectCpuCapabilities - Uses to check CPU feature support\n  InitializeMemoryUtilityFunctionPointers - Uses to select optimized memory routines\n\nRelated Functions:\n  InitializeCpuInfo - Populates the CPU info globals via CPUID instruction",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
