      "name": "ValidateCpuCapabilityLevel",
      "signature": "bool ValidateCpuCapabilityLevel(undefined4 param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Validates if a requested CPU capability level is supported by the detected level.\n\nThis function implements a hierarchical capability validation where higher detected\nlevels can satisfy requests for lower levels, with some special handling for levels 2/3.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize result to false (no capability match)\n2. Switch on detected CPU capability level (0-4)\n3. For each level, check if requested level is in the set of supported levels\n4. Level 0: Only supports request 0\n5. Level 1: Supports requests 0, 1\n6. Level 2: Supports requests 0, 1, 2\n7. Level 3: Supports requests 0, 1, 3 (note: 2 not included)\n8. Level 4: Supports requests 0, 1, 2, 3, 4 (all levels)\n9. Return true if requested level is supported, false otherwise\n\nParameters:\n  nDetectedLevel - Detected CPU capability level (0-4)\n  nRequestedLevel - Requested CPU capability level to validate\n\nReturns:\n  true - Requested capability level is supported by detected level\n  false - Requested capability level exceeds detected capabilities, or invalid detected level\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0 = Base/minimum capability\n  1 = Basic extended capability  \n  2 = SSE2 or similar instruction set\n  3 = SSE3 or similar instruction set\n  4 = Full/maximum capability (all features)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:516911adeccef9643a90db1c48c74eaead6e99808f73a9af05d7c90a711b1872",
