      "name": "ReadFileWrapper",
      "signature": "undefined ReadFileWrapper(HANDLE param_1, LPVOID param_2, DWORD param_3, LPDWORD param_4)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Wrapper for Windows ReadFile API with null OVERLAPPED parameter.\n\nSimplifies synchronous file reads by automatically passing NULL for the\nlpOverlapped parameter, making ReadFile behave synchronously.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve parameters from stack (hFile, lpBuffer, dwBytesToRead, pdwBytesRead)\n2. Push NULL as lpOverlapped (5th parameter)\n3. Push remaining parameters and call ReadFile\n4. Return (caller checks pdwBytesRead for actual bytes read)\n\nParameters:\n    hFile (HANDLE): File handle opened with GENERIC_READ access\n    lpBuffer (LPVOID): Destination buffer for data read from file\n    dwBytesToRead (DWORD): Number of bytes to read from file\n    pdwBytesRead (LPDWORD): Output pointer receiving actual bytes read\n\nReturns:\n    void - Does not return ReadFile result; caller must check pdwBytesRead\n\nCallers:\n    FillJpegInputBuffer - JPEG decoding buffer refill\n    RefillStreamBufferFromFile - Stream buffer management\n\nNotes:\n    - Synchronous read only (lpOverlapped = NULL)\n    - Error checking delegated to caller via GetLastError\n    - No EOF detection; caller must compare pdwBytesRead vs dwBytesToRead",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:faa4aae24443ad8d5fc9e2a09f6d4c5d95ee748f337d136c5bd396c7ffcf0c27",
