      "name": "InitializeMemoryUtilityFunctionPointers",
      "signature": "void InitializeMemoryUtilityFunctionPointers(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes global function pointers for memory and timing utilities.\n\nCalled during DLL initialization to set up optimized memory operation function\npointers based on detected CPU capabilities.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetCpuInfoPointer to retrieve CPU feature flags structure\n2. Set g_pfnMemcpy to CopyMemoryBlock function\n3. Set g_pfnAullshr to memory fill routine at 0x60018260\n4. Check CPU flag bit 4 (RDTSC support) at offset 0x10\n5. If RDTSC supported (bit set): use GetTimestampCounter\n6. If RDTSC not supported: use GetZeroTimestamp (returns 0)\n\nParameters:\n   None\n\nReturns:\n   void\n\nGlobals Modified:\n   g_pfnMemcpy (0x600288e0) - Memory copy function pointer\n   g_pfnAullshr (0x600288e4) - Memory fill/shift function pointer  \n   g_pfnGetTimestamp (0x6002894c) - Timestamp counter function pointer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n   0x10 - Offset to CPU feature flags in CPU info structure\n   0x10 - Bit mask for RDTSC instruction support flag\n\nCalled By:\n   FUN_60018160 - Main module initialization dispatcher",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
