      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes the scalar (non-SIMD) decode function pointer table.\n\nPopulates the global function pointer array with scalar implementations\nof video decode procedures. This is the fallback path when SSE/SIMD\ninstructions are not available or not preferred (case 0 in the\ninitialization dispatcher).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set g_pfnIdct8x8 to PerformInverseDiscreteCosineTransform8x8\n2. Set g_pfnIdct4x4 to PerformInverseDiscreteCosineTransform4x4\n3. Initialize 23 decode procedure pointers (g_pfnDecodeProc0..22)\n   with scalar implementation addresses\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nStructure Layout (Function Pointer Table at 0x600288e8):\n  Offset  Size  Field               Description\n  0x00    4     g_pfnIdct8x8        8x8 IDCT function pointer\n  0x04    4     g_pfnIdct4x4        4x4 IDCT function pointer\n  0x08    4     g_pfnDecodeProc0    Decode procedure 0\n  0x0C    4     g_pfnDecodeProc1    Decode procedure 1\n  ...     ...   ...                 (continues through DecodeProc22)\n  0x60    4     g_pfnDecodeProc22   Decode procedure 22\n\nRelated Functions:\n  InitializeSseDecodeFunctionTable - SSE/SIMD variant (case 1)\n  FUN_600184b0 - Alternative variant (case 3)\n  FUN_600185c0 - Alternative variant (case 2)\n  FUN_600186c0 - Alternative variant (case 4)\n\nCalled By:\n  FUN_60018160 - Initialization dispatcher (when CPU check returns 0)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
