      "name": "ijlInit",
      "signature": "undefined4 ijlInit(undefined4 * param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes a JPEG_CORE_PROPERTIES structure for Intel JPEG Library operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set up SEH exception handling frame\n2. Initialize JFIF interchange format structure at offset 0x58 with defaults\n3. Zero-initialize core property fields (image dimensions, color space, subsampling)\n4. Set default subsampling to 4:2:0 mode (values 3 and 2 for H/V factors)\n5. Configure default quality factor to 75 (0x4B)\n6. Initialize 4 component scan parameter slots via loop (offsets 0x36E4-0x3704)\n7. Align 4 component data pointers to 8-byte boundaries via loop\n8. Allocate 64 bytes for quantization tables via operator_new\n9. Return IJL_MEMORY_ERROR (-5) if allocation fails\n10. Zero-initialize 4 quantization table slots (16 bytes each)\n11. Initialize Huffman codec state flags (offset 0x37DC)\n12. Zero-initialize extended codec state fields (offsets 0x37A4-0x4834)\n13. Call InitJpegProcessorDefaults to configure Huffman and quantization tables\n14. Detect CPU capabilities via FUN_60017eb0 and store result\n15. Initialize additional processor state fields (offsets 0x4DD8-0x4DE4)\n16. Return IJL_OK (0) on success\n\nParameters:\n    pProps (JPEG_CORE_PROPERTIES*) - Pointer to JPEG_CORE_PROPERTIES structure (minimum 0x4DE8 bytes)\n\nReturns:\n    int - IJL_OK (0) on success, IJL_MEMORY_ERROR (-5) if memory allocation fails\n\nStructure Layout (JPEG_CORE_PROPERTIES):\n    Offset   Size  Field                Description\n    0x0000   4     dwReserved           Reserved field\n    0x0004   4     dwWidth              Image width\n    0x0008   4     dwHeight             Image height  \n    0x000C   4     dwChannels           Number of color channels\n    0x0010   4     dwBitsPerChannel     Bits per channel\n    0x0014   4     dwSubsampH           Horizontal subsampling (3=4:1:1, 2=4:2:2)\n    0x0018   4     dwSubsampV           Vertical subsampling (2=4:2:0)\n    0x001C   4     dwColorSpace         Color space identifier\n    0x0048   4     dwQualityFactor      JPEG quality 1-100 (default 75)\n    0x004C   4     dwRestartInterval    Restart marker interval\n    0x0050   4     dwJpegSize           JPEG data size in bytes\n    0x0058   128   jfifHeader           JFIF interchange format structure\n    0x37CC   4     pQuantTables         Pointer to allocated quantization tables\n    0x381C   4     dwCpuCapabilities    CPU feature flags from detection\n\nMagic Numbers:\n    0x03 - Default horizontal subsampling factor (4:1:1 mode)\n    0x02 - Default vertical subsampling factor (4:2:0 mode)\n    0x01 - Progressive scan mode enabled\n    0x4B - Default JPEG quality factor (75 decimal)\n    0x40 - Quantization table allocation size (64 bytes)\n    -0x05 - IJL_MEMORY_ERROR return code\n\nError Handling:\n    Returns -5 (IJL_MEMORY_ERROR) if operator_new fails to allocate quantization tables.\n    SEH frame installed for exception safety during initialization.",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
