      "name": "ijlFree",
      "signature": "undefined4 ijlFree(int param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Releases all resources associated with an Intel JPEG Library (IJL) structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Close any open file handle at offset +0x387C of internal structure\n2. Validate state counter at offset +0x3818 is <= 255 (0xFF)\n3. Free scan line buffer at offset +0x3824\n4. Free DIB data buffer at offset +0x4E3C\n5. Free 4 channel buffers in array at offset +0x373C (loop i=0..3)\n6. Free thumbnail buffer at offset +0x4888\n7. Free sub-structure at offset +0x3838 and its nested buffer at +0x34\n8. Clear dimension fields (width, height, etc.) at offsets +0x80 to +0x8C\n\nParameters:\n    pJpegProps (JPEG_CORE_PROPERTIES*): Pointer to IJL JPEG properties structure\n\nReturns:\n    int: IJL error code\n        0 (IJL_OK) - Success, all resources freed\n        -9 (IJL_ERR_FILE_CLOSE) - Failed to close file handle\n        -8 (IJL_ERR_DATA) - Invalid state (counter > 255)\n\nError Handling:\n    Uses SEH exception handling with scope table at g_adwIjlFreeSehScopeTable\n    All free operations check for NULL before calling AtoiMbcsWrapper (free)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n    0xFF (255) - Maximum valid state counter value\n    0x58 - Offset from JPEG_CORE_PROPERTIES to internal state structure\n    0x3824 - File handle offset\n    0x37C0 - State counter offset\n    0x37CC - Scan line buffer offset\n    0x4DE4 - DIB data buffer offset\n    0x36E4 - Channel buffer array base offset\n    0x4830 - Thumbnail buffer offset\n    0x37E0 - Sub-structure pointer offset",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
