      "name": "ijlRead",
      "signature": "uint ijlRead(int * param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Reads and parses JPEG image data from file or memory buffer.\n\nThis is the main entry point for Intel JPEG Library read operations. It validates\nparameters, opens files if needed, copies user settings to internal state, parses\nJPEG markers, and determines the subsampling mode of the image.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set up SEH exception frame for error recovery\n2. Store I/O type in internal state at offset 0x58\n3. Call ValidateJpegParams to validate JPEG_CORE_PROPERTIES structure\n4. Set read flag for header-only operations (IoTypes 0,1,4,5,0x14,0x15)\n5. Clear dimension fields for non-continuing read operations\n6. Open file if file-based I/O and handle not already open\n7. Copy user buffer settings to internal state when mode is 0\n8. Initialize internal buffer pointers based on I/O type\n9. Adjust buffer pointer for negative height (bottom-up DIB)\n10. Parse JPEG marker stream via ProcessJpegMarkerStream\n11. On partial success, calculate actual image dimensions from MCU blocks\n12. Seek back in file for file-based operations that need re-read\n13. Copy parsed image properties back to output structure\n14. Determine subsampling mode (0=none, 1=422, 2=422H, 3=411, 4=411H)\n15. Close file handle for header-only file reads\n\nParameters:\n  pJpegProps - Pointer to JPEG_CORE_PROPERTIES structure containing I/O settings\n               and receiving parsed image properties\n  nIoType    - IJLIOTYPE enumeration specifying the read operation type:\n               0  = IJL_JFILE_READPARAMS (file header only)\n               1  = IJL_JBUFF_READPARAMS (buffer header only)\n               2  = IJL_JFILE_READHEADER (file header, close after)\n               4  = IJL_JFILE_READWHOLEIMAGE (file full decode)\n               6  = IJL_JFILE_READENTROPY (file entropy only)\n               0x10 = IJL_JFILE_READTHUMBNAIL\n               0x12 = IJL_JFILE_READTHUMBNAIL_HEADER\n               0x14 = IJL_JFILE_READIMAGEC\n               0x15 = IJL_JBUFF_READIMAGEC\n\nReturns:\n  0          - Success (IJL_OK)\n  0xFFFFFFF6 - File open failed (IJL_FILE_NOT_FOUND, -10)\n  0xFFFFFFF7 - File close failed (IJL_ERR_FILE_CLOSE, -9)\n  0xFFFFFFE9 - File seek failed (IJL_ERR_FILE_SEEK, -23)\n  Other      - Error code from ValidateJpegParams or ProcessJpegMarkerStream\n\nI/O Type Constants:\n  0x00 = IJL_JFILE_READPARAMS     0x01 = IJL_JBUFF_READPARAMS\n  0x02 = IJL_JFILE_READHEADER     0x03 = IJL_JBUFF_READHEADER  \n  0x04 = IJL_JFILE_READWHOLEIMAGE 0x05 = IJL_JBUFF_READWHOLEIMAGE\n  0x06 = IJL_JFILE_READENTROPY    0x07 = IJL_JBUFF_READENTROPY\n  0x10 = IJL_JFILE_READTHUMBNAIL  0x11 = IJL_JBUFF_READTHUMBNAIL\n  0x14 = IJL_JFILE_READIMAGEC     0x15 = IJL_JBUFF_READIMAGEC\n\nSubsampling Mode Output (offset 0x3C):\n  0x00 = No subsampling (1:1:1)\n  0x01 = 4:2:2 horizontal\n  0x02 = 4:2:2 vertical  \n  0x03 = 4:1:1 CMYK horizontal\n  0x04 = 4:1:1 CMYK vertical\n  0xFF = Unknown/unsupported\n\nStructure Layout (JPEG_CORE_PROPERTIES internal offsets used):\n  0x00     Mode (0=user buffer, else internal)\n  0x04-1C  User DIB settings (copied to 0x78+)\n  0x20     File path string pointer\n  0x58     I/O type storage (pnIoState)\n  0x3834   Read operation flag\n  0x387C   File handle storage",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
