      "name": "ijlWrite",
      "signature": "uint ijlWrite(int * param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Intel JPEG Library write function - encodes and writes JPEG image data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Setup SEH exception frame for error handling\n2. Store I/O mode in JPEG properties structure at offset 0x58\n3. Validate JPEG parameters via ValidateJpegParams\n4. If file-based write modes (8, 10, 12) and no file handle, open output file with GENERIC_READ|GENERIC_WRITE\n5. If initial state, copy DIB parameters to JPEG core state (dimensions, padding, color format)\n6. Calculate stride and handle negative heights for bottom-up DIBs\n7. Allocate component sampling table if channel count changed (16 bytes per channel)\n8. Configure subsampling factors based on JPG_SUBSAMPLING mode (0-4):\n   - Case 0: No subsampling (1:1:1)\n   - Case 1: 4:2:2 horizontal subsampling\n   - Case 2: 4:2:2 vertical subsampling\n   - Case 3/4: 4:2:0 subsampling (2x2 chroma)\n9. Calculate MCU dimensions and block counts based on max sampling factors\n10. If not file-based mode, write JPEG headers via FUN_60017980\n11. Encode image data via ProcessJpegEncodeScan\n12. For progressive writes (mode 1/2), update progress counters\n13. Close file handle if opened and return status\n\nParameters:\npnJpegProps (int*): Pointer to JPEG_CORE_PROPERTIES structure containing:\n  - [0x00]: dwIOType - I/O type (0=memory, 1=file)\n  - [0x08]: lpszFileName - Output file path for file modes\n  - [0x0d]: nChannels - Number of color channels\n  - [0x0f]: eSubsampling - JPG_SUBSAMPLING enumeration\n  - [0x12]: nQuality - JPEG quality factor (0-100)\n  - [0x58]: nIOMode - Current operation mode\n  - [0x3824]: hFile - File handle for file I/O\n  - [0x37cc]: pComponentInfo - Per-component sampling info\n\nnIoMode (int): JPEG I/O operation mode:\n  - 8: IJL_JFILE_WRITEWHOLEIMAGE\n  - 9: IJL_JBUFF_WRITEWHOLEIMAGE\n  - 10: IJL_JFILE_WRITEHEADER\n  - 11: IJL_JBUFF_WRITEHEADER\n  - 12: IJL_JFILE_WRITEENTROPY\n  - 13: IJL_JBUFF_WRITEENTROPY\n\nReturns:\n0 (IJL_OK): Success\n0xFFFFFFF6 (-10): IJL_FILE_ERROR - Failed to open output file\n0xFFFFFFF7 (-9): IJL_FILE_ERROR - Failed to close file\n0xFFFFFFFB (-5): IJL_MEMORY_ERROR - Component buffer allocation failed\nOther: Validation error from ValidateJpegParams\n\nError Handling:\n- Uses SEH for exception safety\n- Restores exception list on all exit paths\n- Returns specific error codes for file and memory failures",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
