      "name": "ijlErrorStr",
      "signature": "char * ijlErrorStr(undefined4 param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Converts an Intel JPEG Library (IJL) error code to a human-readable error string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Adjust error code by adding 0x63 (99) to normalize the range\n2. If adjusted value exceeds 0x65 (101), return \"Unknown error code\"\n3. Use jump table lookup via byte index table at 0x6001a160\n4. Jump to appropriate case handler via jump table at 0x6001a0e0\n5. Return pointer to static error message string\n\nParameters:\n  nErrorCode (int) - IJL error code value (typically negative for errors, 0 for success)\n\nReturns:\n  char* - Pointer to static null-terminated error message string\n\nError Code Mapping (partial):\n  0 (IJL_OK)                    -> \"Success\"\n  -1 (IJL_RESERVED)             -> \"Reserved\"\n  -2 (IJL_ERR_DATA)             -> \"Data error\"\n  -3 (IJL_ERR_FILE)             -> \"File error\"\n  Unrecognized codes            -> \"Unknown error code\"\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- All returned strings are statically allocated (do not free)\n- Error codes use Intel JPEG Library enumeration values\n- Jump table implementation for O(1) lookup performance\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x63 (99)       - Base offset to normalize error codes\n  0x65 (101)      - Maximum valid adjusted error code\n  0x6001a160      - Byte index table for jump table dispatch\n  0x6001a0e0      - Jump table with case handler addresses",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:22efca801240716fd81b15c0f5e878e6",
