      "name": "ValidateBinkInstallLocation",
      "signature": "undefined4 ValidateBinkInstallLocation(HMODULE param_1, undefined4 param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates Bink DLL installation and dispatches initialization based on reason code.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if dwReason is within valid range (0-3)\n2. If dwReason > 3, return 0 (failure)\n3. Use jump table to dispatch based on dwReason:\n   - Case 0: Return 1 (success)\n   - Case 1: Call InitializeDecoderByCapability with hModule\n   - Case 2: Return 1 (success)\n   - Case 3: Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  hModule (HMODULE): Handle to the Bink DLL module being validated\n  dwReason (dword): Reason code for the validation call (DLL_PROCESS_ATTACH, etc.)\n    0 = DLL_PROCESS_DETACH\n    1 = DLL_PROCESS_ATTACH\n    2 = DLL_THREAD_ATTACH\n    3 = DLL_THREAD_DETACH\n\nReturns:\n  1 (TRUE): Validation successful or no action needed\n  0 (FALSE): Invalid reason code (dwReason > 3)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Only DLL_PROCESS_ATTACH (reason 1) triggers decoder initialization\n  All other valid reasons are no-ops returning success\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Jump Table at 0x6001a1fc:\n  Offset  Target      Case\n  0x00    0x6001a1f2  Case 0 (return 1)\n  0x04    0x6001a1e2  Case 1 (call InitializeDecoderByCapability)\n  0x08    0x6001a1f2  Case 2 (return 1)\n  0x0C    0x6001a1f2  Case 3 (return 1)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
