      "name": "OutputDebugStringLines",
      "signature": "undefined OutputDebugStringLines(uint * param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Outputs a multi-line debug string with thread ID prefixes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if input string is non-empty, return immediately if empty\n2. If nMaxLines > 0, initialize line buffer with 0xFF padding and space-fill\n3. Get current thread ID and format prefix string \"[%02X] \"\n4. Loop through input string, splitting on newline (0x0A) characters\n5. For each line segment, copy to buffer and null-terminate\n6. If continuation line and flag bit 1 set, output thread prefix first\n7. Output the line buffer via function pointer (OutputDebugString)\n8. Advance to next line and repeat until end of string\n\nParameters:\n  lpszInputString - Pointer to null-terminated input string (may contain newlines)\n  nMaxLines - Maximum number of lines to format (controls buffer size)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty input string returns immediately\n  - Single newline character (length 1) uses alternate buffer\n  - Newline detection tracks state in g_fHasNewline global\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x0A (10) - ASCII newline character\n  0xFF (-1) - Buffer initialization fill value\n  0x20 (' ') - Space padding character\n  0x02 - Flag bit in g_dwDebugOutputFlags for prefix output\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset   Size   Field             Description\n  0x000    512    szLineBuffer      Formatted line output buffer\n  0x200    12     szThreadPrefix    Thread ID prefix \"[XX] \"",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:e5e2e6945663fa0974d5bbb88de0e19f",
