      "name": "ShowMessageBoxPreserveQuit",
      "signature": "int ShowMessageBoxPreserveQuit(LPCSTR param_1, UINT param_2, undefined4 param_3, LPCSTR param_4)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Displays a message box while preserving any pending WM_QUIT messages.\n\nThis function safely shows a MessageBox without losing WM_QUIT messages that may have been\nposted before the dialog appeared. Modal dialogs can consume quit messages, so this wrapper\npeeks for WM_QUIT first, shows the dialog, then re-posts the quit if one was pending.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Peek for WM_QUIT (0x12) message in the queue, removing it if found\n2. Display the MessageBox with the provided text, caption, and type\n3. If a WM_QUIT was found in step 1, re-post it with the original wParam (exit code)\n4. Return the MessageBox result\n\nParameters:\n  lpszText - Message text to display in the dialog body\n  dwType - MessageBox type flags (MB_OK, MB_YESNO, etc.)\n  dwReserved - Unused parameter (reserved for future use)\n  lpszCaption - Caption/title text for the dialog window\n\nReturns:\n  int - MessageBox return value (IDOK, IDYES, IDNO, IDCANCEL, etc.)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If WM_QUIT was pending, it will be re-posted after dialog closes\n  - The wParam from the original WM_QUIT is preserved (exit code)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x12 - WM_QUIT message identifier\n  0x1 - PM_REMOVE flag for PeekMessageA (removes message from queue)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:b448a40d91be7dd1b2bd74eda9853b2cbeb580aec6e540f582dbb7fd2ccfc348",
