      "name": "FreeVersionInfoBuffer",
      "signature": "void FreeVersionInfoBuffer(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Frees the version info buffer allocated during module version initialization.\n\nWrapper function that calls LocalFree to release the memory allocated for\nstoring PE version resource data during InitModuleVersionInfo execution.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push EBX (contains pVersionData handle) onto stack as LocalFree parameter\n2. Call LocalFree via import table to release allocated memory\n3. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT EBX - pVersionData: Handle to local memory allocated by LocalAlloc\n                 (HLOCAL from InitModuleVersionInfo's version buffer)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No explicit return value\n  Note: LocalFree return value in EAX is discarded\n\nCalled By:\n  InitModuleVersionInfo - Cleanup at function exit regardless of success/failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - EBX must contain valid HLOCAL or NULL (LocalFree handles NULL safely)\n  - Called unconditionally as part of SEH cleanup sequence",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:d478d4372d1e64c85a51cd620b3eacafd973aa0a6bd25c460272356776cfbd18",
