      "name": "ReadBytesFromJpegStream",
      "signature": "int ReadBytesFromJpegStream(DWORD param_1, uint param_2, int * param_3, int * param_4, undefined4 * param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Reads bytes from JPEG stream context with automatic buffer allocation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if requested bytes exceed available buffer (pStreamCtx+0x24)\n2. If within buffer: call FUN_600010a0 to get pointer directly from stream\n3. If exceeds buffer: allocate new buffer via operator_new\n4. Copy available bytes from stream buffer using g_pfnMemcpy\n5. Loop reading remaining bytes in 0x1000 (4096) byte chunks\n6. Handle read errors by freeing allocated buffer\n\nParameters:\n  pStreamCtx - Pointer to JPEG stream context structure\n               +0x10: Current read position pointer\n               +0x1c: Bytes read counter\n               +0x24: Bytes remaining in buffer\n  dwBytesRequested - Number of bytes to read\n  ppbAllocatedBuffer - OUT: Receives allocated buffer pointer (for cleanup)\n  ppbDataOut - OUT: Receives pointer to actual data\n  pnBufferAllocated - OUT: Set to 1 if buffer was allocated, 0 otherwise\n\nReturns:\n  0 on success\n  -5 (0xFFFFFFFB) on allocation failure\n  -21 (0xFFFFFFEB) on read error (cleans up allocated buffer)\n  Other error codes from FUN_600010a0\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1000 - Chunk size for multi-read operations (4KB)\n  0xFFFF - Maximum single read size check\n\nNote: pbWritePtr is decompiler-generated (undefined1 *) and cannot be explicitly typed via API.",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
