      "name": "ReadNextJpegMarkerCode",
      "signature": "int ReadNextJpegMarkerCode(byte * param_1, uint * param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Reads the next JPEG marker code from a stream context.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if cached marker byte exists at context+0x30\n2. If cached, clear cache, normalize marker, output to pdwMarkerCode, return success\n3. Otherwise, skip entropy-coded data to find next 0xFF marker\n4. If skip failed (EOF), propagate error code\n5. Read one byte from stream for marker code\n6. If read failed, output 0x100 (invalid marker) as fallback, return success\n7. Normalize marker code and output to pdwMarkerCode\n\nParameters:\n    pStreamContext - Pointer to JPEG stream context structure\n    pdwMarkerCode - Output pointer for normalized marker code\n\nReturns:\n    0 on success (marker code written to pdwMarkerCode)\n    Non-zero error code on stream failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n    - Cached byte at offset 0x30 provides look-ahead for marker parsing\n    - RST markers (0xD0-0xDF) are normalized to 0xD0 by FUN_6001a750\n    - If read fails after skip, outputs 0x100 as invalid marker sentinel\n\nStructure Layout (pStreamContext):\n    Offset  Size  Field       Description\n    0x10    4     pBuffer     Current read position\n    0x18    4     dwBufEnd    Buffer end position  \n    0x1C    4     dwBytesRead Total bytes consumed\n    0x24    4     dwBufAvail  Bytes available in buffer\n    0x30    1     bCachedByte Cached marker byte (look-ahead)\n    0x3C    4     pRefillFunc Buffer refill callback",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:4289603cf104298bbccdee23de021ba1f8015af66f0be6c90e086a1d04e14b24",
