      "name": "SkipJpegMarkerSegment",
      "signature": "int SkipJpegMarkerSegment(byte * param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Skips past an unknown or unhandled JPEG marker segment in the stream.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read 2-byte big-endian segment length via FUN_6001aa60\n2. Subtract 2 from length (length field itself is included in count)\n3. If length < 2, return error -21 (invalid segment length)\n4. Skip initial buffered data (from offset 0x24 of frame info)\n5. Loop to skip remaining bytes in 4KB (0x1000) chunks\n6. Return 0 on success\n\nParameters:\npFrameInfo - Pointer to JPEG frame info structure containing:\n  - Offset 0x24: Current buffer size (bytes available to skip)\n\nReturns:\n0 - Success (segment fully skipped)\n-21 (0xFFFFFFEB) - Invalid segment length (less than 2 bytes)\nPropagates errors from FUN_6001aa60 and FUN_600010a0\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x1000 (4096) - Maximum bytes to skip per iteration (4KB chunk)\n0xFFFF (65535) - Maximum valid segment length\n0x2 - Minimum valid segment length (length field itself)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:3e7b4aab132c9c9e0e0bd9294bb703cb36a811f9c910915495f1119365afd131",
