      "name": "ReadBigEndian16FromJpegStream",
      "signature": "int ReadBigEndian16FromJpegStream(byte * param_1, int * param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Reads a 16-bit big-endian value from a JPEG stream.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize error flag to 0\n2. Call ReadBytesFromJpegStream to read 2 bytes into temporary buffer\n3. If read succeeds (return 0):\n   a. Extract first byte, shift left 8 bits (high byte)\n   b. Extract second byte (low byte)\n   c. Combine as (highByte << 8) + lowByte for big-endian value\n   d. Store result in output pointer\n4. Cleanup: If error flag set and temp buffer allocated, call AtoiMbcsWrapper\n5. Return the result code from ReadBytesFromJpegStream\n\nParameters:\n  pJpegStream - Pointer to JPEG stream context structure\n  pnOutValue - Output pointer to receive the 16-bit value as int\n\nReturns:\n  0 on success, non-zero error code on failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Big-endian byte order (network/JPEG standard order)\n  - Reads exactly 2 bytes for 16-bit value\n  - Used for reading JPEG segment lengths and marker parameters\n\nCallers:\n  ParseJpegQuantizationTables, ParseJpegFrameHeader, ParseJpegStartOfFrame,\n  ParseDhtMarkerSegment, SkipJpegMarkerSegment, ParseJfxxThumbnailData",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:0e962c42059faad91af379472e2343b2936d9b81ca7c795041696b9f510e9953",
