      "name": "ReadBigEndian16FromJpegSegment",
      "signature": "int ReadBigEndian16FromJpegSegment(byte * param_1, int * param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Reads a 16-bit big-endian value from a JPEG segment's data content.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output value to 0 and local buffer tracking variables\n2. Call FUN_6001aa60 to read the 2-byte segment length (big-endian)\n3. Validate segment length is at least 2 bytes\n4. Subtract 2 from length (JPEG segment lengths include the length field itself)\n5. Read remaining segment data via ReadBytesFromJpegStream\n6. Extract 16-bit big-endian value: byte[0] * 256 + byte[1]\n7. Store extracted value in output parameter\n8. Free allocated buffer if one was created\n\nParameters:\n  pStreamCtx - Pointer to JPEG stream context structure\n  pnValueOut - OUT: Receives the extracted 16-bit big-endian value\n\nReturns:\n  0 on success\n  -21 (0xFFFFFFEB) if segment length < 2 bytes (invalid segment)\n  Other error codes from FUN_6001aa60 or ReadBytesFromJpegStream\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x2 - Minimum valid JPEG segment length (length field size)\n  0x100 - Multiplier for big-endian byte[0] (256 = 2^8)\n  -0x15 (-21) - Error code for segment too short",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
