      "name": "ParseJpegStartOfFrame",
      "signature": "int ParseJpegStartOfFrame(byte * param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Parses JPEG Start Of Frame (SOF) marker segment to extract frame header.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6001aa60 to get SOF marker data length from stream\n2. Validate data length >= 2 bytes (return 0xFFFFFFEB if too short)\n3. Call ReadBytesFromJpegStream to read SOF segment data\n4. Extract sample precision from byte 0\n5. Extract image height from bytes 1-2 (big-endian)\n6. Extract image width from bytes 3-4 (big-endian)\n7. Extract number of components from byte 5\n8. Free existing component array if present\n9. Allocate new component array (16 bytes per component)\n10. Parse each component: ID, sampling factors, quant table\n11. Track maximum horizontal and vertical sampling factors\n12. Calculate MCU dimensions from frame size and max sampling\n\nParameters:\npbJpegStream - Pointer to JPEG stream/decoder state\npJpegContext - Pointer to JpegImageContext structure\n\nReturns:\n0 - Success\n0xFFFFFFEB - SOF segment too short\n0xFFFFFFF0 - Image height is zero\n0xFFFFFFFB - Memory allocation failed",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:eab41287f6832258ced2ceef25cc3795e7b9b378ea6e314f18d38cb8c3242b45",
