      "name": "ParseJpegQuantizationTables",
      "signature": "int ParseJpegQuantizationTables(int param_1, byte * param_2, int param_3)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Parses JPEG DQT (Define Quantization Table) marker segment and populates quantization tables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read segment length from stream using FUN_6001aa60.\n2. Validate segment length is between 2 and 517 bytes (0x205).\n3. Read quantization table data from JPEG stream via ReadBytesFromJpegStream.\n4. For each table entry in segment:\n   a. Extract table index (low nibble, 0-4) and precision (high nibble).\n   b. Validate table index is in range 0-4.\n   c. Store precision at component offset +0x94.\n   d. Update component count at decoder offset +0x84 if needed.\n   e. Copy quantization values to table at component offset +0x9c.\n   f. If not skipping DCT, call ComputeDctCoefficientsZigzag.\n5. Free allocated buffer if any.\n\nParameters:\n  nDecoderCtx - Pointer to JPEG decoder context structure (cast as int).\n  pStreamCtx - Pointer to JPEG stream context for reading.\n  nSkipDctCompute - If non-zero, skip DCT coefficient zigzag computation.\n\nReturns:\n  0 on success.\n  -21 (0xFFFFFFEB) if segment length out of valid range.\n  -7 (0xFFFFFFF9) if table index greater than 4 (invalid quantization table ID).\n  Other negative values from ReadBytesFromJpegStream or FUN_6001aa60.\n\nStructure Layout (Decoder Context):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Description\n  0x80    4     dwTableCount  Number of quantization tables processed.\n  0x84    4     dwCompCount   Number of components with quantization tables.\n\nStructure Layout (Component, stride 0xB4):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Description\n  0x94    4     dwPrecision   Quantization precision (0=8-bit, 1=16-bit).\n  0x9c    4     pQuantTable   Pointer to 64-entry quantization table.\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x205 (517) - Maximum DQT segment length.\n  0x40 (64) - Quantization table entry count.\n  0x41 (65) - 8-bit table size (1 header + 64 bytes).\n  0x81 (129) - 16-bit table size (1 header + 128 bytes).\n  0xB4 (180) - Component structure stride.",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
