      "name": "ParseDhtMarkerSegment",
      "signature": "int ParseDhtMarkerSegment(int param_1, byte * param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Parses a JPEG DHT (Define Huffman Table) marker segment and builds Huffman decode tables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate marker data pointer and read segment length from stream\n2. Subtract 2-byte length field, verify remaining data is within valid DHT size (0x2-0x445)\n3. Read DHT segment bytes from JPEG stream into allocated buffer\n4. For each Huffman table definition in segment:\n   a. Extract table class (AC=1/DC=0) from upper nibble of first byte\n   b. Extract table destination ID (0-3) from lower nibble\n   c. Validate class is 0 or 1, destination is 0-3\n   d. Track max destination IDs used at context offsets 0x88 (DC) and 0x8c (AC)\n   e. Call BuildHuffmanDecodeTable with code lengths and symbol values\n   f. Sum 16 code length bytes to get symbol count\n   g. Advance past this table definition (17 header bytes + symbol count)\n5. Free allocated buffer if allocation flag set\n\nParameters:\n  pJpegDecoder - Pointer to JPEG decoder context structure containing Huffman tables\n  pbMarkerData - Pointer to DHT marker data (after 0xFFC4 marker bytes)\n\nReturns:\n  0 on success\n  -6 (0xFFFFFFFA) if table class or destination ID out of range\n  -21 (0xFFFFFFEB) if segment length invalid (too small or too large)\n  Other negative values from called functions on error\n\nStructure Layout (pJpegDecoder offsets):\n  Offset   Size   Field               Description\n  0x088    4      dwDcTableCount      Number of DC Huffman tables defined\n  0x08C    4      dwAcTableCount      Number of AC Huffman tables defined\n  0x090    4      dwMaxTableId        Maximum table destination ID + 1\n  0x364    0x670  aDcTables[4]        DC Huffman decode tables (4 x HuffmanDecodeTable)\n  0x1D24   0x670  aAcTables[4]        AC Huffman decode tables (4 x HuffmanDecodeTable)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x2 - Minimum DHT segment length (length field only)\n  0x444 - Maximum DHT segment data after length (1092 bytes)\n  0x11 (17) - DHT table header size (1 class/id byte + 16 code length bytes)\n  0x670 (1648) - Size of each HuffmanDecodeTable structure\n  0x364, 0x1D24 - Context offsets to DC and AC table arrays\n\nDecompiler Notes:\n  SSA temporaries (iVar2, iVar3, iVar5, bVar1, pbVar4) are register-allocated\n  intermediate values that cannot be renamed:\n  - iVar2: Return value / error code accumulator\n  - iVar3: Sum of code length bytes (symbol count)\n  - iVar5: Loop counter for 16 code length bytes\n  - bVar1: Table class byte (upper nibble of table header)\n  - pbVar4: Temporary pointer for stream operations",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:b8178503cccdadb101b08959baf97d18ff507bddd8d03565c5cd3b41c35d668a",
