      "name": "ParseJpegFrameHeader",
      "signature": "int ParseJpegFrameHeader(int param_1, byte * param_2, int param_3, uint * param_4)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Parses JPEG SOF (Start Of Frame) marker to extract frame header information.\nReads component count, allocates component table, and populates component entries\nwith sampling factors, quantization table pointers, and Huffman table pointers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read 2-byte segment length (big-endian) via ReadBigEndian16FromJpegStream\n2. Validate segment length >= 2 bytes, return -21 (0xFFFFFFEB) if invalid\n3. Read frame header data from stream via ReadBytesFromJpegStream\n4. Extract component count from first byte, store in pComponentInfo[0]\n5. Allocate component table: count * 24 bytes via operator_new\n6. Store table pointer at pComponentInfo[0xD] (offset 0x34)\n7. Loop through each component:\n   a. Read component ID byte\n   b. Read sampling factors byte (H=high nibble, V=low nibble)\n   c. Validate H and V sampling factors are in range 0-4\n   d. Search pFrameInfo component array for matching component ID\n   e. Populate component entry (24 bytes each):\n      - [0x00]: Table index\n      - [0x04]: Sampling factor H\n      - [0x08]: Sampling factor V\n      - [0x0C]: Quantization table ptr (pDecoderContext + 0x1D24 + idx*0x670)\n      - [0x10]: DC Huffman table ptr (pDecoderContext + 0x364 + idx*0x670)\n      - [0x14]: AC Huffman table ptr (pDecoderContext + 0x94 + idx*0xB4)\n8. Read sample precision, image height, chroma sampling into pComponentInfo\n9. Free temporary buffer if allocated\n\nParameters:\npDecoderContext - JPEG decoder context base address containing Huffman/quant tables\npbStreamData    - Stream context pointer for reading JPEG data\npFrameInfo      - Frame info structure with component tables at offset +0x28\npComponentInfo  - OUT: Receives parsed frame data and allocated component table\n\nReturns:\n0              - Success\n-5 (0xFFFFFFFB) - Memory allocation failure\n-21 (0xFFFFFFEB) - Invalid segment length or sampling factor out of range\n\nStructure Layout (pComponentInfo output):\nOffset  Size  Field              Description\n0x00    4     dwComponentCount   Number of color components\n0x08    4     dwSamplePrecision  Bits per sample\n0x0C    4     dwImageHeight      Image height in pixels\n0x10    4     dwHChroma          Horizontal chroma sampling\n0x14    4     dwVChroma          Vertical chroma sampling\n0x34    4     pComponentTable    Pointer to allocated component array\n\nComponent Entry Layout (24 bytes each):\nOffset  Size  Field           Description\n0x00    4     nTableIndex     Index into frame component array\n0x04    4     nSamplingH      Horizontal sampling factor\n0x08    4     nSamplingV      Vertical sampling factor\n0x0C    4     pQuantTable     Pointer to quantization table\n0x10    4     pDcHuffman      Pointer to DC Huffman table\n0x14    4     pAcHuffman      Pointer to AC Huffman table\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x1D24 - Quantization table base offset in decoder context\n0x364  - DC Huffman table base offset in decoder context\n0x94   - AC Huffman table base offset in decoder context\n0x670  - Stride between consecutive table entries\n0xB4   - AC Huffman table stride\n0x18   - Size of component entry structure (24 bytes)\n\nNote: dwSehEspBackup is an SEH stack frame variable (stores ESP backup).\nType cannot be set via decompiler due to Ghidra HighVariable limitation.",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
