      "name": "WriteMarkerByte",
      "signature": "undefined WriteMarkerByte(undefined1 param_1, int * param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Writes a JPEG marker byte sequence to the output buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Write the marker prefix byte (0xFF) at current buffer position\n2. Increment buffer position\n3. Write the marker type byte at the new position\n4. Increment buffer position again\n\nParameters:\n  param_1 (bMarkerType) - BYTE: The JPEG marker type identifier (e.g., 0xD8 for SOI, 0xE0 for APP0)\n  param_2 (pnBufferPos) - int*: Pointer to the current write position in the output buffer\n\nReturns:\n  void - Buffer position is updated via the pnBufferPos pointer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xFF - Standard JPEG marker prefix byte\n\nNotes:\n  JPEG markers always consist of 0xFF followed by a marker type byte.\n  Called by various JPEG segment writing functions (SOI, APP0, SOF0, SOS, etc.).",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:c7501e9771acb2576e844f62a25a643c7cd7dedf65d8fe267dd439ae02e5ad6f",
