      "name": "WriteMarkerWord",
      "signature": "undefined WriteMarkerWord(undefined4 param_1, int * param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Writes a 16-bit marker word to a JPEG output buffer in big-endian format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract high byte (bits 8-15) from marker word using right shift\n2. Write high byte to current buffer position\n3. Increment buffer position pointer\n4. Write low byte (bits 0-7) to next buffer position  \n5. Increment buffer position pointer again\n\nParameters:\n  dwMarkerWord - 16-bit JPEG marker value (e.g., 0xFFD8 for SOI, 0xFFE0 for APP0)\n  pnBufferPos  - Pointer to current write position in output buffer (updated on return)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Buffer position pointer is incremented by 2 bytes on return\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Caller must ensure buffer has at least 2 bytes available\n  - Buffer position pointer must be valid and writable\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  - 0x8: Bit shift for extracting high byte from 16-bit value\n\nCalled By:\n  WriteJfifApp0Marker, WriteSof0Marker, WriteQuantizationTableMarker,\n  WriteHuffmanTableMarkers, WriteSosMarker, WriteRestartIntervalMarker",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
