      "name": "WriteSoiMarkerAndInitEncoder",
      "signature": "undefined WriteSoiMarkerAndInitEncoder(undefined4 param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Writes the JPEG SOI (Start of Image) marker and initializes the encoder state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate a 4-byte local buffer (abMarkerBytes) for marker construction\n2. Set buffer pointer (pbMarkerBuffer) to point to local buffer\n3. Call WriteMarkerByte to write SOI marker (0xFFD8) to output stream\n4. Call g_pfnDecodeProc1 function pointer to initialize encoder with buffer and state\n\nParameters:\n  pEncoderState - Pointer to JPEG encoder state structure (offset from main JPEG state)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nLocal Variables:\n  abMarkerBytes (byte[4]) - Stack buffer at [ESP] for marker byte construction\n  pbMarkerBuffer (byte *) - Pointer at [ESP+4] initialized to abMarkerBytes address\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xD8 - JPEG SOI (Start of Image) marker byte (preceded by 0xFF)\n  0x02 - Encoder initialization mode passed to g_pfnDecodeProc1\n\nCalled By:\n  ProcessJpegEncodeScan - Called for non-progressive encoding modes (not types 8 or 9)\n\nRelated Functions:\n  WriteMarkerByte - Writes 0xFF prefix byte followed by marker byte\n  g_pfnDecodeProc1 - Function pointer for encoder state initialization",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
