      "name": "WriteEoiMarkerAndFlushEncoder",
      "signature": "undefined WriteEoiMarkerAndFlushEncoder(undefined4 param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Writes the JPEG EOI (End of Image) marker and flushes the encoder output buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 4-byte local buffer for marker construction\n2. Set buffer pointer to point to local buffer start\n3. Call WriteMarkerByte to write EOI marker (0xFF 0xD9) to buffer\n4. Call g_pfnDecodeProc1 to flush 2 bytes from buffer to encoder output stream\n\nParameters:\n  pEncoderState (int *) - Pointer to JPEG encoder state structure (offset 0xDFA from main state)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nLocal Variables:\n  abMarkerBytes (byte[4]) - Stack buffer at [ESP] for marker byte construction\n  pbMarkerBuffer (byte *) - Pointer at [ESP+0x4] tracking current write position in buffer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xD9 - JPEG EOI (End of Image) marker byte (preceded by 0xFF written by WriteMarkerByte)\n  0x02 - Number of bytes to flush (the 2-byte EOI marker: 0xFF 0xD9)\n\nRelated Functions:\n  WriteMarkerByte - Writes 0xFF prefix followed by marker byte to buffer\n  WriteSoiMarkerAndInitEncoder - Writes SOI marker (0xD8) at stream start\n  g_pfnDecodeProc1 - Function pointer for flushing buffer to output stream\n\nCalled By:\n  ProcessJpegEncodeScan - Called when all scans complete (nScanResult == 0)\n  FUN_60017980 - Called for non-progressive encoding modes",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:340d28b3d352ba3ed8dfd391ac446df8312dde61b9480708dfedea6546174201",
