      "name": "WriteSof0Marker",
      "signature": "undefined WriteSof0Marker(undefined4 param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Writes JPEG SOF0 (Start Of Frame - Baseline DCT) marker segment to output stream.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate segment length as (component_count * 3) + 8\n2. Write 0xFF 0xC0 marker bytes via WriteMarkerByte\n3. Write segment length as big-endian word via WriteMarkerWord\n4. Write sample precision (8 bits per sample)\n5. Write image height and width as big-endian words\n6. Write component count\n7. For each component, write component ID, sampling factors, and quantization table selector\n8. Output complete buffer via g_pfnDecodeProc1 function pointer\n\nParameters:\npOutputStream - JpegOutputBuffer*: Output stream buffer for encoded data\npJpegContext - JpegImageContext*: JPEG encoding context structure\n  +0x04: Image height (uint)\n  +0x08: Image width (uint)\n  +0x1C: Component count (1=grayscale, 3=color)\n  +0x28: Pointer to component info array (16 bytes per component)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0xC0 - SOF0 marker (Start Of Frame, Baseline DCT)\n0x08 - Sample precision (8 bits per component)\n0x11 - Sampling factors 1x1 horizontal and vertical\n0x10 - Component info structure stride (16 bytes per entry)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
