      "name": "WriteHuffmanTableMarkers",
      "signature": "int WriteHuffmanTableMarkers(undefined4 param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Writes DHT (Define Huffman Table) markers to JPEG output stream.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate total symbol count by summing bit lengths across all tables\n2. Write DHT marker header (0xFFC4) with calculated segment length\n3. Call output proc to write initial 4-byte marker header\n4. For each Huffman table (DC and AC pairs):\n   a. Sum bit length counts (16 bytes) to get symbol count\n   b. Validate total size does not exceed 0x144 bytes\n   c. Build table header: (table_class << 4) | table_id\n   d. Copy 16 bit-length bytes to buffer\n   e. Copy symbol values to buffer\n   f. Call output proc to write table data\n\nParameters:\n    pOutputBuffer - Pointer to JPEG output buffer/stream context\n    pJpegEncoder - Pointer to JPEG encoder context containing Huffman tables\n\nReturns:\n    0 - Success\n    -6 (0xFFFFFFFA) - Table size exceeds maximum (0x144 bytes)\n    Other - Error code from output procedure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n    0xC4 - DHT marker type (second byte after 0xFF)\n    0x10 - Number of bit-length counts per table (16 bits max code length)\n    0x11 - Header size: 16 bit-lengths + 1 table identifier byte\n    0x22 - Per-table overhead: 0x11 * 2 bytes\n    0x90 - Offset to Huffman table count in encoder context\n    0x373C - Offset to Huffman table entry array in encoder context\n    0x144 - Maximum allowed table segment size (324 bytes)\n    0x0C - Huffman table entry stride (12 bytes per entry)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:1d32eb4af765882b33d474e25ed58fbc4d12186df6ad152700c6b75c33d962d9",
