      "name": "WriteSosMarker",
      "signature": "undefined WriteSosMarker(undefined4 param_1, char * param_2, char * param_3, char * param_4)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Writes the JPEG SOS (Start of Scan) marker segment to the encoder buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate marker data length as nComponents * 2 + 6 bytes\n2. Write 0xDA (SOS marker identifier) via WriteMarkerByte\n3. Write marker length word via WriteMarkerWord\n4. Write number of scan components (Ns)\n5. For grayscale (1 component):\n   a. Write component ID 0\n   b. Write combined Huffman selector 0x00 (DC=0, AC=0)\n6. For YCbCr (3+ components):\n   a. Write component ID 1 with first DC/AC selector pair\n   b. For components 2 to nComponents, write ID and combined selectors\n   c. Combined selector = (DC_table << 4) | AC_table\n7. Write spectral selection: Ss=0, Se=0x3F (63), Ah/Al=0\n8. Call g_pfnDecodeProc1 to process complete marker buffer\n\nParameters:\n  pEncoderState - Pointer to encoder state structure (passed to g_pfnDecodeProc1)\n  nComponents - Number of color components (1=grayscale, 3=YCbCr)\n  pbDcTableSelectors - Array of DC Huffman table indices per component\n  pbAcTableSelectors - Array of AC Huffman table indices per component\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xDA - JPEG SOS (Start of Scan) marker identifier\n  0x3F (63) - End spectral selection (Se) for baseline DCT\n  6 - Base marker length (2 length + 1 Ns + 3 spectral bytes)\n  0x10 (16) - DC table index left shift amount for combining",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:cc8ce22f6ece050556f980443d46fbc19a2a5cea54e9723c8a4591ac31a347d3",
