      "name": "WriteRestartIntervalMarker",
      "signature": "undefined WriteRestartIntervalMarker(undefined4 param_1, undefined4 param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Writes the JPEG DRI (Define Restart Interval) marker to the output stream.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 6-byte buffer on stack for marker data\n2. Write marker header: 0xFF followed by 0xDD (DRI marker identifier)\n3. Write marker length: 0x0004 (4 bytes, big-endian)\n4. Write restart interval value as 2-byte big-endian integer\n5. Call g_pfnDecodeProc1 to flush 6-byte buffer to output stream\n\nParameters:\n- nRestartInterval: Number of MCUs between restart markers (0 disables restart markers)\n- pScanState: Pointer to scan state structure containing output buffer context\n\nReturns:\n- Return value from g_pfnDecodeProc1 (0 on success, non-zero on error)\n\nJPEG Marker Structure (6 bytes total):\nOffset  Size  Field              Value\n0x00    1     Marker prefix      0xFF\n0x01    1     Marker type        0xDD (DRI)\n0x02    2     Length             0x0004 (big-endian)\n0x04    2     Restart interval   nRestartInterval (big-endian)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Restart interval of 0 means no restart markers in the JPEG stream\n- Called during progressive JPEG encoding setup (from FUN_600179f0)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:48ebf39310417de5a9327bd7290dd3851e076c9a1a3a6db378d6dfd73436ee37",
