      "name": "WriteRestartMarkerAndDecode",
      "signature": "undefined4 WriteRestartMarkerAndDecode(undefined4 param_1, undefined4 param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Writes a JPEG restart marker and invokes the decode procedure.\n\nConverts a restart marker index (0-7) to the corresponding JPEG RST marker byte\n(0xD0-0xD7) and writes it to the output stream, then continues decoding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate restart index is in range 0-7 (RST0-RST7)\n2. Convert index to marker byte (0xD0 + index) via switch statement\n3. Setup write position pointer to parameter stack location\n4. Write marker sequence via FUN_6001b8b0 (writes 0xFF + marker byte)\n5. Call g_pfnDecodeProc1 to continue decoding from new position\n6. Return decode result or error code for invalid index\n\nParameters:\nnRestartIndex (dword): Restart marker index (0-7)\n  - 0 = RST0 (0xD0), 1 = RST1 (0xD1), ... 7 = RST7 (0xD7)\n  - Values > 7 return error immediately\npScanState (void*): Pointer to scan state structure for decoding context\n\nReturns:\n0: Success - decode completed normally\nNon-zero positive: Decode procedure return value (suspension or continuation)\n-25 (0xFFFFFFE7): Invalid restart marker index (out of range 0-7)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0xD0-0xD7: JPEG RST0-RST7 restart marker bytes\n0xFFFFFFE7: -25 decimal, invalid restart index error\n0x02: Decode mode parameter passed to g_pfnDecodeProc1\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Index > 7 returns immediately with error, no marker written\n- Compiler optimized switch statement for index-to-marker conversion",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
