      "comment": "Dispatches JPEG scan decoding to appropriate handler based on DCT mode and bit depth.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output bytes decoded to zero\n2. Check if scan progress is within bounds (scan lines, spectral selection)\n3. If within bounds, dispatch to immediate scan decode (baseline or progressive DCT)\n4. If out of bounds, clamp scan parameters to valid range\n5. Allocate MCU working buffer (0x50000 bytes) if not already allocated\n6. Initialize MCU buffer header with frame dimensions and reset all entries\n7. Dispatch to MCU block decoder (baseline or progressive)\n8. Call decode completion callback on success\n9. Return result code\n\nParameters:\n    pnBytesDecoded (int*) - OUT: Number of bytes successfully decoded\n    pFrameInfo (uint*) - IN: JPEG frame information structure\n    pBitStream (int*) - IN: Bit stream reader state\n    pScanState (int*) - IN/OUT: Scan decoder state structure\n\nReturns:\n    0 on success\n    -5 on memory allocation failure\n    Other negative values on decode error\n\nMagic Numbers:\n    0x50000 - MCU working buffer size (327680 bytes, ~8192 MCU entries)\n    0x28 - MCU entry stride (40 bytes per entry)\n    0x120C - Offset to MCU buffer pointer in scan state (index 4620)\n    0x1378 - Offset to progressive mode flag in scan state (index 4984)\n\nJPEG Mode Dispatch (scan state[0]):\n    0x0E, 0x0F: 2-bit depth\n    0x10, 0x11: 4-bit depth\n    0x12, 0x13: 8-bit depth\n    default: 1-bit depth",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
