      "name": "ProcessProgressiveDctScanBlocks",
      "signature": "undefined4 ProcessProgressiveDctScanBlocks(undefined4 param_1, uint * param_2, int * param_3, int param_4, undefined4 param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Processes DCT (Discrete Cosine Transform) blocks for JPEG progressive scan decoding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize component information arrays (block widths, quant table pointers, block counts)\n2. Calculate total block count from component structure at offset 0x37c0\n3. Branch based on component mode (interleaved vs non-interleaved)\n4. For each MCU row and column:\n   a. Calculate coefficient buffer offset using (row * width + col) * blockCount * 128\n   b. Clear or decode DCT coefficients based on component settings\n   c. Apply inverse DCT transform based on precision mode switch\n   d. Call FUN_6001cc30 to process decoded blocks\n   e. Update row/column state for progressive decoding\n5. Handle scan boundary conditions and resumption state for streaming\n\nParameters:\n- pnOutputBuffer: Output buffer for decoded image data (unused in some paths)\n- pScanBuffer: Input scan buffer with encoded DCT coefficients  \n- pComponentInfo: JPEG component descriptor structure\n  - [0]: Number of components in scan\n  - [2],[3]: Component dimensions (0 indicates non-interleaved mode)\n  - [4]: Interleave flag (0=non-interleaved, non-zero=interleaved)\n  - [5]: Successive approximation bit position\n  - [7]: Current column position in MCU grid\n  - [8]: Current row position in MCU grid\n  - [0xd]: Pointer to component info sub-structure array\n- nDecoderContext: JPEG decoder context structure base address\n  - +0x4,+0x8,+0xc,+0x10: Resume state column/row positions\n  - +0x1c: Streaming interrupt flag (non-zero triggers save/resume)\n  - +0x4c: Maximum horizontal block coordinate\n  - +0x50: Maximum vertical block coordinate\n  - +0x78: Horizontal MCU count per row\n  - +0x7c: Vertical MCU count (total rows)\n  - +0x37c0: Number of components in current scan\n  - +0x37cc: Pointer to scan component info array\n  - +0x37d4,+0x37d8: Scan spectral start/end positions\n  - +0x4834: Coefficient dequantization working buffer pointer\n  - +0x4de4: DCT coefficient storage buffer pointer\n- dwPrecisionMode: DCT precision and transform mode selector\n  - 1: Full 8x8 IDCT via PerformInverseDiscreteCosineTransform8x8\n  - 2: 4x4 scaled IDCT via FUN_600129e0\n  - 4: 2x2 scaled IDCT via FUN_60012c50\n  - 8: DC-only mode with direct scaling and rounding\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Success - scan processing complete\n- 1: Partial decode - streaming interrupted, resume state saved\n- -25 (0xFFFFFFE7): Decode error from FUN_6001cc30\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x80 (128): Size of one 8x8 DCT block in bytes (64 coefficients * 2 bytes)\n- 0x40 (64): Number of coefficients per 8x8 DCT block\n- 8: Rounding bias for DC-only scaling ((val + 8) >> 4)\n- 4: Right shift count for DC scaling (divide by 16)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Non-interleaved mode (component[2]==0 or [3]==0): Process each component independently\n- Interleaved mode: Process all components together in MCU order\n- Streaming mode (context+0x1c != 0): Can pause mid-decode and resume later",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
