      "name": "ProcessMcuBlocksDecode",
      "signature": "undefined4 ProcessMcuBlocksDecode(undefined4 param_1, uint * param_2, int * param_3, int param_4, int param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Processes JPEG MCU (Minimum Coded Unit) blocks during decoding with configurable IDCT scaling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize component data arrays from scan info structure (blocks per component, quantization tables, DCT buffers)\n2. Compute MCU grid boundaries based on image dimensions and IDCT scale factor (8/nIdctScale)\n3. Calculate total DCT blocks from component sampling factors\n4. Branch based on progressive vs sequential scan mode (pScanInfo[2] and pScanInfo[3])\n5. For sequential mode: iterate over MCU rows and columns\n   a. For first spectral selection (DC): call memset to init block, decode with FUN_60014150\n   b. For subsequent AC bands: decode with FUN_60014220\n   c. Copy coefficients to temp buffer, perform scaled IDCT based on nIdctScale\n   d. Call FUN_6001cc30 for restart marker processing\n   e. Call output routines (FUN_600021b0 or FUN_600038b0) for color conversion\n6. For progressive mode: similar flow with hierarchical coefficient accumulation\n7. Update scan progress state for interleaved/restart processing\n\nParameters:\n  pBitstream    - Bitstream reader state for entropy coded data\n  pHuffmanState - Huffman decoding state and coefficient storage\n  pScanInfo     - Scan header info (component count, spectral selection, successive approximation)\n  nJpegContext  - JPEG decoder context containing image dimensions and component info\n  nIdctScale    - IDCT output scale factor (1=8x8, 2=4x4, 4=2x2, 8=1x1)\n\nReturns:\n  -25 (0xFFFFFFE7) - Error during restart marker processing (FUN_6001cc30 failed)\n  0                - Scan completed, reached end of image\n  1                - Partial decode, more MCUs remaining (for restart processing)\n  2                - Scan completed successfully with full coefficient accumulation\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Single component images force blocks-per-component to 1\n  - Progressive scans check coefficient accumulation thresholds before IDCT\n  - Restart marker handling updates x/y position and returns early\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x80   - DCT block size in bytes (64 coefficients * 2 bytes each)\n  0x40   - 64 coefficients per 8x8 DCT block\n  0x18   - Component descriptor stride (24 bytes per component)\n  0x37b8 - Offset to max H sampling factor in context\n  0x37bc - Offset to max V sampling factor in context\n  0x37c0 - Offset to number of components in context\n  0x37cc - Offset to component info array in context\n  0x37d4 - Offset to DC coefficient count in context\n  0x37d8 - Offset to AC coefficient count in context\n  0x37e0 - Offset to EOB run flag in context\n  0x4834 - Offset to temporary DCT buffer pointer in context\n  0x4de4 - Offset to coefficient storage base pointer in context",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
