      "comment": "Decodes baseline DCT scan blocks for JPEG image decompression.\n\nProcesses Minimum Coded Units (MCUs) by decoding entropy-coded DCT coefficients,\napplying inverse discrete cosine transforms (IDCT), and writing output pixels.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize component block counts from scan information header\n2. Calculate MCU grid dimensions based on component count and image size\n3. For single component, compute MCU dimensions from sample factors\n4. Loop through MCU rows (Y) and columns (X)\n5. For each MCU, decode all DCT blocks for each component via g_pfnDecodeProc19\n6. Check restart marker synchronization via FUN_6001cc30\n7. Apply IDCT transform based on output precision mode:\n   - Mode 1: Full 8x8 IDCT via g_pfnIdct8x8, then output via FUN_600021b0\n   - Mode 2: 4-bit output IDCT via FUN_600129e0\n   - Mode 4: 2-bit output IDCT via FUN_60012c50\n   - Mode 8: 1-bit output with DC-only scaling\n8. Write output samples via FUN_600038b0 for modes 2/4/8\n9. Handle restart interval state update\n\nParameters:\n  pnResult - Output result pointer (unused in baseline mode)\n  pBitstream - Pointer to bitstream context for entropy decoding\n  pScanInfo - Scan information structure containing:\n    [0x00] Component count\n    [0x1C] Current MCU X position\n    [0x20] Current MCU Y position\n    [0x24] DC predictor values array\n    [0x34] Component info table pointer\n  nDecoderContext - Decoder context structure containing:\n    [0x1C] Restart interval enable flag\n    [0x4C] Image width in pixels\n    [0x50] Image height in pixels (signed)\n    [0x78] MCU columns count\n    [0x7C] MCU rows count\n    [0x37B8] Max horizontal samples\n    [0x37BC] Max vertical samples\n    [0x4834] DCT coefficient buffer pointer\n  nOutputPrecision - Output bit depth mode (1=8-bit, 2=4-bit, 4=2-bit, 8=1-bit)\n\nReturns:\n  0 - Success, all MCUs decoded\n  1 - Partial decode, restart interval triggered\n  -21 (0xFFFFFFEB) - Decode error from entropy decoder\n  -25 (0xFFFFFFE7) - Restart marker synchronization error\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x80 - DCT block coefficient buffer stride (64 shorts * 2 bytes)\n  0x40 - DCT block pointer increment (64 coefficient entries)\n  8 - DCT block dimensions (8x8)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
