      "name": "DecodeJpegScanData",
      "signature": "int DecodeJpegScanData(undefined4 param_1, byte * param_2, int * param_3, int * param_4, int param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Decodes JPEG scan data performing MCU-based entropy decoding and IDCT transformation.\n\nThis is the core JPEG scan decoder that processes compressed scan data from a\nbitstream, decodes Huffman-coded coefficients for each component, performs\ninverse discrete cosine transform (IDCT), and writes output to destination buffers.\nSupports multiple scale factors (1:1, 1:2, 1:4, 1:8) for progressive decoding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize component block counts and DC coefficient pointers from scan info\n2. Calculate scaled MCU dimensions based on sampling factors and scale factor\n3. Determine horizontal/vertical block counts for output grid\n4. For single-component scans: calculate direct output dimensions\n5. For multi-component scans: use pre-calculated MCU grid from frame info\n6. Loop through MCU rows (Y) and columns (X):\n   a. For each component in scan, decode all blocks using g_pfnDecodeProc\n   b. Call ProcessMcuBlock to process decoded MCU data\n   c. Check restart interval boundaries if applicable\n7. For full MCU rows, perform IDCT based on scale factor:\n   - Scale 1: Full 8x8 IDCT via g_pfnIdct8x8\n   - Scale 2: 4x4 IDCT\n   - Scale 4: 2x2 IDCT  \n   - Scale 8: 1x1 DC-only scaling\n8. Copy transformed blocks to output buffer via CopyBlocksToOutput_*\n9. Update partial decode state for incremental decoding support\n\nParameters:\n  pJpegProps    - JPEG_CORE_PROPERTIES* context with decoder state, sampling factors,\n                  output buffers, and restart interval configuration at offset 0x37e0\n  pBitStream    - byte* pointer to compressed bitstream data\n  pScanInfo     - int* scan header info: [0]=component count, [0x1c]=partial row,\n                  [0x20]=partial col, [0x24+]=DC coefficient pointers per component,\n                  [0x34]=component descriptor array\n  pFrameInfo    - int* frame header with MCU grid dimensions at [0x78], [0x7c]\n  nScaleFactor  - int downscale factor: 1=full size, 2=1/2, 4=1/4, 8=1/8\n\nReturns:\n  0  - Success, scan fully decoded\n  1  - Partial decode completed (incremental decoding in progress)\n  2  - Scan complete, more data available\n  -21 (0xFFFFFFEB) - Decode error from Huffman/entropy decoder\n  -25 (0xFFFFFFE7) - MCU processing error\n\nStack Layout (local arrays):\n  Offset  Size  Name              Description\n  -0x10   16    anHSampFactors    Horizontal sampling factors per component (int[4])\n  -0x20   16    anVSampFactors    Vertical sampling factors per component (int[4])\n  -0x30   16    adBlockCounts     Block counts per component for iteration (uint[4])\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x37b8 - Horizontal sampling factor max in JPEG_CORE_PROPERTIES\n  0x37bc - Vertical sampling factor max in JPEG_CORE_PROPERTIES  \n  0x37e0 - Restart interval enabled flag\n  0x4830 - Restart marker table pointer\n  0x4834 - DCT coefficient buffer pointer\n  0x80   - DCT block size in bytes (64 coefficients * 2 bytes)\n  0x28   - Restart table entry stride (40 bytes)\n\nCalled By: DecodeJpegScanDispatch\nCalls: g_pfnDecodeProc (entropy decoder), g_pfnIdct8x8/4x4 (IDCT),\n       ProcessMcuBlock, CopyBlocksToOutput_8x8/4x4/2x2/1x1,\n       InitializeMcuRowFromRestartTable",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
