      "name": "CopyJpegComponentData",
      "signature": "undefined CopyJpegComponentData(int param_1, undefined4 * param_2, int param_3, int * param_4)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Copies JPEG component data from source structures to destination buffer slot.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate destination slot offset: nComponentIndex * 40 bytes (0x28)\n2. Copy DCT parameters from pScanParams to dest buffer offsets 0x04-0x10\n3. Copy coefficient data from pSourceComp to dest offsets 0x18-0x24\n4. Read JPEG marker type from pJpegContext[0]\n5. If progressive scan type (2,6,0xE,0x10,0x12): use pSourceComp[7]\n6. Otherwise (baseline): use pSourceComp[4] for dest offset 0x00\n\nParameters:\n  nComponentIndex - Zero-based component index (0-3 for Y,Cb,Cr,K channels)\n  pSourceComp     - Component data with coefficients and quantization info\n  pScanParams     - Scan parameters with DCT block dimensions\n  pJpegContext    - Decoder context: [0]=marker type, [0x120C]=output buffer\n\nReturns:\n  void - Data copied directly to buffer at pJpegContext[0x120C]\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  SOF2(2), SOF6(6), SOF14(0xE), SOF16(0x10), SOF18(0x12) are progressive markers",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
