      "name": "DecodeBaselineScanBlocks",
      "signature": "undefined4 DecodeBaselineScanBlocks(uint param_1, uint param_2, int * param_3)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Decodes baseline (non-progressive) JPEG scan blocks using IDCT and Huffman decoding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize component lookup tables (DC/AC Huffman tables, quantization tables)\n2. Calculate total block count per MCU from scan header component data\n3. Iterate over MCU rows (dwMcuRow) from pScanHeader[8] to context max rows\n4. Iterate over MCU columns (dwMcuColumn) from pScanHeader[7] to context max cols\n5. Call FUN_60004ff0 to prepare coefficient blocks for current MCU position\n6. Apply 4x4 IDCT transform (g_pfnIdct4x4) to each block in the MCU\n7. For each color component, apply dequantization (g_pfnDecodeProc21) and \n   output conversion (g_pfnDecodeProc18) to decoded coefficients\n8. If restart interval hit (context+0x1c != 0), save position and return 1\n9. After all MCUs processed, call finalization proc and return 0\n\nParameters:\n  pJpegContext - Pointer to JPEG decoder context structure (passed as uint)\n  pScanState   - Pointer to current scan state/buffer structure (passed as uint)\n  pScanHeader  - Pointer to scan header with component info and MCU positions\n\nReturns:\n  0 - Scan completed successfully (all MCUs decoded)\n  1 - Restart interval reached, caller should resume later\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x379c - Offset to sampling factor table in context\n  0x37e0 - Offset to progressive mode flag in context\n  0x36e4 - Offset to DC Huffman table pointer array\n  0x36f4 - Offset to quantization table pointer array\n  0x3704 - Offset to AC Huffman table pointer array\n  0x37cc - Offset to component index lookup table\n  0x4834 - Offset to coefficient block buffer pointer\n  0x78   - Offset to MCU columns count\n  0x7c   - Offset to MCU rows count\n  0x80   - Size of one DCT coefficient block (128 bytes = 64 shorts)\n\nStructure Layout (pScanHeader offsets):\n  +0x00 - Component count in scan\n  +0x1C - Current MCU column position\n  +0x20 - Current MCU row position\n  +0x24 - Output position array (per component)\n  +0x34 - Component descriptor array pointer (stride 0x18)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:895ec59129fc01ee9fc84ff8877ab1a395db3c4ec39c58b0c013396d8060ecf7",
