      "name": "DecodeProgressiveScanBlocks",
      "signature": "int DecodeProgressiveScanBlocks(uint param_1, uint param_2, int * param_3)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Decodes JPEG progressive scan blocks for interleaved image data.\nProcesses MCU rows and columns iteratively, applying IDCT and dequantization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize component block count arrays from scan parameters\n2. Validate MCU row/column bounds against image dimensions\n3. Call FUN_60004ff0 to set up decode parameters for current MCU\n4. Apply IDCT 4x4 transform via g_pfnIdct4x4 for each block\n5. Dequantize and decode blocks via g_pfnDecodeProc21/g_pfnDecodeProc18\n6. Increment frame counter and check for restart marker interval\n7. Process restart markers via FUN_6001be30 when interval reached\n8. Reset component counters after restart marker\n9. Update scan state position for next MCU row/column\n10. Return 0 on completion, 1 on suspension, or error code\n\nParameters:\npJpegContext (void*): Pointer to JPEG decoder context structure\n  - Offset 0x78: Image height in MCU rows\n  - Offset 0x7C: Image width in MCU columns\n  - Offset 0x37D0: Restart marker interval\n  - Offset 0x37E0: Interleave mode flag\n  - Offset 0x4834: Pointer to DCT coefficient buffer\npScanState (void*): Pointer to scan state tracking structure\n  - Offset 0x24+: Per-component block counters array\n  - Offset 0x34: Pointer to component descriptor array\npComponentInfo (int*): Component information array\n  - Offset 0x00: Number of components in scan\n  - Offset 0x18: Current frame counter\n  - Offset 0x1C: Current MCU column position\n  - Offset 0x20: Current MCU row position\n\nReturns:\n0: Scan completed successfully\n1: Scan suspended (restart marker processing in progress)\nNegative: Error code from restart marker handler (FUN_6001be30)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handles restart marker intervals (RST0-RST7 markers: 0xD0-0xD7)\n- Supports multiple components per scan (up to component count)\n- Resets all component block counters after 8 restart intervals\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x379C: Component scan parameter table offset in context\n0x36E4, 0x36F4, 0x3704: Quantization table offsets\n0x80: DCT block stride in bytes (8x8 block * 2 bytes per coefficient)\n0x18: Component descriptor stride (24 bytes per component)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:e0275c92c3e9d55abedfe13770f94890abb1c8cca007e13894f6ef03cbf3ced6",
