      "name": "ScaleQuantizationTable",
      "signature": "undefined ScaleQuantizationTable(int param_1, int param_2, undefined2 * param_3)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Scales a JPEG quantization table based on quality factor.\n\nConverts a standard 64-element quantization table (8x8 DCT block) to scaled 16-bit values\nbased on the IJG libjpeg quality scaling algorithm.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute scale factor based on quality:\n   - quality < 1: scale = 5000 (minimum quality, max quantization)\n   - quality 1-49: scale = 5000 / quality (inverse scaling)\n   - quality 50-100: scale = 2 * (100 - quality) (linear scaling)\n   - quality > 100: clamped to 100 (zero quantization)\n2. For each of 64 table elements:\n   a. Compute: scaledValue = (sourceValue * scaleFactor + 50) / 100\n   b. Clamp result to range [1, 255]\n   c. Store as 16-bit value in destination\n\nParameters:\n  nQuality - JPEG quality factor (1-100 typical, higher = better quality)\n  pbSourceTable - Pointer to 64-byte source quantization table\n  pwDestTable - Pointer to 64-element ushort destination array\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  5000 - Maximum scale factor for lowest quality\n  0x32 (50) - Rounding offset for division by 100\n  0x40 (64) - DCT block size (8x8)\n  0xff (255) - Maximum quantization value\n  0x64 (100) - Division constant and quality threshold\n\nCalled By:\n  InitializeQuantizationAndHuffmanTables - During JPEG encoder initialization",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
