      "name": "BuildHuffmanTable",
      "signature": "undefined BuildHuffmanTable(int param_1, int param_2, int param_3)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Builds a Huffman decoding table from bit counts and symbol values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize the Huffman table arrays to zero (256 entries each)\n2. For each bit length 1-16, read count from pbBitCounts and fill anBitLengthPerSymbol array\n3. Generate canonical Huffman codes - same bit length symbols get sequential codes\n4. Populate output table with code values and bit lengths indexed by symbol\n\nParameters:\n  pbBitCounts - Pointer to 16-byte array of symbol counts per bit length (1-16 bits)\n  pbSymbolValues - Pointer to symbol value array (indices 0 to nTotalSymbols-1)\n  pnHuffmanTable - Pointer to output Huffman table structure:\n                   +0x008: int[256] - Bit lengths indexed by symbol\n                   +0x408: short[256] - Code values indexed by symbol\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset   Size   Field              Description\n  0x008    1024   nBitLengths[256]   Bit length for each symbol (4 bytes each)\n  0x408    512    wCodes[256]        Huffman code for each symbol (2 bytes each)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x100 (256) - Maximum number of symbols in table\n  0x11 (17) - Loop bound for bit lengths 1-16\n  0x408 - Offset to code values array in output table\n  0x808 - Stack allocation for two 257-entry int arrays",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
