      "name": "ConvertYCbCrBlockToRgbWithClipping",
      "signature": "void ConvertYCbCrBlockToRgbWithClipping(short * pnYCbCrPlanes, byte * pbRgbOutput, Rect * pClipRect, int nOutputStride)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts an 8x8 YCbCr color block to RGB format with optional clipping support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Define full block rectangle as (0,0,8,8) representing complete 8x8 MCU\n2. Compare clip rectangle against full block bounds\n3. If clip rect equals full block, use fast path ConvertYCbCrBlockToRgb\n4. Otherwise, calculate intersection of clip rect with decode block params\n5. Copy intersection result to local rect variables\n6. If intersection is valid (non-empty), convert partial block via ConvertYCbCrPartialBlockToRgb888\n\nParameters:\n  pnYCbCrPlanes - Pointer to interleaved YCbCr plane data (Y at +0x00, Cb at +0x80, Cr at +0x100)\n  pbRgbOutput - Destination buffer for RGB pixel output\n  pClipRect - Clipping rectangle defining valid output region\n  nOutputStride - Bytes per row in output buffer\n\nReturns:\n  void - RGB data written directly to pbRgbOutput\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Full 8x8 block (no clipping): Uses optimized ConvertYCbCrBlockToRgb path\n  - Partial block: Uses ConvertYCbCrPartialBlockToRgb888 with intersection bounds\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x40 (64) - Offset to Cb plane (64 shorts = 128 bytes)\n  0x80 (128) - Offset to Cr plane (128 shorts = 256 bytes)\n  8 - MCU block dimension (8x8 pixels)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
