      "name": "ConvertRgbMcuToYCbCr420",
      "signature": "void ConvertRgbMcuToYCbCr420(byte * pbRgbInput, short * psMcuOutput, int nWidth, int nHeight, int nRgbStride)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts RGB image data to YCbCr 4:2:0 format for JPEG MCU encoding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if block dimensions are exactly 16x16 pixels\n2. If 16x16: Use optimized 4:2:0 path - process four 8x8 Y blocks plus shared CbCr\n   a. Top-left Y block: psMcuOutput[0x000], Cb at +0x100, Cr at +0x140\n   b. Top-right Y block: psMcuOutput[0x040], Cb at +0x104, Cr at +0x144\n   c. Bottom-left Y block: psMcuOutput[0x080], Cb at +0x120, Cr at +0x160\n   d. Bottom-right Y block: psMcuOutput[0x0C0], Cb at +0x124, Cr at +0x164\n3. If not 16x16: Use generic path with edge replication and arbitrary dimensions\n\nParameters:\n  pbRgbInput  - Source RGB pixel data (BGR byte order, 3 bytes per pixel)\n  psMcuOutput - Destination buffer for YCbCr MCU (384 shorts: 4x64 Y + 64 Cb + 64 Cr)\n  nWidth      - Source image width in pixels (1-16)\n  nHeight     - Source image height in pixels (1-16)\n  nRgbStride  - Bytes between consecutive rows in source buffer\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nMCU Buffer Layout (16x16 block, 4:2:0):\n  Offset  Size    Component   Description\n  0x000   0x100   Y0-Y3       Four 8x8 luma blocks (256 shorts total)\n  0x100   0x040   Cb          8x8 chroma-blue block (64 shorts)\n  0x140   0x040   Cr          8x8 chroma-red block (64 shorts)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Dimensions != 16x16: Falls back to ConvertRgbBlockToYCbCr with edge padding\n  - Referenced from Scalar, SSE, and SSE2 decode function tables",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
