      "name": "PerformInverseDiscreteCosineTransform4x4",
      "signature": "void PerformInverseDiscreteCosineTransform4x4(short * pDctBlock)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Performs a 4x4 Inverse Discrete Cosine Transform (IDCT) for JPEG decoding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Apply 1D column IDCT to 4 columns of the 4x4 DCT coefficient block\n2. Apply 1D row IDCT to 4 rows with level shift and clamping\n3. Each 1D transform uses butterfly stages with fixed-point cosine multipliers\n4. Output values are scaled, DC-shifted by +128, and clamped to [0,255]\n\nParameters:\n  pDctBlock - Pointer to 16-element short array (4x4 DCT coefficients)\n              Modified in-place: input coefficients replaced with pixel values\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nNotes:\n  - This function is a smaller block variant of PerformInverseDiscreteCosineTransform8x8\n  - Used in JPEG progressive mode or for chroma subsampling\n  - Stored in function pointer table at g_pfnPerformIdct4x4 (0x600288ec)\n  - Called indirectly through JPEG decoder dispatch table\n\nMagic Number Reference:\n  0x14e7b (85627) - cos(pi/16) * sqrt(2) * 32768, 1D stage rotation\n  0xb505  (46341) - sqrt(2) * 32768, even-odd butterfly rotation\n  0x8a8c  (35468) - cos(3*pi/16) * sqrt(2) * 32768, odd stage scaling\n  0x61f8  (25080) - (cos(pi/16) - cos(3*pi/16)) * sqrt(2) * 32768\n  0x4000  (16384) - Rounding constant for 15-bit right shift\n  0x80    (128)   - DC level shift for unsigned pixel output\n  0xff    (255)   - Maximum clamped pixel value\n\nStructure Layout (4x4 block addressing):\n  Offset    Size    Field           Description\n  0x00      8       Row 0           First row of 4 short coefficients\n  0x08      8       Row 1           Second row\n  0x10      8       Row 2           Third row\n  0x18      8       Row 3           Last row\n\nINCOMPLETE: Function body not disassembled (0x600122e3-0x600129d3).\nIn Ghidra, select address range and press 'D' to disassemble bytes.",
