      "name": "CopyMemoryBlock",
      "signature": "void * CopyMemoryBlock(void * pDest, void * pSrc, uint dwSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Copies a block of memory from source to destination using optimized DWORD-aligned transfers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load size parameter into ECX, save original value\n2. Push ESI/EDI to preserve caller registers\n3. Load source pointer into ESI, destination into EDI\n4. Calculate DWORD count (size >> 2) and copy with REP MOVSD\n5. Calculate remaining byte count (size & 3) and copy with REP MOVSB\n6. Restore ESI/EDI and return destination pointer\n\nParameters:\n- pDest: Destination buffer pointer (void*)\n- pSrc: Source buffer pointer (void*)\n- dwSize: Number of bytes to copy (uint)\n\nReturns:\n- void*: Returns pDest (destination pointer) in EAX\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Zero-size copy: No bytes copied, returns pDest\n- Unaligned size: Handles remainder bytes after DWORD copies\n- Overlapping buffers: NOT SAFE - use memmove for overlapping regions\n\nNote: This is a function pointer callback stored at g_pMemcpyHandler (0x600288e0)\nby the initialization function at 0x60018200.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
