      "name": "GetTimestampCounter",
      "signature": "ulonglong GetTimestampCounter(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "ulonglong",
      "comment": "Reads the CPU time-stamp counter using the RDTSC instruction.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Execute RDTSC instruction to read the 64-bit timestamp counter\n2. Return the timestamp value (EDX:EAX combined into 64-bit result)\n\nParameters:\n- None (void function)\n\nReturns:\n- ulonglong: Current value of the CPU's time-stamp counter (TSC)\n  The TSC increments at a constant rate since processor reset\n\nNotes:\n- Used as a function pointer via global timestamp function pointer\n- Falls back to fallback implementation (returns 0) if RDTSC unsupported\n- RDTSC support checked via CPUID feature flag (bit 4 of EDX)\n- Single instruction function - no stack frame needed",
