      "name": "ResetMmxState",
      "signature": "void ResetMmxState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Resets MMX state by executing the EMMS instruction to restore x87 FPU mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Execute EMMS instruction to empty MMX technology state\n2. Return immediately (single-instruction function)\n\nParameters:\n    None.\n\nReturns:\n    None. Side effect only - clears MMX register state.\n\nPurpose:\nThis function is registered as g_pfnDecodeProc22 in both MMX and MMX2 decode \nfunction pointer tables. It must be called after any MMX operations before \nusing x87 FPU instructions to prevent undefined behavior from mixed MMX/FPU state.\n\nThe EMMS instruction:\n- Marks all x87 FPU tag words as empty\n- Clears the MMX state, allowing subsequent x87 floating-point operations\n- Required by Intel architecture after MMX usage before FPU usage\n\nCalled By:\n- Video decode pipeline completion routines via g_pfnDecodeProc22 function pointer\n- Referenced by InitializeMmxDecodeFunctionTable (0x600184b0)\n- Referenced by InitializeMmx2DecodeFunctionTable (0x600186c0)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
