      "name": "ShowAssertionFailureDialog",
      "signature": "bool ShowAssertionFailureDialog(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Displays an assertion failure dialog box with module path and error details.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get the current module's full file path using GetModuleFileNameA\n2. Find the last backslash to extract the module filename\n3. Format the assertion failure message with file/line information\n4. Display message box via ShowMessageBoxPreserveQuit function pointer\n5. If user clicks \"Abort\" (result 3), call ReportError to terminate\n6. Return true if user clicks \"Retry\" (result 4), false otherwise\n\nParameters:\n  None - Uses assertion context from format string parameters passed elsewhere\n\nReturns:\n  bool - true if user selected \"Retry\" (value 4), false otherwise\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x5c (92)     - ASCII backslash character '\\\\'\n  0x104 (260)   - MAX_PATH constant for Windows paths\n  0x12112       - Message box style flags (MB_ABORTRETRYIGNORE | MB_ICONHAND | MB_TASKMODAL)\n  3             - IDABORT - User clicked Abort button\n  4             - IDRETRY - User clicked Retry button\n\nError Handling:\n  If user clicks Abort, calls ReportError(3) to terminate the process",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
