      "name": "CompareStringsOptimized",
      "signature": "int CompareStringsOptimized(char * lpszStr1, char * lpszStr2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Compares two null-terminated strings for equality using optimized DWORD-aligned comparison.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load string pointers from stack into EDX (lpszStr1) and ECX (lpszStr2)\n2. Test first pointer for DWORD alignment (TEST EDX, 3)\n3. If aligned, compare 4 bytes at a time for performance\n4. Compare individual bytes when misaligned or near string end\n5. Return 0 if strings equal, non-zero if different\n\nParameters:\nlpszStr1 (char *): First null-terminated string to compare\nlpszStr2 (char *): Second null-terminated string to compare\n\nReturns:\n0: Strings are identical\nNon-zero: Strings differ (sign indicates lexicographic ordering)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty strings: Compared correctly, two empty strings return 0\n- Alignment optimization: Uses DWORD comparison when pointer is 4-byte aligned\n- Early exit: Returns immediately when difference found\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x03: Alignment mask for testing DWORD boundary (addr & 3 == 0 means aligned)\n0x3C: Jump offset for unaligned path handling\n\nNote: Function body appears truncated in Ghidra analysis. This is a CRT strcmp implementation\nusing alignment-optimized comparison for performance.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:f9ee21d61135771f8bfaeca9f2ff173a05938d7bdae0448b2c706393a8367f30",
