      "comment": "Performs unsigned 64-bit multiplication of two 32-bit value pairs.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if high dwords of both operands are zero (simple 32x32 case)\n2. If both high dwords zero: perform single MUL and return 64-bit result in EDX:EAX\n3. Otherwise: perform full 64x64 multiplication using partial products\n   a. Multiply low dwords: dwMultiplicandLo * dwMultiplierLo\n   b. Multiply dwMultiplicandLo * dwMultiplierHi, add to high result\n   c. Multiply dwMultiplicandHi * dwMultiplierLo, add to high result\n4. Return 64-bit result in EDX:EAX\n\nParameters:\n  dwMultiplicandLo (uint, ESP+0x4): Low 32 bits of first 64-bit operand\n  dwMultiplicandHi (uint, ESP+0x8): High 32 bits of first 64-bit operand\n  dwMultiplierLo (uint, ESP+0xC): Low 32 bits of second 64-bit operand\n  dwMultiplierHi (uint, ESP+0x10): High 32 bits of second 64-bit operand\n\nReturns:\n  ulonglong in EDX:EAX - 64-bit product of the two operands\n  Note: Only lower 64 bits returned; overflow is discarded\n\nCalling Convention: __stdcall (callee cleans 16 bytes)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Fast path when both high dwords are zero (32x32 multiplication)\n  - Implements Microsoft _allmul compiler intrinsic for 64-bit multiply",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
