      "name": "CloseAndDeallocateExtraStreams",
      "signature": "int CloseAndDeallocateExtraStreams(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Closes and deallocates extra file stream structures beyond the reserved slots.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire critical section 2 (stream table lock)\n2. Iterate through stream structures starting from index 3 (skip reserved 0-2)\n3. For each non-null stream with active flags (0x83 = read/write/error):\n   a. Call ThreadSafeFileClose to close the file\n   b. If close succeeds (not -1), increment closed count\n4. For indices >= 20 (0x14), cleanup dynamically allocated streams:\n   a. Delete the embedded critical section at offset 0x20\n   b. Deallocate the stream structure memory\n   c. Clear the table entry to NULL\n5. Release critical section 2\n6. Return count of successfully closed files\n\nParameters:\n  None (void)\n\nReturns:\n  int - Number of files successfully closed\n\nFlag Bits (0x83 mask):\n  0x01 - _IOREAD  (file open for reading)\n  0x02 - _IOWRT   (file open for writing)\n  0x80 - _IOERR   (error occurred)\n\nStream Table Layout:\n  Indices 0-2:   Reserved/system streams (stdin, stdout, stderr)\n  Indices 3-19:  Standard stream slots (close only, no dealloc)\n  Indices 20+:   Dynamically allocated streams (close + dealloc)\n\nStructure Layout (stream at g_pStreamStructureTable[n]):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Description\n  0x00    0x20  FILE            Standard C FILE structure\n  0x20    0x18  CRITICAL_SECTION Embedded lock for thread safety",
